\s1 Laws for Burnt Offerings
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb called to|וַיִּקְרָ֖א\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb and spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to him|אֶל־\rb* \rb from the Tent|מֵאֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֖ד\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Speak|דַּבֵּ֞ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb*: \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb any|אָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb of|מִכֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb you brings|יַקְרִ֥יב\rb* \rb an offering|קָרְבָּ֖ן\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb you may bring|תַּקְרִ֖יבוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as your offering|קָרְבַּנְכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb an|מִן־\rb* \rb animal|הַבְּהֵמָ֗ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the herd|הַבָּקָר֙\rb*\rb |וּמִן־\rb* \rb or the flock|הַצֹּ֔אן\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb his offering|קָרְבָּנוֹ֙\rb* \rb is a burnt offering|עֹלָ֤ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the herd|הַבָּקָ֔ר\rb*, \rb he is to present|יַקְרִיבֶ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb an unblemished|תָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb male|זָכָ֥ר\rb*. \rb He must bring|יַקְרִ֣יב\rb* \rb it|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֝תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֤הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵד֙\rb* \rb for its acceptance|לִרְצֹנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb He is to lay|וְסָמַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֑ה\rb*, \rb so it can be accepted|וְנִרְצָ֥ה\rb* \rb on his behalf|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb to make atonement|לְכַפֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb for him|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb And he shall slaughter|וְשָׁחַ֛ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the young|בֶּ֥ן\rb* \rb bull|הַבָּקָ֖ר\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֤ן\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb the priests|הַֽכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb are to present|וְ֠הִקְרִיבוּ\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֔ם\rb* \rb and splatter|וְזָרְק֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it|הַדָּ֤ם\rb* \rb on all sides|סָבִ֔יב\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb Next, he is to skin|וְהִפְשִׁ֖יט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb and cut|וְנִתַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb it into pieces|לִנְתָחֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֧ן\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb shall put|וְ֠נָתְנוּ\rb* \rb a fire|אֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb and arrange|וְעָרְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb wood|עֵצִ֖ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the fire|הָאֵֽשׁ׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Then Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb are to arrange|וְעָרְכ֗וּ\rb* \rb the pieces|הַנְּתָחִ֔ים\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb including the head|הָרֹ֖אשׁ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the fat|הַפָּ֑דֶר\rb*, \rb atop|עַל־\rb* \rb the burning|הָאֵ֔שׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb wood|הָעֵצִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb The entrails|וְקִרְבּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb and legs|וּכְרָעָ֖יו\rb* \rb must be washed|יִרְחַ֣ץ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמָּ֑יִם\rb*, \rb and the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall burn|וְהִקְטִ֨יר\rb* \rb all of it|הַכֹּל֙\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חָה\rb* \rb as a burnt offering|עֹלָ֛ה\rb*, \rb a food offering|אִשֵּׁ֥ה\rb*, \rb a pleasing|נִיח֖וֹחַ\rb* \rb aroma|רֵֽיחַ־\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb If, however|וְאִם־\rb*, \rb one’s offering|קָרְבָּנ֧וֹ\rb* \rb is a burnt offering|לְעֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֨אן\rb* — \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the sheep|הַכְּשָׂבִ֛ים\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb goats|הָעִזִּ֖ים\rb* — \rb he is to present|יַקְרִיבֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb an unblemished|תָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb male|זָכָ֥ר\rb*. \v 11 \rb He shall slaughter|וְשָׁחַ֨ט\rb*\rb |אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb it on|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb the north|צָפֹ֖נָה\rb* \rb side|יֶ֧רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֛חַ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֨ן\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵי֩\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֧ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb are to splatter|וְזָרְק֡וּ\rb* \rb its blood|דָּמ֛וֹ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb on all sides|סָבִֽיב׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb He is to cut|וְנִתַּ֤ח\rb* \rb the animal|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb into pieces|לִנְתָחָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb shall arrange|וְעָרַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb including|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the head|רֹאשׁ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and fat|פִּדְר֑וֹ\rb*, \rb atop|עַל־\rb* \rb the burning|הָאֵ֔שׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb wood|הָֽעֵצִים֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb is on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb The entrails|וְהַקֶּ֥רֶב\rb* \rb and legs|וְהַכְּרָעַ֖יִם\rb* \rb must be washed|יִרְחַ֣ץ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמָּ֑יִם\rb*, \rb and the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall present|וְהִקְרִ֨יב\rb* \rb all of it|הַכֹּל֙\rb* \rb and burn it|וְהִקְטִ֣יר\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חָה\rb*; \rb it|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb is a burnt offering|עֹלָ֣ה\rb*, \rb a food offering|אִשֵּׁ֛ה\rb*, \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb aroma|רֵ֥יחַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb If, instead|וְאִ֧ם\rb*, \rb one’s offering|קָרְבָּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb is a burnt offering|עֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb birds|הָע֛וֹף\rb*, \rb he is to present|וְהִקְרִ֣יב\rb*\rb |קָרְבָּנֽוֹ׃\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb a turtledove|הַתֹּרִ֗ים\rb* \rb or|א֛וֹ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb a young|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb pigeon|הַיּוֹנָ֖ה\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 15 \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb shall bring|וְהִקְרִיב֤וֹ\rb* \rb it to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb*, \rb twist off|וּמָלַק֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its head|רֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and burn|וְהִקְטִ֖יר\rb* \rb it on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חָה\rb*; \rb its blood|דָמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb should be drained out|וְנִמְצָ֣ה\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the side|קִ֥יר\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb And he is to remove|וְהֵסִ֥יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the crop|מֻרְאָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb with its contents|בְּנֹצָתָ֑הּ\rb*\f + \fr 1:16 \ft Or \fqa the crop and feathers\f* \rb and throw|וְהִשְׁלִ֨יךְ\rb* \rb it|אֹתָ֜הּ\rb* \rb to the east|קֵ֔דְמָה\rb* \rb side|אֵ֤צֶל\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb*, \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|מְק֖וֹם\rb* \rb for ashes|הַדָּֽשֶׁן׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb He shall tear it open|וְשִׁסַּ֨ע\rb*\rb |אֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb by its wings|בִכְנָפָיו֮\rb*, \rb without|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb dividing the bird completely|יַבְדִּיל֒\rb*. \rb And the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb is to burn|וְהִקְטִ֨יר\rb* \rb it|אֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חָה\rb* \rb atop|עַל־\rb* \rb the burning|הָאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb wood|הָעֵצִ֖ים\rb*.\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb It|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb is a burnt offering|עֹלָ֣ה\rb*, \rb a food offering|אִשֵּׁ֛ה\rb*, \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb aroma|רֵ֥יחַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.[’’]
\c 2
\s1 Laws for Grain Offerings
\p \v 1 “\rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb anyone|וְנֶ֗פֶשׁ\rb* \rb brings|תַקְרִ֞יב\rb* \rb a grain offering|קָרְבַּ֤ן\rb*\rb |מִנְחָה֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb his offering|קָרְבָּנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb must consist of fine flour|סֹ֖לֶת\rb*.\rb |יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb He is to pour|וְיָצַ֤ק\rb* \rb olive oil|שֶׁ֔מֶן\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*, \rb put|וְנָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb frankincense|לְבֹנָֽה׃\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb*, \v 2 \rb and bring|וֶֽהֱבִיאָ֗הּ\rb* \rb it to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹן֮\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִים֒\rb*. \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall take a handful|וְקָמַ֨ץ\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁ֜ם\rb*\rb |מְלֹ֣א\rb*\rb |קֻמְצ֗וֹ\rb* \rb of the flour|מִסָּלְתָּהּ֙\rb* \rb and oil|וּמִשַּׁמְנָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb together with|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the frankincense|לְבֹנָתָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb and burn this|וְהִקְטִ֨יר\rb* \rb as a memorial portion|אַזְכָּרָתָהּ֙\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חָה\rb*, \rb a food offering|אִשֵּׁ֛ה\rb*, \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb aroma|רֵ֥יחַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb The remainder|וְהַנּוֹתֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the grain offering|הַמִּנְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb shall belong to Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּלְבָנָ֑יו\rb*; \rb it is a most|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb holy part|קָֽדָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb of the food offerings|מֵאִשֵּׁ֥י\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Now if|וְכִ֥י\rb* \rb you bring|תַקְרִ֛ב\rb* \rb an offering of grain|קָרְבַּ֥ן\rb*\rb |מִנְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb baked|מַאֲפֵ֣ה\rb* \rb in an oven|תַנּ֑וּר\rb*, \rb it must consist of fine flour|סֹ֣לֶת\rb*, \rb either unleavened|מַצֹּת֙\rb* \rb cakes|חַלּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb mixed|בְּלוּלֹ֣ת\rb* \rb with oil|בַּשֶּׁ֔מֶן\rb* \rb or unleavened|מַצּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb wafers|וּרְקִיקֵ֥י\rb* \rb coated|מְשֻׁחִ֥ים\rb* \rb with oil|בַּשָּֽׁמֶן׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb your offering|קָרְבָּנֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb is a grain offering|מִנְחָ֥ה\rb* \rb prepared on|עַל־\rb* \rb a griddle|הַֽמַּחֲבַ֖ת\rb*,\f + \fr 2:5 \ft That is, a shallow pan for baking or frying\f* \rb it must be|תִהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb unleavened bread|מַצָּ֥ה\rb* \rb made of fine flour|סֹ֛לֶת\rb* \rb mixed|בְּלוּלָ֥ה\rb* \rb with oil|בַשֶּׁ֖מֶן\rb*. \v 6 \rb Crumble it|פָּת֤וֹת\rb*\rb |אֹתָהּ֙\rb*\rb |פִּתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and pour|וְיָצַקְתָּ֥\rb* \rb oil|שָׁ֑מֶן\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb*; \rb it|הִֽוא׃ס\rb* \rb is a grain offering|מִנְחָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb your offering|קָרְבָּנֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb is a grain offering|מִנְחַ֥ת\rb* \rb cooked in a pan|מַרְחֶ֖שֶׁת\rb*,\f + \fr 2:7 \ft That is, a deep pan or stew pan\f* \rb it must consist|תֵּעָשֶֽׂה׃\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֥לֶת\rb* \rb with oil|בַּשֶּׁ֖מֶן\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb When you bring|וְהֵבֵאתָ֣\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb the grain offering|הַמִּנְחָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb made|יֵעָשֶׂ֛ה\rb* \rb in any of these ways|מֵאֵ֖לֶּה\rb*, \rb it is to be presented|וְהִקְרִיבָהּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb and he shall take|וְהִגִּישָׁ֖הּ\rb* \rb it to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֤ן\rb* \rb is to remove|וְהֵרִ֨ים\rb* \rb the memorial portion|אַזְכָּ֣רָתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the grain offering|הַמִּנְחָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and burn|וְהִקְטִ֖יר\rb* \rb it on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חָה\rb* \rb as a food offering|אִשֵּׁ֛ה\rb*, \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb aroma|רֵ֥יחַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb But the remainder|וְהַנּוֹתֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the grain offering|הַמִּנְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb shall belong to Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּלְבָנָ֑יו\rb*; \rb it is a most|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb holy|קָֽדָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb part of the food offerings|מֵאִשֵּׁ֥י\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb No|כָּל־\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb grain offering|הַמִּנְחָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you present|תַּקְרִ֙יבוּ֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb may be made|תֵעָשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb with leaven|חָמֵ֑ץ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you are not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to burn|תַקְטִ֧ירוּ\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֛נּוּ\rb* \rb any|כָל־\rb* \rb leaven|שְׂאֹר֙\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb or honey|דְּבַ֔שׁ\rb* \rb as a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb You may bring|תַּקְרִ֥יבוּ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb as an offering|קָרְבַּ֥ן\rb* \rb of firstfruits|רֵאשִׁ֛ית\rb*, \rb but they must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb go up|יַעֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb on|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֥חַ\rb* \rb as a pleasing|נִיחֹֽחַ׃\rb* \rb aroma|לְרֵ֥יחַ\rb*. \v 13 \rb And you shall season|תִּמְלָח֒\rb* \rb each|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of your grain offerings|קָרְבַּ֣ן\rb*\rb |מִנְחָתְךָ֮\rb* \rb with salt|בַּמֶּ֣לַח\rb*. \rb You must not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb leave|תַשְׁבִּ֗ית\rb* \rb the salt|מֶ֚לַח\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb out of|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb your grain offering|מִנְחָתֶ֑ךָ\rb*; \rb you are to add|תַּקְרִ֥יב\rb* \rb salt|מֶֽלַח׃ס\rb* \rb to|עַ֥ל\rb* \rb each|כָּל־\rb* \rb of your offerings|קָרְבָּנְךָ֖\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you bring|תַּקְרִ֛יב\rb* \rb a grain offering|מִנְחַ֥ת\rb* \rb of firstfruits|בִּכּוּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb you shall offer|תַּקְרִ֕יב\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb crushed|גֶּ֣רֶשׂ\rb* \rb heads of new grain|אָבִ֞יב\rb*\rb |כַּרְמֶ֔ל\rb* \rb roasted|קָל֤וּי\rb* \rb on the fire|בָּאֵשׁ֙\rb*\rb |מִנְחַ֥ת\rb*\rb |בִּכּוּרֶֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb And you are to put|וְנָתַתָּ֤\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֔מֶן\rb*\rb |וְשַׂמְתָּ֥\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb and frankincense|לְבֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*; \rb it|הִֽוא׃\rb* \rb is a grain offering|מִנְחָ֖ה\rb*. \v 16 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall then burn|וְהִקְטִ֨יר\rb* \rb the memorial portion|אַזְכָּרָתָ֗הּ\rb* \rb of the crushed grain|מִגִּרְשָׂהּ֙\rb* \rb and the oil|וּמִשַּׁמְנָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb together with|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its frankincense|לְבֹנָתָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb as a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.[’’]
\c 3
\s1 Laws for Peace Offerings
\p \v 1 “\rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb one’s offering|קָרְבָּנ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |זֶ֥בַח\rb* \rb is a peace offering|שְׁלָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and he|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb offers|מַקְרִ֔יב\rb* \rb an animal from|מִן־\rb* \rb the herd|הַבָּקָר֙\rb*, \rb whether|אִ֤ם\rb* \rb male|זָכָר֙\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb female|נְקֵבָ֔ה\rb*, \rb he must present|יַקְרִיבֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb it without blemish|תָּמִ֥ים\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb He is to lay|וְסָמַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb his hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the offering|קָרְבָּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and slaughter|וּשְׁחָט֕וֹ\rb* \rb it at the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb*. \rb Then Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֨ן\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵי֩\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֧ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall splatter|וְזָרְק֡וּ\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֛ם\rb* \rb on all sides|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb |מִזֶּ֣בַח\rb* \rb From the peace offering|הַשְּׁלָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb he is to bring|וְהִקְרִיב֙\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*:\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵ֙לֶב֙\rb* \rb that covers|הַֽמְכַסֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the entrails|הַקֶּ֔רֶב\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵ֔לֶב\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb is on|עַל־\rb* \rb them|הַקֶּֽרֶב׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb both|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb kidneys|הַכְּלָיֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with the fat|הַחֵ֙לֶב֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵהֶ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb* \rb the loins|הַכְּסָלִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the lobe|הַיֹּתֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the liver|הַכָּבֵ֔ד\rb*, \rb which he is to remove|יְסִירֶֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the kidneys|הַכְּלָי֖וֹת\rb*. \v 5 \rb Then Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb are to burn|וְהִקְטִ֨ירוּ\rb* \rb it|אֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חָה\rb* \rb atop|עַל־\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָ֣עֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is on|עַל־\rb* \rb the burning|הָאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb wood|הָעֵצִ֖ים\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb as a food offering|אִשֵּׁ֛ה\rb*, \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb aroma|רֵ֥יחַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb If, however|וְאִם־\rb*,\rb |קָרְבָּנ֛וֹ\rb* \rb one’s peace offering|שְׁלָמִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לְזֶ֥בַח\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb is from|מִן־\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֧אן\rb*, \rb he must present|יַקְרִיבֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb a male|זָכָר֙\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb female|נְקֵבָ֔ה\rb* \rb without blemish|תָּמִ֖ים\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb is presenting|מַקְרִ֖יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a lamb|כֶּ֥שֶׂב\rb* \rb for his offering|קָרְבָּנ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb he must present|וְהִקְרִ֥יב\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb it before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb He is to lay|וְסָמַ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of his offering|קָרְבָּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and slaughter|וְשָׁחַ֣ט\rb* \rb it|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb in front of|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb*. \rb Then Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֧ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb shall splatter|וְ֠זָרְקוּ\rb* \rb its blood|דָּמ֛וֹ\rb* \rb on all sides|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb |מִזֶּ֣בַח\rb* \rb And from the peace offering|הַשְּׁלָמִים֮\rb* \rb he shall bring|וְהִקְרִ֨יב\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָה֒\rb* \rb consisting of its fat|חֶלְבּוֹ֙\rb*: \rb the entire|תְמִימָ֔ה\rb* \rb fat tail|הָאַלְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb cut off|יְסִירֶ֑נָּה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb close to|לְעֻמַּ֥ת\rb* \rb the backbone|הֶעָצֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb the fat|הַחֵ֙לֶב֙\rb* \rb that covers|הַֽמְכַסֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the entrails|הַקֶּ֔רֶב\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵ֔לֶב\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb them|הַקֶּֽרֶב׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb both|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb kidneys|הַכְּלָיֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with the fat|הַחֵ֙לֶב֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵהֶ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb* \rb the loins|הַכְּסָלִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the lobe|הַיֹּתֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the liver|הַכָּבֵ֔ד\rb*, \rb which he is to remove|יְסִירֶֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the kidneys|הַכְּלָיֹ֖ת\rb*. \v 11 \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb is to burn them|וְהִקְטִיר֥וֹ\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חָה\rb* \rb as food|לֶ֥חֶם\rb*, \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb If|וְאִ֥ם\rb* \rb one’s offering|קָרְבָּנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb is a goat|עֵ֖ז\rb*, \rb he is to present|וְהִקְרִיב֖וֹ\rb* \rb it before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb He must lay|וְסָמַ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its head|רֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and slaughter|וְשָׁחַ֣ט\rb* \rb it|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb in front of|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb*. \rb Then Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֧ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb shall splatter|וְ֠זָרְקוּ\rb* \rb its blood|דָּמ֛וֹ\rb* \rb on all sides|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb And from|מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb his offering|קָרְבָּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb he shall present|וְהִקְרִ֤יב\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*:\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵ֙לֶב֙\rb* \rb that covers|הַֽמְכַסֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the entrails|הַקֶּ֔רֶב\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵ֔לֶב\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb is on|עַל־\rb* \rb them|הַקֶּֽרֶב׃\rb*, \v 15 \rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb both|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb kidneys|הַכְּלָיֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with the fat|הַחֵ֙לֶב֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵהֶ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb* \rb the loins|הַכְּסָלִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the lobe|הַיֹּתֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the liver|הַכָּבֵ֔ד\rb*, \rb which he is to remove|יְסִירֶֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the kidneys|הַכְּלָיֹ֖ת\rb*. \v 16 \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb is to burn|וְהִקְטִירָ֥ם\rb* \rb the food|לֶ֤חֶם\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חָה\rb* \rb as a food offering|אִשֶּׁה֙\rb*, \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֔חַ\rb* \rb aroma|לְרֵ֣יחַ\rb*. \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fat|חֵ֖לֶב\rb* \rb is the LORD’s|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb This is a permanent|עוֹלָם֙\rb* \rb statute|חֻקַּ֤ת\rb* \rb for the generations to come|לְדֹרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb wherever|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb you live|מֽוֹשְׁבֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*: \rb You must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכֵֽלוּ׃פ\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb fat|חֵ֥לֶב\rb* \rb or any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb blood|דָּ֖ם\rb*.”
\c 4
\s1 Laws for Sin Offerings
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Tell|דַּבֵּ֞ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֘ל\rb* \rb to|לֵאמֹר֒\rb* \rb do as follows|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb with one|נֶ֗פֶשׁ\rb* \rb who sins|תֶחֱטָ֤א\rb* \rb unintentionally|בִשְׁגָגָה֙\rb* \rb against any|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb of the LORD’s|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb commandments|מִצְוֺ֣ת\rb* \rb and does|תֵעָשֶׂ֑ינָה\rb*\rb |וְעָשָׂ֕ה\rb* \rb what is|מֵאַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb forbidden|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb by them|מֵהֵֽנָּה׃\rb*:
\p \v 3 \rb If|אִ֣ם\rb* \rb the anointed|הַמָּשִׁ֛יחַ\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֧ן\rb* \rb sins|יֶחֱטָ֖א\rb*, \rb bringing guilt|לְאַשְׁמַ֣ת\rb* \rb on the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*, \rb he must bring|וְהִקְרִ֡יב\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb a young bull|פַּ֣ר\rb* \rb without blemish|תָּמִ֛ים\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בָּקָ֥ר\rb* \rb as|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb a sin offering|חַטָּאתוֹ֩\rb*\f + \fr 4:3 \ft Or \fqa purification offering\ft ; here and throughout Leviticus\f*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb for the sin|לְחַטָּֽאת׃\rb* \rb he has committed|חָטָ֜א\rb*. \v 4 \rb He must bring|וְהֵבִ֣יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bull|הַפָּ֗ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֛תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֖ד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb lay|וְסָמַ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the bull’s|הַפָּ֔ר\rb* \rb head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb*, \rb and slaughter|וְשָׁחַ֥ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it|הַפָּ֖ר\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Then the anointed|הַמָּשִׁ֖יחַ\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֥ן\rb* \rb shall take|וְלָקַ֛ח\rb* \rb some of the bull’s|הַפָּ֑ר\rb* \rb blood|מִדַּ֣ם\rb* \rb and bring|וְהֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb it|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to dip|וְטָבַ֧ל\rb* \rb his finger|אֶצְבָּע֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the blood|בַּדָּ֑ם\rb* \rb and sprinkle|וְהִזָּ֨ה\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb it|הַדָּ֜ם\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֤בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִים֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in front of|פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the veil|פָּרֹ֥כֶת\rb* \rb of the sanctuary|הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֨ן\rb* \rb must then put|וְנָתַן֩\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֜ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the horns|קַ֠רְנוֹת\rb* \rb of the altar|מִזְבַּ֨ח\rb* \rb of fragrant|הַסַּמִּים֙\rb* \rb incense|קְטֹ֤רֶת\rb* \rb that is before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the Tent|בְּאֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb*. \rb And|וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb he is to pour out|יִשְׁפֹּךְ֙\rb* \rb the rest|כָּל־\rb* \rb of the bull’s|הַפָּ֗ר\rb* \rb blood|דַּ֣ם\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the base|יְסוֹד֙\rb* \rb of the altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb of burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Then|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he shall remove|יָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fat|חֵ֛לֶב\rb* \rb from|מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bull|פַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּ֖את\rb*— \rb the fat|הַחֵ֙לֶב֙\rb* \rb that covers|הַֽמְכַסֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb the entrails|הַקֶּ֔רֶב\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵ֔לֶב\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb is on|עַל־\rb* \rb them|הַקֶּֽרֶב׃\rb*, \v 9 \rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb both|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb kidneys|הַכְּלָיֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with the fat|הַחֵ֙לֶב֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb* \rb the loins|הַכְּסָלִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the lobe|הַיֹּתֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the liver|הַכָּבֵ֔ד\rb*, \rb which he is to remove|יְסִירֶֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the kidneys|הַכְּלָי֖וֹת\rb*— \v 10 \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the fat is removed|יוּרַ֔ם\rb* \rb from the ox|מִשּׁ֖וֹר\rb*\rb |זֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb of the peace offering|הַשְּׁלָמִ֑ים\rb*. \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb shall burn them|וְהִקְטִירָם֙\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of burnt offering|הָעֹלָֽה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb But the hide|ע֤וֹר\rb* \rb of the bull|הַפָּר֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its flesh|בְּשָׂר֔וֹ\rb*, \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb its head|רֹאשׁ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and legs|כְּרָעָ֑יו\rb* \rb and its entrails|וְקִרְבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and dung|וּפִרְשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*— \v 12 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the rest of the bull|הַ֠פָּר\rb*— \rb he must take|וְהוֹצִ֣יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb outside|מִח֨וּץ\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֜ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a ceremonially clean|טָהוֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb place|מָק֤וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ashes|הַדֶּ֔שֶׁן\rb* \rb are poured out|שֶׁ֣פֶךְ\rb*, \rb and there he must burn|וְשָׂרַ֥ף\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb a wood|עֵצִ֖ים\rb* \rb fire|בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb*\rb |יִשָּׂרֵֽף׃פ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ash|הַדֶּ֖שֶׁן\rb* \rb heap|שֶׁ֥פֶךְ\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Now if|וְאִ֨ם\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֤ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb strays unintentionally|יִשְׁגּ֔וּ\rb* \rb and the matter|דָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb escapes|וְנֶעְלַ֣ם\rb* \rb the notice|מֵעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the assembly|הַקָּהָ֑ל\rb* \rb so that they violate|וְ֠עָשׂוּ\rb* \rb any|אַחַ֨ת\rb*\rb |מִכָּל־\rb* \rb of the LORD’s|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb commandments|מִצְוֺ֧ת\rb* \rb and incur guilt|וְאָשֵֽׁמוּ׃\rb* \rb by doing what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is forbidden|לֹא־\rb*\rb |תֵעָשֶׂ֖ינָה\rb*, \v 14 \rb when they become aware|וְנֽוֹדְעָה֙\rb* \rb of the sin|הַֽחַטָּ֔את\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they have committed|חָטְא֖וּ\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb*, \rb then the assembly|הַקָּהָ֜ל\rb*\rb |פַּ֤ר\rb* \rb must bring|וְהִקְרִ֨יבוּ\rb* \rb a young|בֶּן־\rb* \rb bull|בָּקָר֙\rb* \rb as a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֔את\rb* \rb and present|וְהֵבִ֣יאוּ\rb* \rb it|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb The elders|זִקְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the congregation|הָעֵדָ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb are to lay|וְ֠סָמְכוּ\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the bull’s|הַפָּ֖ר\rb* \rb head|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and it|הַפָּ֖ר\rb* \rb shall be slaughtered|וְשָׁחַ֥ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Then the anointed|הַמָּשִׁ֖יחַ\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֥ן\rb* \rb is to bring|וְהֵבִ֛יא\rb* \rb some of the bull’s|הַפָּ֑ר\rb* \rb blood|מִדַּ֣ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֖הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*, \v 17 \rb and he|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb is to dip|וְטָבַ֧ל\rb* \rb his finger|אֶצְבָּע֖וֹ\rb* \rb in|מִן־\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֑ם\rb* \rb and sprinkle|וְהִזָּ֞ה\rb* \rb it seven|שֶׁ֤בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִים֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb in front|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the veil|הַפָּרֹֽכֶת׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb He is also to put|יִתֵּ֣ן׀\rb* \rb some of|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֞ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the horns|קַרְנֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֗חַ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb is before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the Tent|בְּאֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb*, \rb and|וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb he must pour out|יִשְׁפֹּךְ֙\rb* \rb the rest|כָּל־\rb* \rb of the blood|הַדָּ֗ם\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the base|יְסוֹד֙\rb* \rb of the altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb of burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb And|וְאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb he is to remove|יָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fat|חֶלְבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb from it|מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb and burn it|וְהִקְטִ֖יר\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחָה׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb He shall offer|וְעָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb this bull|לַפָּ֔ר\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb he did|עָשָׂה֙\rb* \rb the bull|לְפַ֣ר\rb* \rb for the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּ֔את\rb*\rb |יַעֲשֶׂה־\rb*; \rb in this way|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb will make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֧ר\rb* \rb on their behalf|עֲלֵהֶ֛ם\rb*, \rb and they will be forgiven|וְנִסְלַ֥ח\rb*.\rb |לָהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 21 \rb Then he is to take|וְהוֹצִ֣יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bull|הַפָּ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb outside|מִחוּץ֙\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and burn|וְשָׂרַ֣ף\rb* \rb it|אֹת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he burned|שָׂרַ֔ף\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the first|הָרִאשׁ֑וֹן\rb* \rb bull|הַפָּ֣ר\rb*. \rb It|הֽוּא׃פ\rb* \rb is the sin offering|חַטַּ֥את\rb* \rb for the assembly|הַקָּהָ֖ל\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb When|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb a leader|נָשִׂ֖יא\rb* \rb sins|יֶֽחֱטָ֑א\rb* \rb unintentionally|בִּשְׁגָגָ֖ה\rb* \rb and does|וְעָשָׂ֡ה\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb is prohibited|לֹא־\rb* \rb by any|אַחַ֣ת\rb* \rb of|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺת֩\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָ֜יו\rb*\rb |תֵעָשֶׂ֛ינָה\rb*, \rb he incurs guilt|וְאָשֵֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb |אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb When he becomes aware|הוֹדַ֤ע\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb of the sin|חַטָּאת֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he has committed|חָטָ֖א\rb*, \rb he must bring|וְהֵבִ֧יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb an unblemished|תָּמִֽים׃\rb* \rb male goat|שְׂעִ֥יר\rb*\rb |עִזִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |זָכָ֥ר\rb* \rb as his offering|קָרְבָּנ֛וֹ\rb*. \v 24 \rb He is to lay|וְסָמַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb his hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the goat|הַשָּׂעִ֔יר\rb* \rb and slaughter|וְשָׁחַ֣ט\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb it at the place|בִּמְק֛וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb is slaughtered|יִשְׁחַ֥ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb It|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is a sin offering|חַטָּ֖את\rb*. \v 25 \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb is to take|וְלָקַ֨ח\rb* \rb some of the blood|מִדַּ֤ם\rb* \rb of the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּאת֙\rb* \rb with his finger|בְּאֶצְבָּע֔וֹ\rb*, \rb put it|וְנָתַ֕ן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the horns|קַרְנֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of the altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb of burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb pour out|יִשְׁפֹּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb the rest of the blood|דָּמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the base|יְס֖וֹד\rb* \rb of the altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |הָעֹלָֽה׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb He must burn|יַקְטִ֣יר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its fat|חֶלְבּוֹ֙\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חָה\rb*, \rb like the fat|כְּחֵ֖לֶב\rb*\rb |זֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb of the peace offerings|הַשְּׁלָמִ֑ים\rb*; \rb thus the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb will make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb for|עָלָ֧יו\rb* \rb that man’s sin|מֵחַטָּאת֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and he will be forgiven|וְנִסְלַ֥ח\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb And if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb one|נֶ֧פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אַחַ֛ת\rb* \rb of the common|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb people|מֵעַ֣ם\rb* \rb sins|תֶּחֱטָ֥א\rb* \rb unintentionally|בִשְׁגָגָ֖ה\rb* \rb and does what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is prohibited|לֹא־\rb*\rb |תֵעָשֶׂ֖ינָה\rb*\rb |בַּ֠עֲשֹׂתָהּ\rb* \rb by any|אַחַ֨ת\rb* \rb of the LORD’s|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb commandments|מִמִּצְוֺ֧ת\rb*, \rb he incurs guilt|וְאָשֵֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb |א֚וֹ\rb* \rb When he becomes aware|הוֹדַ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb of the sin|חַטָּאת֖וֹ\rb* \rb he has committed|חָטָ֑א\rb*, \rb he must bring|וְהֵבִ֨יא\rb* \rb an unblemished|תְּמִימָ֣ה\rb* \rb female|נְקֵבָ֔ה\rb* \rb goat|שְׂעִירַ֤ת\rb*\rb |עִזִּים֙\rb* \rb as his offering|קָרְבָּנ֜וֹ\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb that sin|חַטָּאת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |חָטָֽא׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb He is to lay|וְסָמַךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּ֑את\rb* \rb and slaughter|וְשָׁחַט֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it|הַ֣חַטָּ֔את\rb* \rb at the place|בִּמְק֖וֹם\rb* \rb of the burnt offering|הָעֹלָֽה׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֤ן\rb* \rb is to take|וְלָקַ֨ח\rb* \rb some of its blood|מִדָּמָהּ֙\rb* \rb with his finger|בְּאֶצְבָּע֔וֹ\rb*, \rb put it|וְנָתַ֕ן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the horns|קַרְנֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of the altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb of burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb pour out|יִשְׁפֹּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb the rest|כָּל־\rb* \rb of the blood|דָּמָ֣הּ\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the base|יְס֖וֹד\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb Then|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he is to remove|יָסִ֗יר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fat|חֶלְבָּ֣הּ\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb it|חֵלֶב֮\rb* \rb is removed|הוּסַ֣ר\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb*\rb |זֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb the peace offering|הַשְּׁלָמִים֒\rb*, \rb and the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb is to burn|וְהִקְטִ֤יר\rb* \rb it on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חָה\rb* \rb as a pleasing|נִיחֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb aroma|לְרֵ֥יחַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb In this way the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb will make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb for him|עָלָ֛יו\rb*, \rb and he will be forgiven|וְנִסְלַ֥ח\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb If, however|וְאִם־\rb*, \rb he brings|יָבִ֥יא\rb* \rb a lamb|כֶּ֛בֶשׂ\rb*\rb |קָרְבָּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb as a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֑את\rb*, \rb he must bring|יְבִיאֶֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb an unblemished|תְמִימָ֖ה\rb* \rb female|נְקֵבָ֥ה\rb*. \v 33 \rb And he is to lay|וְסָמַךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּ֑את\rb* \rb and slaughter|וְשָׁחַ֤ט\rb* \rb it|אֹתָהּ֙\rb* \rb as a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֔את\rb* \rb at the place|בִּמְק֕וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb is slaughtered|יִשְׁחַ֖ט\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 34 \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb is to take|וְלָקַ֨ח\rb* \rb some of the blood|מִדַּ֤ם\rb* \rb of the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּאת֙\rb* \rb with his finger|בְּאֶצְבָּע֔וֹ\rb*, \rb put it|וְנָתַ֕ן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the horns|קַרְנֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of the altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb of burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb pour out|יִשְׁפֹּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb the rest|כָּל־\rb* \rb of its blood|דָּמָ֣הּ\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the base|יְס֖וֹד\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he shall remove|יָסִ֗יר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fat|חֶלְבָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the fat|חֵֽלֶב־\rb* \rb of the lamb|הַכֶּשֶׂב֮\rb* \rb is removed|יוּסַ֥ר\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֣בַח\rb* \rb from the peace offerings|הַשְּׁלָמִים֒\rb*, \rb and he|הַכֹּהֵ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb shall burn|וְהִקְטִ֨יר\rb* \rb it on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חָה\rb* \rb along with|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the food offerings|אִשֵּׁ֣י\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb In this way the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb will make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb for him|עָלָ֧יו\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the sin|חַטָּאת֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has committed|חָטָ֖א\rb*, \rb and he will be forgiven|וְנִסְלַ֥ח\rb*.[’’]
\c 5
\s1 Sins Requiring a Sin Offering
\p \v 1 “\rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb someone|וְנֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb sins|תֶחֱטָ֗א\rb* \rb by failing|ל֥וֹא\rb* \rb to testify|יַגִּ֖יד\rb* \rb when he hears|וְשָֽׁמְעָה֙\rb* \rb a public|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb charge|אָלָ֔ה\rb* \rb about something he|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb has witnessed|עֵ֔ד\rb*, \rb whether|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb he has seen it|רָאָ֖ה\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb learned of it|יָדָ֑ע\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb*, \rb he shall bear|וְנָשָׂ֥א\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺנֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb if a person|נֶ֗פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb touches|תִּגַּע֮\rb* \rb anything|בְּכָל־\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb unclean|טָמֵא֒\rb*—\rb |אוֹ֩\rb* \rb whether the carcass|בְנִבְלַ֨ת\rb* \rb of any unclean|טְמֵאָ֗ה\rb* \rb wild animal|חַיָּ֜ה\rb*\rb |טְמֵאָ֔ה\rb* \rb or|א֕וֹ\rb*\rb |בְּנִבְלַ֖ת\rb* \rb livestock|בְּהֵמָ֣ה\rb* \rb or|א֤וֹ\rb*\rb |בְּנִבְלַת֙\rb*\rb |טָמֵ֑א\rb* \rb crawling creature|שֶׁ֣רֶץ\rb*— \rb even if he is unaware|וְנֶעְלַ֣ם\rb* \rb of it|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb*, \rb he|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb is unclean|טָמֵ֖א\rb* \rb and guilty|וְאָשֵֽׁם׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb if|כִ֤י\rb* \rb he touches|יִגַּע֙\rb* \rb human|אָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb uncleanness|בְּטֻמְאַ֣ת\rb*— \rb anything|לְכֹל֙\rb*\rb |טֻמְאָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb by which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb one becomes unclean|יִטְמָ֖א\rb*— \rb even if he is unaware|וְנֶעְלַ֣ם\rb* \rb of it|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb*, \rb when he|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb realizes it|יָדַ֖ע\rb*, \rb he is guilty|וְאָשֵֽׁם׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb if|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb someone|נֶ֡פֶשׁ\rb* \rb swears|תִשָּׁבַע֩\rb* \rb thoughtlessly|לְבַטֵּ֨א\rb* \rb with his lips|בִשְׂפָתַ֜יִם\rb* \rb to do anything good|לְהֵיטִ֗יב\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb evil|לְהָרַ֣ע׀\rb*— \rb in|לְ֠כֹל\rb* \rb whatever matter|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb a man|הָאָדָ֛ם\rb* \rb may rashly pronounce|יְבַטֵּ֧א\rb* \rb an oath|בִּשְׁבֻעָ֖ה\rb*— \rb even if he is unaware|וְנֶעְלַ֣ם\rb* \rb of it|מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb*, \rb when he|וְהוּא־\rb* \rb realizes it|יָדַ֥ע\rb*, \rb he is guilty|וְאָשֵׁ֖ם\rb*\rb |לְאַחַ֥ת\rb* \rb in the matter|מֵאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb |וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb If|כִֽי־\rb* \rb someone incurs guilt|יֶאְשַׁ֖ם\rb* \rb in one|לְאַחַ֣ת\rb* \rb of these ways|מֵאֵ֑לֶּה\rb*, \rb he must confess|וְהִ֨תְוַדָּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the sin he has committed|חָטָ֖א\rb*\rb |עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb and he must bring|וְהֵבִ֣יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his guilt offering|אֲשָׁמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֡ה\rb* \rb for|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb the sin|חַטָּאתוֹ֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb he has committed|חָטָ֜א\rb*: \rb a female|נְקֵבָ֨ה\rb* \rb lamb|כִּשְׂבָּ֛ה\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb goat|שְׂעִירַ֥ת\rb*\rb |עִזִּ֖ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֥אן\rb* \rb as a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֑את\rb*. \rb And the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb will make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb for him|עָלָ֛יו\rb* \rb concerning his sin|מֵחַטָּאתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb If, however|וְאִם־\rb*, \rb he cannot|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb afford|תַגִּ֣יע\rb*\rb |יָדוֹ֮\rb*\rb |דֵּ֣י\rb* \rb a lamb|שֶׂה֒\rb*, \rb he may bring|וְהֵבִ֨יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb as restitution|אֲשָׁמ֜וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb for his sin|חָטָ֗א\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb turtledoves|תֹרִ֛ים\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb young|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb pigeons|יוֹנָ֖ה\rb* — \rb one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb as a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֖את\rb* \rb and the other|וְאֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb as a burnt offering|לְעֹלָֽה׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb He is to bring|וְהֵבִ֤יא\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb who shall first|רִאשׁוֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb present|וְהִקְרִ֛יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the one|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb for the sin offering|לַחַטָּ֖את\rb*. \rb He is to twist|וּמָלַ֧ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its head|רֹאשׁ֛וֹ\rb* \rb at the front|מִמּ֥וּל\rb* \rb of its neck|עָרְפּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb without|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb severing it|יַבְדִּֽיל׃\rb*; \v 9 \rb then he is to sprinkle|וְהִזָּ֞ה\rb* \rb some of the blood|מִדַּ֤ם\rb* \rb of the sin offering|הַחַטָּאת֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the side|קִ֣יר\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb*, \rb while the rest|וְהַנִּשְׁאָ֣ר\rb* \rb of the blood|בַּדָּ֔ם\rb* \rb is drained out|יִמָּצֵ֖ה\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the base|יְס֣וֹד\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb*. \rb It is|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb a sin offering|חַטָּ֖את\rb*. \v 10 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the priest must prepare|יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb the second bird|הַשֵּׁנִ֛י\rb* \rb as a burnt offering|עֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb according to the ordinance|כַּמִּשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb*. \rb In this way the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb will make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb for him|עָלָ֧יו\rb* \rb for the sin|מֵחַטָּאת֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has committed|חָטָ֖א\rb*, \rb and he will be forgiven|וְנִסְלַ֥ח\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb he cannot|לֹא֩\rb* \rb afford|תַשִּׂ֨יג\rb*\rb |יָד֜וֹ\rb* \rb two|לִשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb turtledoves|תֹרִ֗ים\rb* \rb or|אוֹ֮\rb* \rb two|לִשְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb young|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb pigeons|יוֹנָה֒\rb*, \rb he may bring|וְהֵבִ֨יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |קָרְבָּנ֜וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |חָטָ֗א\rb* \rb a tenth|עֲשִׂירִ֧ת\rb* \rb of an ephah|הָאֵפָ֛ה\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֖לֶת\rb*\f + \fr 5:11 \fqa A tenth of an ephah \ft is approximately 2 dry quarts or 2.2 liters (probably about 2.6 pounds or 1.2 kilograms of flour).\f* \rb as a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֑את\rb*. \rb He must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb put|יָשִׂ֨ים\rb* \rb olive oil|שֶׁ֗מֶן\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |יִתֵּ֤ן\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb or frankincense|לְבֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶ֜יהָ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb it|הִֽיא׃\rb* \rb is a sin offering|חַטָּ֖את\rb*. \v 12 \rb He is to bring|וֶהֱבִיאָהּ֮\rb* \rb it to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֒\rb*, \rb who shall take|וְקָמַ֣ץ\rb*\rb |הַכֹּהֵ֣ן׀\rb* \rb a handful|מְל֨וֹא\rb*\rb |קֻמְצ֜וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from it|מִ֠מֶּנָּה\rb* \rb as a memorial portion|אַזְכָּרָתָה֙\rb* \rb and burn it|וְהִקְטִ֣יר\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חָה\rb* \rb atop|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the food offerings|אִשֵּׁ֣י\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*; \rb it|הִֽוא׃\rb* \rb is a sin offering|חַטָּ֖את\rb*. \v 13 \rb In this way the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb will make atonement|וְכִפֶּר֩\rb* \rb for him|עָלָ֨יו\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb any|מֵֽאַחַ֥ת\rb* \rb of these|מֵאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb sins|חַטָּאת֧וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has committed|חָטָ֛א\rb*, \rb and he will be forgiven|וְנִסְלַ֣ח\rb*. \rb The remainder will belong to|וְהָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb the priest|לַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb*, \rb like the grain offering|כַּמִּנְחָֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 Laws for Guilt Offerings
\p \v 14 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 15 “\rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb someone|נֶ֚פֶשׁ\rb* \rb acts|תִמְעֹ֣ל\rb* \rb unfaithfully|מַ֔עַל\rb* \rb and sins|וְחָֽטְאָה֙\rb* \rb unintentionally against|בִּשְׁגָגָ֔ה\rb* \rb any of the LORD’s|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb holy things|מִקָּדְשֵׁ֖י\rb*, \rb he must bring|וְהֵבִיא֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his guilt offering|אֲשָׁמ֨וֹ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֜ה\rb*: \rb an unblemished|תָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb ram|אַ֧יִל\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֗אן\rb*, \rb of proper value|בְּעֶרְכְּךָ֛\rb*\f + \fr 5:15 \ft Or \fqa flock or its equivalence\f* \rb in silver|כֶּֽסֶף־\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֥ים\rb* \rb according to the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb shekel|בְּשֶֽׁקֶל־\rb*;\f + \fr 5:15 \fqa A shekel \ft is approximately 0.4 ounces or 11.4 grams of silver.\f* \rb it is a guilt offering|לְאָשָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Regarding any holy thing|הַקֹּ֜דֶשׁ\rb* \rb he has harmed|חָטָ֨א\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb he must make restitution|יְשַׁלֵּ֗ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb by adding|יוֹסֵ֣ף\rb* \rb a fifth|חֲמִֽישִׁתוֹ֙\rb* \rb of its value to it|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and giving|וְנָתַ֥ן\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb it to the priest|לַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb*, \rb who|וְהַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb will make atonement|יְכַפֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb on his behalf|עָלָ֛יו\rb* \rb with the ram|בְּאֵ֥יל\rb* \rb as a guilt offering|הָאָשָׁ֖ם\rb*, \rb and he will be forgiven|וְנִסְלַ֥ח\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb someone|נֶ֙פֶשׁ֙\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb sins|תֶֽחֱטָ֔א\rb* \rb and violates|וְעָֽשְׂתָ֗ה\rb* \rb any|אַחַת֙\rb*\rb |מִכָּל־\rb* \rb of the LORD’s|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb commandments|מִצְוֺ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb even though he was|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |תֵעָשֶׂ֑ינָה\rb* \rb unaware|יָדַ֥ע\rb*, \rb he is guilty|וְאָשֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb and shall bear|וְנָשָׂ֥א\rb* \rb his punishment|עֲוֺנֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb He is to bring|וְ֠הֵבִיא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb an unblemished|תָּמִ֧ים\rb* \rb ram|אַ֣יִל\rb* \rb of proper value|בְּעֶרְכְּךָ֥\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֛אן\rb* \rb as a guilt offering|לְאָשָׁ֖ם\rb*. \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb will make atonement|וְכִפֶּר֩\rb* \rb on his behalf|עָלָ֨יו\rb* \rb for|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb the wrong|שִׁגְגָת֧וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has committed|שָׁגָ֛ג\rb*\rb |וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb in ignorance|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |יָדַ֖ע\rb*, \rb and he will be forgiven|וְנִסְלַ֥ח\rb*. \v 19 \rb It|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb is a guilt offering|אָשָׁ֖ם\rb*; \rb he was certainly guilty|אָשֹׁ֥ם\rb*\rb |אָשַׁ֖ם\rb*\f + \fr 5:19 \ft Or \fqa he has paid full compensation\f* \rb before the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\c 6
\s1 Sins Requiring a Guilt Offering
\p \v 1 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb If|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb someone|נֶ֚פֶשׁ\rb* \rb sins|תֶחֱטָ֔א\rb* \rb and acts|וּמָעֲלָ֥ה\rb* \rb unfaithfully|מַ֖עַל\rb* \rb against the LORD|בַּיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb by deceiving|וְכִחֵ֨שׁ\rb* \rb his neighbor|בַּעֲמִית֜וֹ\rb* \rb in regard to a deposit|בְּפִקָּד֗וֹן\rb* \rb or security|בִתְשׂ֤וּמֶת\rb* \rb entrusted to him|יָד֙\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb stolen|בְגָזֵ֔ל\rb*,\rb |א֖וֹ\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb if he extorts|עָשַׁ֥ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his neighbor|עֲמִיתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb finds|מָצָ֧א\rb* \rb lost property|אֲבֵדָ֛ה\rb* \rb and lies|וְכִ֥חֶשׁ\rb* \rb about it|בָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb and swears|וְנִשְׁבַּ֣ע\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb falsely|שָׁ֑קֶר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*, \rb or if he commits any such sin|לַחֲטֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אַחַ֗ת\rb*\rb |מִכֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |בָהֵֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb a man|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb might commit|יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb*— \v 4 \rb |וְהָיָה֮\rb* \rb once|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he has sinned|יֶחֱטָ֣א\rb* \rb and becomes guilty|וְאָשֵׁם֒\rb*, \rb he must return|וְהֵשִׁ֨יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |גָּזָ֗ל\rb* \rb he has stolen|הַגְּזֵלָ֜ה\rb* \rb or|א֤וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָעֹ֙שֶׁק֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb taken by extortion|עָשָׁ֔ק\rb*, \rb or|א֚וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the deposit|הַפִּקָּד֔וֹן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb entrusted|הָפְקַ֖ד\rb* \rb to him|אִתּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the lost property|הָאֲבֵדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he found|מָצָֽא׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb or|א֠וֹ\rb* \rb anything else|מִכֹּ֞ל\rb* \rb about|עָלָיו֮\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has sworn|יִשָּׁבַ֣ע\rb* \rb falsely|לַשֶּׁקֶר֒\rb*.
\p \rb He must make|בְּרֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb restitution in full|וְשִׁלַּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb*, \rb add|יֹסֵ֣ף\rb* \rb a fifth|וַחֲמִשִׁתָ֖יו\rb* \rb of the value|עָלָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and pay it|יִתְּנֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb to the owner|לַאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |ה֥וּא\rb*\rb |ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb he acknowledges his guilt|אַשְׁמָתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Then he must bring|יָבִ֖יא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb* \rb his guilt offering|אֲשָׁמ֥וֹ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*: \rb an unblemished|תָּמִ֧ים\rb* \rb ram|אַ֣יִל\rb* \rb of proper value|בְּעֶרְכְּךָ֥\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֛אן\rb*\rb |לְאָשָׁ֖ם\rb*. \v 7 \rb In this way the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb will make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb for him|עָלָ֧יו\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and he will be forgiven|וְנִסְלַ֣ח\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb anything|אַחַ֛ת\rb*\rb |מִכֹּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb he may have done|יַעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb to incur guilt|לְאַשְׁמָ֥ה\rb*.”
\s1 The Burnt Offering
\p \v 8 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 9 “\rb Command|צַ֤ו\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֣יו\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb that this|זֹ֥את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֑ה\rb*: \rb The burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֡ה\rb*\rb |הִ֣וא\rb* \rb is to remain|עַל֩\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the hearth|מוֹקְדָ֨ה\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֤חַ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb night|הַלַּ֙יְלָה֙\rb*, \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning|הַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb*, \rb and the fire|וְאֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb must be kept burning|תּ֥וּקַד\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb And the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb shall put on|וְלָבַ֨שׁ\rb* \rb his linen|בַ֗ד\rb* \rb robe|מִדּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb and linen|בַד֮\rb*\rb |יִלְבַּ֣שׁ\rb* \rb undergarments|וּמִֽכְנְסֵי־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |בְּשָׂרוֹ֒\rb*, \rb and he shall remove|וְהֵרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb the ashes|הַדֶּ֗שֶׁן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb of the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb that the fire|הָאֵ֛שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has consumed|תֹּאכַ֥ל\rb* \rb and place them|וְשָׂמ֕וֹ\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֖צֶל\rb* \rb it|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Then he must take off|וּפָשַׁט֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his garments|בְּגָדָ֔יו\rb*, \rb put on|וְלָבַ֖שׁ\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֑ים\rb* \rb clothes|בְּגָדִ֣ים\rb*, \rb and carry|וְהוֹצִ֤יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ashes|הַדֶּ֙שֶׁן֙\rb* \rb outside|מִח֣וּץ\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a ceremonially clean|טָהֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb place|מָק֖וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb The fire|וְהָאֵ֨שׁ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֤חַ\rb* \rb shall be kept burning|תּֽוּקַד־\rb*; \rb it must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be extinguished|תִכְבֶּ֔ה\rb*. \rb Every morning|בַּבֹּ֣קֶר\rb*\rb |בַּבֹּ֑קֶר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb is to add|וּבִעֵ֨ר\rb* \rb wood|עֵצִ֖ים\rb* \rb to the fire|עָלֶ֧יהָ\rb*, \rb arrange|וְעָרַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָֽעֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*, \rb and burn|וְהִקְטִ֥יר\rb* \rb the fat portions|חֶלְבֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the peace offerings|הַשְּׁלָמִֽים׃\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb*. \v 13 \rb The fire|אֵ֗שׁ\rb* \rb shall be kept burning|תּוּקַ֥ד\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb continually|תָּמִ֛יד\rb*; \rb it must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be extinguished|תִכְבֶֽה׃ס\rb*.
\s1 The Grain Offering
\p \v 14 \rb Now this|וְזֹ֥את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the grain offering|הַמִּנְחָ֑ה\rb*: \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb shall present|הַקְרֵ֨ב\rb* \rb it|אֹתָ֤הּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb front|פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb The priest is to remove|וְהֵרִ֨ים\rb* \rb a handful|בְּקֻמְצ֗וֹ\rb* \rb of|מִמֶּ֜נּוּ\rb* \rb fine flour|מִסֹּ֤לֶת\rb*\rb |הַמִּנְחָה֙\rb* \rb and olive oil|וּמִשַּׁמְנָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb*, \rb together with all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the frankincense|הַלְּבֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb from the grain offering|הַמִּנְחָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and burn|וְהִקְטִ֣יר\rb* \rb the memorial portion|אַזְכָּרָתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֗חַ\rb* \rb as a pleasing|נִיחֹ֛חַ\rb* \rb aroma|רֵ֧יחַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb are to eat|יֹאכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb the remainder|וְהַנּוֹתֶ֣רֶת\rb*. \rb It must be eaten|תֵּֽאָכֵל֙\rb* \rb without leaven|מַצּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb in a holy|קָדֹ֔שׁ\rb* \rb place|בְּמָק֣וֹם\rb*; \rb they are to eat it|יֹאכְלֽוּהָ׃\rb* \rb in the courtyard|בַּחֲצַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the Tent|אֹֽהֶל־\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֖ד\rb*. \v 17 \rb It must not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb be baked|תֵאָפֶה֙\rb* \rb with leaven|חָמֵ֔ץ\rb*; \rb I have assigned|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb it as their portion|חֶלְקָ֛ם\rb* \rb of My food offerings|מֵאִשָּׁ֑י\rb*. \rb It is|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb most|קֹ֤דֶשׁ\rb* \rb holy|קָֽדָשִׁים֙\rb*, \rb like the sin offering|כַּחַטָּ֖את\rb* \rb and the guilt offering|וְכָאָשָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb Any|כָּל־\rb* \rb male|זָכָ֞ר\rb* \rb among the sons|בִּבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb may eat it|יֹֽאכֲלֶ֔נָּה\rb*. \rb This is a permanent|עוֹלָם֙\rb* \rb portion|חָק־\rb* \rb from the food offerings|מֵאִשֵּׁ֖י\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb for the generations to come|לְדֹרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb Anything|כֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb touches|יִגַּ֥ע\rb* \rb them|בָּהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will become holy|יִקְדָּֽשׁ׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 19 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 20 “\rb This|זֶ֡ה\rb* \rb is the offering|קָרְבַּן֩\rb* \rb that Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֨ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֜יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb must present|יַקְרִ֣יבוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb on the day|בְּיוֹם֙\rb* \rb he is anointed|הִמָּשַׁ֣ח\rb*:\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb a tenth|עֲשִׂירִ֨ת\rb* \rb of an ephah|הָאֵפָ֥ה\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֛לֶת\rb*\f + \fr 6:20 \fqa A tenth of an ephah \ft is approximately 2 dry quarts or 2.2 liters (probably about 2.6 pounds or 1.2 kilograms of flour).\f* \rb as a regular|תָּמִ֑יד\rb* \rb grain offering|מִנְחָ֖ה\rb*, \rb half|מַחֲצִיתָ֣הּ\rb* \rb of it in the morning|בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb and half|וּמַחֲצִיתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb in the evening|בָּעָֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb It shall be prepared|תֵּעָשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb with oil|בַּשֶּׁ֛מֶן\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb a griddle|מַחֲבַ֗ת\rb*;\f + \fr 6:21 \ft That is, a shallow pan for baking or frying\f* \rb you are to bring it|תְּבִיאֶ֑נָּה\rb* \rb well-kneaded|מֻרְבֶּ֣כֶת\rb* \rb and present it|תַּקְרִ֥יב\rb* \rb as a grain offering|מִנְחַ֣ת\rb* \rb broken|תֻּפִינֵי֙\rb*\f + \fr 6:21 \ft Or \fqa baked\f* \rb in pieces|פִּתִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb aroma|רֵֽיחַ־\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb The priest|וְהַכֹּהֵ֨ן\rb*, \rb who is one of Aaron’s sons|מִבָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb and will be anointed|הַמָּשִׁ֧יחַ\rb* \rb to take his place|תַּחְתָּ֛יו\rb*, \rb is to prepare it|יַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb*.\rb |אֹתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb As a permanent|עוֹלָ֕ם\rb* \rb portion|חָק־\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb it must be burned|תָּקְטָֽר׃\rb* \rb completely|כָּלִ֥יל\rb*. \v 23 \rb Every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb grain offering|מִנְחַ֥ת\rb* \rb for a priest|כֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb shall be burned|תִּהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb completely|כָּלִ֥יל\rb*; \rb it is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to be eaten|תֵאָכֵֽל׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 The Sin Offering
\p \v 24 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 25 “\rb Tell|דַּבֵּ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֣יו\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb that this|זֹ֥את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּ֑את\rb*: \rb In the place|בִּמְק֡וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֜ה\rb* \rb is slaughtered|תִּשָּׁחֵ֨ט\rb*, \rb the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּאת֙\rb* \rb shall be slaughtered|תִּשָּׁחֵ֤ט\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*; \rb it is most|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb holy|קָֽדָשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |הִֽוא׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb who offers|הַֽמְחַטֵּ֥א\rb* \rb it|אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb shall eat it|יֹאכֲלֶ֑נָּה\rb*; \rb it must be eaten|תֵּֽאָכֵ֔ל\rb* \rb in a holy|קָדֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb place|בְּמָק֤וֹם\rb*, \rb in the courtyard|בַּחֲצַ֖ר\rb* \rb of the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb Anything|כֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb touches|יִגַּ֥ע\rb* \rb its flesh|בִּבְשָׂרָ֖הּ\rb* \rb will become holy|יִקְדָּ֑שׁ\rb*, \rb and if|וַאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb any of the blood|מִדָּמָהּ֙\rb* \rb is spattered|יִזֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a garment|הַבֶּ֔גֶד\rb*, \rb you must wash|תְּכַבֵּ֖ס\rb* \rb it|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb*\rb |יִזֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb in a holy|קָדֹֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb place|בְּמָק֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb The clay|חֶ֛רֶשׂ\rb* \rb pot|וּכְלִי־\rb* \rb in which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the sin offering is boiled|תְּבֻשַּׁל־\rb* \rb must be broken|יִשָּׁבֵ֑ר\rb*; \rb if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb it is boiled|בֻּשָּׁ֔לָה\rb* \rb in a bronze|נְחֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb pot|בִּכְלִ֤י\rb*, \rb the pot must be scoured|וּמֹרַ֥ק\rb* \rb and rinsed|וְשֻׁטַּ֖ף\rb* \rb with water|בַּמָּֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb Any|כָּל־\rb* \rb male|זָכָ֥ר\rb* \rb among the priests|בַּכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb may eat it|יֹאכַ֣ל\rb*;\rb |אֹתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb it is|הִֽוא׃\rb* \rb most|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb holy|קָֽדָשִׁ֖ים\rb*. \v 30 \rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb But no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb sin offering|חַטָּ֡את\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb may be eaten|תֵאָכֵ֑ל\rb* \rb if its blood|מִדָּמָ֜הּ\rb* \rb has been brought|יוּבָ֨א\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֧הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֛ד\rb* \rb to make atonement|לְכַפֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb in the Holy Place|בַּקֹּ֖דֶשׁ\rb*;\rb |בָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb it must be burned|תִּשָּׂרֵֽף׃פ\rb*.[’’]
\c 7
\s1 The Guilt Offering
\p \v 1 “\rb Now this|וְזֹ֥את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the guilt offering|הָאָשָׁ֑ם\rb*, \rb which is|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb most|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb holy|קָֽדָשִׁ֖ים\rb*: \v 2 \rb The guilt offering|הָאָשָׁ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb must be slaughtered|יִשְׁחֲטוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in the place|בִּמְק֗וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָ֣עֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb is slaughtered|יִשְׁחֲט֖וּ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and the priest shall splatter|יִזְרֹ֥ק\rb* \rb its blood|דָּמ֛וֹ\rb* \rb on all sides|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*. \v 3 \rb And|וְאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fat|חֶלְבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb from|מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb it|אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb shall be offered|יַקְרִ֣יב\rb*: \rb the fat tail|הָֽאַלְיָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵ֖לֶב\rb* \rb that covers|הַֽמְכַסֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the entrails|הַקֶּֽרֶב׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb both|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb kidneys|הַכְּלָיֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with the fat|הַחֵ֙לֶב֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb* \rb the loins|הַכְּסָלִ֑ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the lobe|הַיֹּתֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the liver|הַכָּבֵ֔ד\rb*, \rb which is to be removed|יְסִירֶֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the kidneys|הַכְּלָיֹ֖ת\rb*. \v 5 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb shall burn|וְהִקְטִ֨יר\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֤ם\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חָה\rb* \rb as a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*; \rb it|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is a guilt offering|אָשָׁ֖ם\rb*. \v 6 \rb Every|כָּל־\rb* \rb male|זָכָ֥ר\rb* \rb among the priests|בַּכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb may eat of it|יֹאכְלֶ֑נּוּ\rb*. \rb It must be eaten|יֵאָכֵ֔ל\rb* \rb in a holy|קָדוֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb place|בְּמָק֤וֹם\rb*; \rb it is|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb most|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb holy|קָֽדָשִׁ֖ים\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb The guilt offering|כָּֽאָשָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb is like the sin offering|כַּֽחַטָּאת֙\rb*; \rb the same|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb law|תּוֹרָ֥ה\rb* \rb applies to both|לָהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb It belongs to|יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb makes atonement|יְכַפֶּר־\rb* \rb with it|בּ֖וֹ\rb*. \v 8 \rb As for the priest|וְהַ֨כֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb who presents|הַמַּקְרִ֖יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a burnt offering|עֹ֣לַת\rb* \rb for anyone|אִ֑ישׁ\rb*, \rb the hide|ע֤וֹר\rb* \rb of that offering|הָֽעֹלָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |הִקְרִ֔יב\rb*\rb |לַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb belongs to him|ל֥וֹ\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Likewise , every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb grain offering|מִנְחָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb is baked|תֵּֽאָפֶה֙\rb* \rb in an oven|בַּתַּנּ֔וּר\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb or cooked|נַעֲשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb in a pan|בַמַּרְחֶ֖שֶׁת\rb*\f + \fr 7:9 \ft That is, a deep pan or stew pan\f* \rb or on|וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb a griddle|מַחֲבַ֑ת\rb*\f + \fr 7:9 \ft That is, a shallow pan for baking or frying\f* \rb belongs|תִֽהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb to|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb the priest|לַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb who presents|הַמַּקְרִ֥יב\rb* \rb it|אֹתָ֖הּ\rb*, \v 10 \rb and every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb grain offering|מִנְחָ֥ה\rb*, \rb whether dry|וַחֲרֵבָ֑ה\rb* \rb or mixed|בְלוּלָֽה־\rb* \rb with oil|בַשֶּׁ֖מֶן\rb*, \rb belongs equally|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |כְּאָחִֽיו׃פ\rb* \rb to|תִּהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֛ן\rb*.
\s1 The Peace Offering
\p \v 11 \rb Now this|וְזֹ֥את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַ֖ת\rb*\rb |זֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb of the peace offering|הַשְּׁלָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb one may present|יַקְרִ֖יב\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*: \v 12 \rb If|אִ֣ם\rb* \rb he offers it|יַקְרִיבֶנּוּ֒\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb thanksgiving|תּוֹדָה֮\rb*, \rb then along with|עַל־\rb* \rb the sacrifice|זֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb of thanksgiving|הַתּוֹדָ֗ה\rb* \rb he shall offer|וְהִקְרִ֣יב׀\rb* \rb unleavened|מַצּוֹת֙\rb* \rb cakes|חַלּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb mixed|בְּלוּלֹ֣ת\rb* \rb with olive oil|בַּשֶּׁ֔מֶן\rb*, \rb unleavened|מַצּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb wafers|וּרְקִיקֵ֥י\rb* \rb coated|מְשֻׁחִ֣ים\rb* \rb with oil|בַּשָּׁ֑מֶן\rb*, \rb and well-kneaded|מֻרְבֶּ֔כֶת\rb* \rb cakes|חַלֹּ֖ת\rb* \rb of fine flour|וְסֹ֣לֶת\rb* \rb mixed|בְּלוּלֹ֥ת\rb* \rb with oil|בַּשָּֽׁמֶן׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Along|עַל־\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb*\rb |זֶ֖בַח\rb* \rb his peace offering|שְׁלָמָֽיו׃\rb* \rb of thanksgiving|תּוֹדַ֥ת\rb* \rb he is to present|יַקְרִ֖יב\rb* \rb an offering|קָרְבָּנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb with cakes|חַלֹּת֙\rb* \rb of leavened|חָמֵ֔ץ\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֣חֶם\rb*. \v 14 \rb From|מִמֶּ֤נּוּ\rb* \rb the cakes he must present|וְהִקְרִ֨יב\rb* \rb one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb portion of each|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb offering|קָרְבָּ֔ן\rb* \rb as a contribution|תְּרוּמָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb It belongs|יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb to|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb the priest|לַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb who sprinkles|הַזֹּרֵ֛ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the blood|דַּ֥ם\rb* \rb of the peace offering|הַשְּׁלָמִ֖ים\rb*. \v 15 \rb The meat|וּבְשַׂ֗ר\rb* \rb of the sacrifice|זֶ֚בַח\rb* \rb of his peace offering|שְׁלָמָ֔יו\rb* \rb of thanksgiving|תּוֹדַ֣ת\rb* \rb must be eaten|יֵאָכֵ֑ל\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb he offers it|קָרְבָּנ֖וֹ\rb*; \rb none|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb of it|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb may be left|יַנִּ֥יחַ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning|בֹּֽקֶר׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb If, however|וְאִם־\rb*, \rb the sacrifice|זֶ֚בַח\rb* \rb he offers|קָרְבָּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb is a vow|נֶ֣דֶר׀\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb a freewill offering|נְדָבָ֗ה\rb*, \rb it shall be eaten|יֵאָכֵ֑ל\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֛וֹם\rb* \rb he presents|הַקְרִיב֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his sacrifice|זִבְח֖וֹ\rb*, \rb but the remainder|וְהַנּוֹתָ֥ר\rb* \rb may be eaten|יֵאָכֵֽל׃\rb* \rb on|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb the next day|וּמִֽמָּחֳרָ֔ת\rb*. \v 17 \rb But any meat|מִבְּשַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of the sacrifice|הַזָּ֑בַח\rb* \rb remaining|וְהַנּוֹתָ֖ר\rb* \rb until the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֔י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּוֹם֙\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb must be burned up|יִשָּׂרֵֽף׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb If|וְאִ֣ם\rb* \rb any of|הֵאָכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb the meat|מִבְּשַׂר־\rb*\rb |זֶ֨בַח\rb* \rb from his peace offering|שְׁלָמָ֜יו\rb* \rb is eaten|יֵ֠אָכֵל\rb* \rb on the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁי֮\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb it will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be accepted|יֵרָצֶה֒\rb*. \rb It will not|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb be credited|יֵחָשֵׁ֛ב\rb* \rb to|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb the one who presented it|הַמַּקְרִ֣יב\rb*;\rb |אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb it shall be|יִהְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb an abomination|פִּגּ֣וּל\rb*, \rb and the one|וְהַנֶּ֛פֶשׁ\rb* \rb who eats|הָאֹכֶ֥לֶת\rb* \rb of it|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb shall bear|תִּשָּֽׂא׃\rb* \rb his iniquity|עֲוֺנָ֥הּ\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Meat|וְהַבָּשָׂ֞ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb touches|יִגַּ֤ע\rb* \rb anything|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb unclean|טָמֵא֙\rb* \rb must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be eaten|יֵֽאָכֵ֔ל\rb*;\rb |בָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb it is to be burned up|יִשָּׂרֵ֑ף\rb*. \rb As for|בָּשָֽׂר׃\rb* \rb any other meat|וְהַ֨בָּשָׂ֔ר\rb*, \rb anyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb who is ceremonially clean|טָה֖וֹר\rb* \rb may eat it|יֹאכַ֥ל\rb*. \v 20 \rb But if anyone|וְהַנֶּ֜פֶשׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb is unclean|וְטֻמְאָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb eats|תֹּאכַ֣ל\rb* \rb meat|בָּשָׂ֗ר\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֤בַח\rb* \rb from the peace offering|הַשְּׁלָמִים֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb belongs to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |עָלָ֑יו\rb*, \rb that|הַהִ֖וא\rb* \rb person|הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb must be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb from his people|מֵעַמֶּֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb one|וְנֶ֜פֶשׁ\rb* \rb touches|תִגַּ֣ע\rb* \rb anything|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb unclean|טָמֵ֗א\rb*, \rb whether|א֣וֹ׀\rb* \rb human|אָדָם֙\rb* \rb uncleanness|בְּטֻמְאַ֤ת\rb*, \rb an unclean|טְמֵאָ֗ה\rb* \rb animal|בִּבְהֵמָ֣ה\rb*, \rb or|א֚וֹ\rb* \rb any|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb unclean|טָמֵ֔א\rb*, \rb detestable thing|שֶׁ֣קֶץ\rb*, \rb and then eats|וְאָכַ֛ל\rb* \rb any of the meat|מִבְּשַׂר־\rb*\rb |זֶ֥בַח\rb* \rb of the peace offering|הַשְּׁלָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb belongs to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb that|הַהִ֖וא\rb* \rb person|הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb must be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb from his people|מֵעַמֶּֽיהָ׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 Fat and Blood Forbidden
\p \v 22 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 23 “\rb Speak|דַּבֵּ֛ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and say|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb You are not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to eat|תֹאכֵֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb of the fat|חֵ֜לֶב\rb* \rb of an ox|שׁ֥וֹר\rb*, \rb a sheep|וְכֶ֛שֶׂב\rb*, \rb or a goat|וָעֵ֖ז\rb*. \v 24 \rb The fat|וְחֵ֤לֶב\rb* \rb of an animal found dead|נְבֵלָה֙\rb*\rb |וְחֵ֣לֶב\rb* \rb or mauled by wild beasts|טְרֵפָ֔ה\rb* \rb may be used|יֵעָשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb for any other|לְכָל־\rb* \rb purpose|מְלָאכָ֑ה\rb*, \rb but you must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb eat|וְאָכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb it|תֹאכְלֻֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb If|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb anyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb eats|אֹכֵ֣ל\rb* \rb the fat|חֵ֔לֶב\rb* \rb of an animal|הַ֨בְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb from which|מִן־\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb may be presented|יַקְרִ֥יב\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb the one|הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb who eats it|הָאֹכֶ֖לֶת\rb* \rb must be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb from his people|מֵֽעַמֶּֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכְל֔וּ\rb* \rb the blood|דָּם֙\rb* \rb of any bird|לָע֖וֹף\rb* \rb or animal|וְלַבְּהֵמָֽה׃\rb* \rb in any|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb of your dwellings|מוֹשְׁבֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \v 27 \rb If anyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |נֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb eats|תֹּאכַ֣ל\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb blood|דָּ֑ם\rb*, \rb that|הַהִ֖וא\rb* \rb person|הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb must be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb from his people|מֵֽעַמֶּֽיהָ׃פ\rb*.’”
\s1 The Priests’ Portion
\p \v 28 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 29 “\rb Speak|דַּבֵּ֛ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and say|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb Anyone who presents|הַמַּקְרִ֞יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |זֶ֤בַח\rb* \rb a peace offering|שְׁלָמָיו֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb must bring|יָבִ֧יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it|קָרְבָּנ֛וֹ\rb* \rb as his sacrifice|מִזֶּ֥בַח\rb*\rb |שְׁלָמָֽיו׃\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*. \v 30 \rb With his own hands|יָדָ֣יו\rb* \rb he is to bring|תְּבִיאֶ֔ינָה\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the food offerings|אִשֵּׁ֣י\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*;\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he shall bring|יְבִיאֶ֔נּוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵ֤לֶב\rb*, \rb together with|עַל־\rb* \rb the breast|הֶֽחָזֶה֙\rb*, \rb and wave|לְהָנִ֥יף\rb* \rb the breast|הֶחָזֶ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb as a wave offering|תְּנוּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to burn|וְהִקְטִ֧יר\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵ֖לֶב\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חָה\rb*, \rb but the breast|הֶֽחָזֶ֔ה\rb* \rb belongs to|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּלְבָנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb And|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb you are to give|תִּתְּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb the right|הַיָּמִ֔ין\rb* \rb thigh|שׁ֣וֹק\rb* \rb to the priest|לַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb as a contribution|תְרוּמָ֖ה\rb*\rb |מִזִּבְחֵ֖י\rb* \rb from your peace offering|שַׁלְמֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 33 \rb The son|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֑ן\rb* \rb who presents|הַמַּקְרִ֞יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the blood|דַּ֧ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb fat|הַחֵ֖לֶב\rb* \rb of the peace offering|הַשְּׁלָמִ֛ים\rb* \rb shall have|תִהְיֶ֛ה\rb* \rb the right|הַיָּמִ֖ין\rb* \rb thigh|שׁ֥וֹק\rb* \rb as a portion|לְמָנָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb |כִּי֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I have taken|לָקַ֙חְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb from the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb the breast|חֲזֵ֨ה\rb* \rb of the wave offering|הַתְּנוּפָ֜ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb and the thigh|שׁ֣וֹק\rb* \rb of the contribution|הַתְּרוּמָ֗ה\rb*\rb |מִזִּבְחֵ֖י\rb* \rb of their peace offerings|שַׁלְמֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and I have given|וָאֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb them|אֹ֠תָם\rb* \rb to Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֨ן\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֤ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּלְבָנָיו֙\rb* \rb as a permanent|עוֹלָ֔ם\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb portion|לְחָק־\rb* \rb from the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 35 \rb This|זֹ֣את\rb* \rb is the portion|מִשְׁחַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the food offerings|מֵאִשֵּׁ֖י\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb for Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb*\rb |וּמִשְׁחַ֣ת\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb since the day|בְּיוֹם֙\rb* \rb they were presented|הִקְרִ֣יב\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb to serve the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb as priests|לְכַהֵ֖ן\rb*. \v 36 \rb On the day|בְּיוֹם֙\rb* \rb they were anointed|מָשְׁח֣וֹ\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb commanded that|צִוָּ֨ה\rb* \rb this|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb be given|לָתֵ֣ת\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb by|לָהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*.\rb |מֵאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb It is a permanent|עוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb portion|חֻקַּ֥ת\rb* \rb for the generations to come|לְדֹרֹתָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb This|זֹ֣את\rb* \rb is the law|הַתּוֹרָ֗ה\rb* \rb of the burnt offering|לָֽעֹלָה֙\rb*, \rb the grain offering|לַמִּנְחָ֔ה\rb*, \rb the sin offering|וְלַֽחַטָּ֖את\rb*, \rb the guilt offering|וְלָאָשָׁ֑ם\rb*, \rb the ordination offering|וְלַ֨מִּלּוּאִ֔ים\rb*,\rb |וּלְזֶ֖בַח\rb* \rb and the peace offering|הַשְּׁלָמִֽים׃\rb*, \v 38 \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave|צִוָּ֧ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb Sinai|סִינָ֑י\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֨וֹם\rb* \rb He commanded|צַוֺּת֜וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb to present|לְהַקְרִ֧יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their offerings|קָרְבְּנֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the Wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of Sinai|סִינָֽי׃פ\rb*.
\c 8
\s1 Moses Consecrates Aaron and His Sons
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Take|קַ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֣יו\rb*\rb |אִתּ֔וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb their garments|הַבְּגָדִ֔ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the anointing|הַמִּשְׁחָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֣מֶן\rb*, \rb the bull|פַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּ֗את\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb rams|הָֽאֵילִ֔ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and the basket|סַ֥ל\rb* \rb of unleavened bread|הַמַּצּֽוֹת׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb |וְאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb and assemble|הַקְהֵ֑ל\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָעֵדָ֖ה\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb had commanded him|צִוָּ֥ה\rb*, \rb and the assembly|הָֽעֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb gathered|וַתִּקָּהֵל֙\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb And Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|אֶל־\rb*\rb |הָעֵדָ֑ה\rb*, “\rb This|זֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb is what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb to be done|לַעֲשֽׂוֹת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb presented|וַיַּקְרֵ֣ב\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֑יו\rb* \rb and washed|וַיִּרְחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with water|בַּמָּֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb He put|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb the tunic|הַכֻּתֹּ֗נֶת\rb* \rb on Aaron|עָלָ֜יו\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb tied the sash|בָּֽאַבְנֵ֔ט\rb* \rb around him|וַיַּחְגֹּ֤ר\rb*,\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb clothed|וַיַּלְבֵּ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb him|אֶֽת־\rb* \rb with the robe|הַמְּעִ֔יל\rb*, \rb and put|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb the ephod|הָאֵפֹ֑ד\rb* \rb on him|עָלָ֖יו\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb He tied the woven band|בְּחֵ֙שֶׁב֙\rb* \rb of the ephod|הָֽאֵפֹ֔ד\rb* \rb around|וַיַּחְגֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb him|אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb and fastened it|וַיֶּאְפֹּ֥ד\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb*. \v 8 \rb Then he put|וַיָּ֥שֶׂם\rb* \rb the breastpiece|הַחֹ֑שֶׁן\rb* \rb on|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb him|אֶת־\rb* \rb and placed|וַיִּתֵּן֙\rb* \rb the Urim|הָאוּרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Thummim|הַתֻּמִּֽים׃\rb*\f + \fr 8:8 \ft Literally \fqa Lights and Perfections\f* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the breastpiece|הַחֹ֔שֶׁן\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 9 \rb Moses also put|וַיָּ֥שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the turban|הַמִּצְנֶ֖פֶת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Aaron’s head|רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and set|וַיָּ֨שֶׂם\rb*\rb |עַֽל־\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָב֙\rb* \rb plate|צִ֤יץ\rb*, \rb the holy|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb diadem|נֵ֣זֶר\rb*, \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the front|מ֣וּל\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֗יו\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb of the turban|הַמִּצְנֶ֜פֶת\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb him|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Next, Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb the anointing|הַמִּשְׁחָ֔ה\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֣מֶן\rb* \rb and anointed|וַיִּמְשַׁ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in it|בּ֑וֹ\rb*; \rb and so he consecrated|וַיְקַדֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָֽם׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb He sprinkled|וַיַּ֥ז\rb* \rb some of|מִמֶּ֛נּוּ\rb* \rb the oil on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb anointing|וַיִּמְשַׁ֨ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֜חַ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its utensils|כֵּלָ֗יו\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the basin|הַכִּיֹּ֛ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with its stand|כַּנּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb to consecrate them|לְקַדְּשָֽׁם׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb He also poured|וַיִּצֹק֙\rb* \rb some of the anointing|הַמִּשְׁחָ֔ה\rb* \rb oil|מִשֶּׁ֣מֶן\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֑ן\rb* \rb head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb and anointed|וַיִּמְשַׁ֥ח\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to consecrate him|לְקַדְּשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb presented|וַיַּקְרֵ֨ב\rb* \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*, \rb put|וַיַּלְבִּשֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb tunics on them|כֻּתֳּנֹת֙\rb*, \rb wrapped sashes|אַבְנֵ֔ט\rb* \rb around them|וַיַּחְגֹּ֤ר\rb*,\rb |אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb and tied|וַיַּחֲבֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb headbands|מִגְבָּע֑וֹת\rb* \rb on them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb him|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*.
\s1 The Priests’ Sin Offering
\p \v 14 \rb Moses then brought the bull|פַּ֣ר\rb* \rb near|וַיַּגֵּ֕שׁ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb for the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּ֑את\rb*, \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֤ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָיו֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb laid|וַיִּסְמֹ֨ךְ\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its head|רֹ֖אשׁ\rb*\rb |פַּ֥ר\rb*\rb |הַֽחַטָּֽאת׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb slaughtered the bull|וַיִּשְׁחָ֗ט\rb*, \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb some of the blood|הַדָּם֙\rb*, \rb and applied|וַ֠יִּתֵּן\rb* \rb it with his finger|בְּאֶצְבָּע֔וֹ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb all four|סָבִיב֙\rb* \rb horns|קַרְנ֨וֹת\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֤חַ\rb*, \rb purifying|וַיְחַטֵּ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb*.\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb He poured out|יָצַק֙\rb* \rb the rest of the blood|הַדָּ֗ם\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the base|יְס֣וֹד\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb and consecrated it|וַֽיְקַדְּשֵׁ֖הוּ\rb* \rb so that atonement could be made|לְכַפֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb on it|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb Moses also|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֗ח\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵלֶב֮\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was on|עַל־\rb* \rb the entrails|הַקֶּרֶב֒\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb the lobe|יֹתֶ֣רֶת\rb* \rb of the liver|הַכָּבֵ֔ד\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and both|שְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb kidneys|הַכְּלָיֹ֖ת\rb* \rb and|וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb their fat|חֶלְבְּהֶ֑ן\rb*, \rb and burned it all|וַיַּקְטֵ֥ר\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחָה׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb But|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the bull|הַפָּ֤ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with its hide|עֹרוֹ֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb flesh|בְּשָׂר֣וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and dung|פִּרְשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb he burned|שָׂרַ֣ף\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb outside|מִח֖וּץ\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb him|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*.
\s1 The Priests’ Burnt Offering
\p \v 18 \rb Then Moses presented|וַיַּקְרֵ֕ב\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the ram|אֵ֣יל\rb* \rb for the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֧ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֛יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb laid|וַֽיִּסְמְכ֞וּ\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its head|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb*\rb |הָאָֽיִל׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb slaughtered the ram|וַיִּשְׁחָ֑ט\rb* \rb and splattered|וַיִּזְרֹ֨ק\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֛ם\rb* \rb on all sides|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*. \v 20 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb He|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb cut|נִתַּ֖ח\rb* \rb the ram|הָאַ֔יִל\rb* \rb into pieces|לִנְתָחָ֑יו\rb* \rb and burned|וַיַּקְטֵ֤ר\rb* \rb the head|הָרֹ֔אשׁ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the pieces|הַנְּתָחִ֖ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the fat|הַפָּֽדֶר׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb He washed|רָחַ֣ץ\rb* \rb the entrails|הַקֶּ֥רֶב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and legs|הַכְּרָעַ֖יִם\rb* \rb with water|בַּמָּ֑יִם\rb*\rb |מֹשֶׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and burned|וַיַּקְטֵר֩\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb ram|הָאַ֜יִל\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֗חָה\rb*\rb |ה֤וּא\rb* \rb as a burnt offering|עֹלָ֨ה\rb*, \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb aroma|לְרֵֽיחַ־\rb*, \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |הוּא֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*.
\s1 The Ram of Ordination
\p \v 22 \rb After that, Moses presented|וַיַּקְרֵב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the other|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb ram|הָאַ֣יִל\rb*, \rb the ram|אֵ֖יל\rb* \rb of ordination|הַמִּלֻּאִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֧ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֛יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb laid|וַֽיִּסְמְכ֞וּ\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its|הָאָֽיִל׃\rb* \rb head|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb*. \v 23 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb slaughtered the ram|וַיִּשְׁחָ֓ט׀\rb* \rb and took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb some of its blood|מִדָּמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and put|וַיִּתֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb right|הַיְמָנִ֑ית\rb* \rb earlobe|תְּנ֥וּךְ\rb*\rb |אֹֽזֶן־\rb*, \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the thumb|בֹּ֤הֶן\rb* \rb of his right|הַיְמָנִ֔ית\rb* \rb hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb*, \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the big toe|בֹּ֥הֶן\rb* \rb of his right|הַיְמָנִֽית׃\rb* \rb foot|רַגְל֖וֹ\rb*. \v 24 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb* \rb also presented|וַיַּקְרֵ֞ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and put|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּם֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their right|הַיְמָנִ֔ית\rb* \rb earlobes|תְּנ֤וּךְ\rb*\rb |אָזְנָם֙\rb*, \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the thumbs|בֹּ֤הֶן\rb* \rb of their right|הַיְמָנִ֔ית\rb* \rb hands|יָדָם֙\rb*, \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the big toes|בֹּ֥הֶן\rb* \rb of their right|הַיְמָנִ֑ית\rb* \rb feet|רַגְלָ֖ם\rb*. \rb Then he|מֹשֶׁ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb splattered|וַיִּזְרֹ֨ק\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֛ם\rb* \rb on all sides|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַֽמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb And Moses took|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵ֣לֶב\rb*—\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the fat tail|הָֽאַלְיָ֗ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵלֶב֮\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was on|עַל־\rb* \rb the entrails|הַקֶּרֶב֒\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb the lobe|יֹתֶ֣רֶת\rb* \rb of the liver|הַכָּבֵ֔ד\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and both|שְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb kidneys|הַכְּלָיֹ֖ת\rb* \rb with their|וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb fat|חֶלְבְּהֶ֑ן\rb*—\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb as well as the right|הַיָּמִֽין׃\rb* \rb thigh|שׁ֥וֹק\rb*. \v 26 \rb And from the basket|וּמִסַּ֨ל\rb* \rb of unleavened bread|הַמַּצּ֜וֹת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb was before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb he took|לָ֠קַח\rb* \rb one|אַחַת֙\rb* \rb cake|חַלַּ֨ת\rb* \rb of unleavened bread|מַצָּ֤ה\rb*, \rb one|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb cake|וְֽחַלַּ֨ת\rb* \rb of bread|לֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb made with oil|שֶׁ֛מֶן\rb*, \rb and one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb wafer|וְרָקִ֣יק\rb*, \rb and he placed them|וַיָּ֙שֶׂם֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the fat portions|הַ֣חֲלָבִ֔ים\rb* \rb and on|וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the right|הַיָּמִֽין׃\rb* \rb thigh|שׁ֥וֹק\rb*. \v 27 \rb He put|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all these|הַכֹּ֔ל\rb* \rb in|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the hands|כַּפֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb*\rb |וְעַ֖ל\rb*\rb |כַּפֵּ֣י\rb* \rb and his sons|בָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb and waved|וַיָּ֧נֶף\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb as a wave offering|תְּנוּפָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb took these|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb their hands|כַּפֵּיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and burned them|וַיַּקְטֵ֥ר\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חָה\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֑ה\rb*. \rb This|הֵם֙\rb* \rb was an ordination offering|מִלֻּאִ֥ים\rb*, \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֔חַ\rb* \rb aroma|לְרֵ֣יחַ\rb*, \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb He also|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb the breast|הֶ֣חָזֶ֔ה\rb* —\rb |הָיָה֙\rb* \rb Moses’|לְמֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb* \rb portion|לְמָנָ֔ה\rb* \rb of the ram|מֵאֵ֣יל\rb* \rb of ordination|הַמִּלֻּאִ֗ים\rb* — \rb and waved|וַיְנִיפֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb it before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb as a wave offering|תְנוּפָ֖ה\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb him|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb Next, Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb some of|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the anointing|הַמִּשְׁחָ֗ה\rb* \rb oil|מִשֶּׁ֣מֶן\rb* \rb and some of the blood|הַדָּם֮\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּחַ֒\rb* \rb and sprinkled them|וַיַּ֤ז\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb and his garments|בְּגָדָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֛יו\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and their|בָנָ֖יו\rb*\rb |אִתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb garments|בִּגְדֵ֥י\rb*. \rb So he consecrated|וַיְקַדֵּ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and his garments|בְּגָדָ֔יו\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb as well as Aaron’s sons|בָּנָ֛יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and their|בָנָ֖יו\rb*\rb |אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb garments|בִּגְדֵ֥י\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb And Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Boil|בַּשְּׁל֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the meat|הַבָּשָׂר֮\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵד֒\rb* \rb and eat|תֹּאכְל֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb it|וְאֶ֨ת־\rb* \rb there|וְשָׁם֙\rb* \rb with the bread|הַלֶּ֔חֶם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb is in the basket|בְּסַ֣ל\rb* \rb of ordination offerings|הַמִּלֻּאִ֑ים\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I commanded|צִוֵּ֙יתִי֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb are to eat it|יֹאכְלֻֽהוּ׃\rb*.’ \v 32 \rb Then you must burn up|בָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |תִּשְׂרֹֽפוּ׃\rb* \rb the remainder|וְהַנּוֹתָ֥ר\rb* \rb of the meat|בַּבָּשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb and bread|וּבַלָּ֑חֶם\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb You must not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb go outside|תֵֽצְאוּ֙\rb* \rb the entrance|וּמִפֶּתַח֩\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֨הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֜ד\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb until|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb the days|י֣וֹם\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֖י\rb* \rb of your ordination|מִלֻּאֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb are complete|מְלֹ֔את\rb*; \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb it will take seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb to ordain|יְמַלֵּ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you|יֶדְכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 34 \rb What|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb has been done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb today|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb has been commanded|צִוָּ֧ה\rb* \rb by the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |לַעֲשֹׂ֖ת\rb* \rb in order to make atonement|לְכַפֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb on your behalf|עֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb You must remain|תֵּשְׁב֨וּ\rb* \rb at the entrance|וּפֶתַח֩\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֨הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֜ד\rb* \rb day|יוֹמָ֤ם\rb* \rb and night|וָלַ֙יְלָה֙\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb and keep|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb charge|מִשְׁמֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb so that you will not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb die|תָמ֑וּתוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb I have been commanded|צֻוֵּֽיתִי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 36 \rb So Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֑יו\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃ס\rb*.
\c 9
\s1 Aaron’s First Offerings
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb On the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֔י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb summoned|קָרָ֣א\rb* \rb Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּלְבָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb and the elders|וּלְזִקְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb*, “\rb Take|קַח־\rb* \rb for yourself|לְ֠ךָ\rb* \rb a young bull|עֵ֣גֶל\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בָּקָ֧ר\rb* \rb for a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֛את\rb* \rb and a ram|וְאַ֥יִל\rb* \rb for a burnt offering|לְעֹלָ֖ה\rb*, \rb both without blemish|תְּמִימִ֑ם\rb*, \rb and present them|וְהַקְרֵ֖ב\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb Then speak|תְּדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and say|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb Take|קְח֤וּ\rb* \rb a male goat|שְׂעִיר־\rb*\rb |עִזִּים֙\rb* \rb for a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֔את\rb*, \rb a calf|וְעֵ֨גֶל\rb* \rb and a lamb|וָכֶ֧בֶשׂ\rb* — \rb both a year old|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֛ה\rb* \rb and without blemish|תְּמִימִ֖ם\rb* — \rb for a burnt offering|לְעֹלָֽה׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb an ox|וְשׁ֨וֹר\rb*\f + \fr 9:4 \ft Or \fqa a bull \ft or \fqa a cow\ft ; also in verses 18 and 19\f* \rb and a ram|וָאַ֜יִל\rb* \rb for a peace offering|לִשְׁלָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb to sacrifice|לִזְבֹּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and a grain offering|וּמִנְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb mixed|בְּלוּלָ֣ה\rb* \rb with oil|בַשָּׁ֑מֶן\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will appear|נִרְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 5 \rb So they took|וַיִּקְח֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the front|פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb*, \rb and the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָ֣עֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb drew near|וַֽיִּקְרְבוּ֙\rb* \rb and stood|וַיַּֽעַמְד֖וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb And Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb This|זֶ֧ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֛ר\rb* \rb is what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb you to do|תַּעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb*, \rb so that the glory|כְּב֥וֹד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb may appear|וְיֵרָ֥א\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb*, “\rb Approach|קְרַ֤ב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb and sacrifice|וַעֲשֵׂ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your sin offering|חַטָּֽאתְךָ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and your burnt offering|עֹ֣לָתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb to make atonement|וְכַפֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb for yourself|בַּֽעַדְךָ֖\rb* \rb and for|וּבְעַ֣ד\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*. \rb And sacrifice|וַעֲשֵׂ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people’s|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb offering|קָרְבַּ֤ן\rb* \rb to make atonement|וְכַפֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb for them|בַּֽעֲדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb So Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb approached|וַיִּקְרַ֥ב\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb and slaughtered|וַיִּשְׁחַ֛ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the calf|עֵ֥גֶל\rb* \rb as a sin offering|הַחַטָּ֖את\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb for himself|לֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb The sons|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb brought|וַ֠יַּקְרִבוּ\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּם֮\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֒\rb*, \rb and he dipped|וַיִּטְבֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb his finger|אֶצְבָּעוֹ֙\rb* \rb in the blood|בַּדָּ֔ם\rb* \rb and applied|וַיִּתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb it to|עַל־\rb* \rb the horns|קַרְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb*. \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he poured out|יָצַ֔ק\rb* \rb the rest of the blood|הַדָּ֣ם\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the base|יְס֖וֹד\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb On the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חָה\rb* \rb he burned|הִקְטִ֖יר\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵ֨לֶב\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the kidneys|הַכְּלָיֹ֜ת\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the lobe|הַיֹּתֶ֤רֶת\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the liver|הַכָּבֵד֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the sin offering|הַ֣חַטָּ֔את\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb But|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he burned up|שָׂרַ֣ף\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb the flesh|הַבָּשָׂ֖ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the hide|הָע֑וֹר\rb* \rb outside|מִח֖וּץ\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Then Aaron slaughtered|וַיִּשְׁחַ֖ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֑ה\rb*. \rb His|אַהֲרֹ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb brought him|וַ֠יַּמְצִאוּ\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֔ם\rb*, \rb and he splattered|וַיִּזְרְקֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb all sides|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*. \v 13 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb They brought|הִמְצִ֧יאוּ\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֛יו\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֗ה\rb* \rb piece by piece|לִנְתָחֶ֖יהָ\rb*, \rb including|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the head|הָרֹ֑אשׁ\rb*, \rb and he burned them|וַיַּקְטֵ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb He washed|וַיִּרְחַ֥ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the entrails|הַקֶּ֖רֶב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the legs|הַכְּרָעָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and burned them|וַיַּקְטֵ֥ר\rb* \rb atop|עַל־\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Aaron then presented|וַיַּקְרֵ֕ב\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the people’s|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb offering|קָרְבַּ֣ן\rb*. \rb He took|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the male goat|שְׂעִ֤יר\rb* \rb for the people’s|לָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb sin offering|הַֽחַטָּאת֙\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb slaughtered it|וַיִּשְׁחָטֵ֥הוּ\rb*, \rb and offered it for sin|וַֽיְחַטְּאֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb like the first one|כָּרִאשֽׁוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb He presented|וַיַּקְרֵ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb and offered it|וַֽיַּעֲשֶׂ֖הָ\rb* \rb according to the ordinance|כַּמִּשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Next he presented|וַיַּקְרֵב֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the grain offering|הַמִּנְחָה֒\rb*, \rb took|וַיְמַלֵּ֤א\rb* \rb a handful|כַפּוֹ֙\rb* \rb of it|מִמֶּ֔נָּה\rb*, \rb and burned|וַיַּקְטֵ֖ר\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb in addition to|מִלְּבַ֖ד\rb* \rb the morning’s|הַבֹּֽקֶר׃\rb* \rb burnt offering|עֹלַ֥ת\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Then he slaughtered|וַיִּשְׁחַ֤ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ox|הַשּׁוֹר֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the ram|הָאַ֔יִל\rb* \rb as the people’s|לָעָ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |זֶ֥בַח\rb* \rb peace offering|הַשְּׁלָמִ֖ים\rb*. \rb His|אַהֲרֹ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb brought him|וַ֠יַּמְצִאוּ\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּם֙\rb*,\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and he splattered|וַיִּזְרְקֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb all sides|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb They also brought the fat portions|הַחֲלָבִ֖ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the ox|הַשּׁ֑וֹר\rb*\rb |וּמִן־\rb* \rb and the ram|הָאַ֔יִל\rb*— \rb the fat tail|הָֽאַלְיָ֤ה\rb*, \rb the fat covering|וְהַֽמְכַסֶּה֙\rb* \rb the entrails, the kidneys|וְהַכְּלָיֹ֔ת\rb*, \rb and the lobe|וְיֹתֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb of the liver|הַכָּבֵֽד׃\rb*— \v 20 \rb and placed|וַיָּשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הַחֲלָבִ֖ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the breasts|הֶחָז֑וֹת\rb*. \rb Aaron burned|וַיַּקְטֵ֥ר\rb* \rb the fat portions|הַחֲלָבִ֖ים\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחָה׃\rb*, \v 21 \rb but|וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb he|אַהֲרֹ֛ן\rb* \rb waved|הֵנִ֧יף\rb* \rb the breasts|הֶחָז֗וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and the right|הַיָּמִ֔ין\rb* \rb thigh|שׁ֣וֹק\rb* \rb as a wave offering|תְּנוּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֧ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb lifted up|וַיִּשָּׂ֨א\rb* \rb his hands|יָדוֹ\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb and blessed them|וַֽיְבָרְכֵ֑ם\rb*. \rb And having made|מֵעֲשֹׂ֧ת\rb* \rb the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּ֛את\rb*, \rb the burnt offering|וְהָעֹלָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and the peace offering|וְהַשְּׁלָמִֽים׃\rb*, \rb he stepped down|וַיֵּ֗רֶד\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb then entered|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb*. \rb When they came out|וַיֵּ֣צְא֔וּ\rb*, \rb they blessed|וַֽיְבָרֲכ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and the glory|כְבוֹד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb Fire|אֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb came|וַתֵּ֤צֵא\rb* \rb out from the presence|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and consumed|וַתֹּ֙אכַל֙\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the fat portions|הַחֲלָבִ֑ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*. \rb And when all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb saw it|וַיַּ֤רְא\rb*, \rb they shouted for joy|וַיָּרֹ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb and fell|וַֽיִּפְּל֖וּ\rb* \rb facedown|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\c 10
\s1 The Sin of Nadab and Abihu
\p \v 1 \rb Now Aaron’s|אַ֠הֲרֹן\rb* \rb sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb Nadab|נָדָ֨ב\rb* \rb and Abihu|וַאֲבִיה֜וּא\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקְח֣וּ\rb* \rb their censers|מַחְתָּת֗וֹ\rb*, \rb put|וַיִּתְּנ֤וּ\rb* \rb fire|אֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb in them|בָהֵן֙\rb* \rb and added|וַיָּשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb incense|קְטֹ֑רֶת\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb*, \rb and offered|וַיַּקְרִ֜בוּ\rb* \rb unauthorized|זָרָ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 10:1 \ft Or \fqa strange\f* \rb fire|אֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb contrary to|לֹ֦א\rb* \rb His command|צִוָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb So fire|אֵ֛שׁ\rb* \rb came out|וַתֵּ֥צֵא\rb* \rb from the presence|מִלִּפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and consumed|וַתֹּ֣אכַל\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and they died|וַיָּמֻ֖תוּ\rb* \rb in the presence of|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb*, “\rb This|הוּא֩\rb* \rb is what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה׀\rb* \rb meant|דִּבֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb when He said|לֵאמֹר֙\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb To those who come near Me|בִּקְרֹבַ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb I will show My holiness|אֶקָּדֵ֔שׁ\rb*,
\q1 \rb and in|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the sight of|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb I will reveal My glory|אֶכָּבֵ֑ד\rb*.’”
\p \rb But Aaron|אַהֲרֹֽן׃\rb* \rb remained silent|וַיִּדֹּ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb Mishael|מִֽישָׁאֵל֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֣ל\rb* \rb and Elzaphan|אֶלְצָפָ֔ן\rb*,\f + \fr 10:4 \fqa Elzaphan \ft is a variant of \fqa Elizaphan\ft ; see Numbers 3:30.\f* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֑ן\rb* \rb uncle|דֹּ֣ד\rb* \rb Uzziel|עֻזִּיאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb*, “\rb Come here|קִ֠רְב֞וּ\rb*; \rb carry|שְׂא֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bodies of your cousins|אֲחֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb outside|מִח֖וּץ\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb*, \rb away from the front|פְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*.” \v 5 \rb So they came forward|וַֽיִּקְרְב֗וּ\rb* \rb and carried them|וַיִּשָּׂאֻם֙\rb*, \rb still in their tunics|בְּכֻתֳּנֹתָ֔ם\rb*,\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb outside|מִח֖וּץ\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \rb had directed|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֡ן\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֜יו\rb* \rb Eleazar|וּלְאֶלְעָזָר֩\rb* \rb and Ithamar|וּלְאִֽיתָמָ֨ר׀\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let your hair|רָֽאשֵׁיכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb become disheveled|תִּפְרָ֣עוּ׀\rb*\f + \fr 10:6 \ft Or \fqa Do not uncover your heads\f* \rb and do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb tear|תִפְרֹ֙מוּ֙\rb* \rb your garments|וּבִגְדֵיכֶ֤ם\rb*, \rb or else|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb you will die|תָמֻ֔תוּ\rb*, \rb and the LORD will be angry|יִקְצֹ֑ף\rb* \rb with|וְעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָעֵדָ֖ה\rb*. \rb But your brothers|וַאֲחֵיכֶם֙\rb*, \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb may mourn on account of|יִבְכּוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the fire|הַשְּׂרֵפָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has ignited|שָׂרַ֥ף\rb*. \v 7 \rb You shall not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb go outside|תֵֽצְאוּ֙\rb* \rb the entrance|וּמִפֶּתַח֩\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֨הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֜ד\rb*, \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb you will die|תָּמֻ֔תוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb anointing|מִשְׁחַ֥ת\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֛מֶן\rb* \rb is on you|עֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*.”
\p \rb So they did|וַֽיַּעֲשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb as Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃פ\rb* \rb instructed|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb*.
\s1 Restrictions for Priests
\p \v 8 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 9 “\rb You|אַתָּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb and your sons|וּבָנֶ֣יךָ\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֗ךְ\rb* \rb are not|אַל־\rb* \rb to drink|תֵּ֣שְׁתְּ׀\rb* \rb wine|יַ֣יִן\rb* \rb or strong drink|וְשֵׁכָ֞ר\rb* \rb when you enter|בְּבֹאֲכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֖ד\rb*, \rb or else|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb you will die|תָמֻ֑תוּ\rb*; \rb this is a permanent|עוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb statute|חֻקַּ֥ת\rb* \rb for the generations to come|לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb You must distinguish|וּֽלֲהַבְדִּ֔יל\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the holy|הַקֹּ֖דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and the common|הַחֹ֑ל\rb*, \rb between|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb the clean|הַטָּהֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb and the unclean|הַטָּמֵ֖א\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb*, \v 11 \rb so that you may teach|וּלְהוֹרֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the statutes|הַ֣חֻקִּ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has given|דִּבֶּ֧ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb And Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֣ל\rb* \rb and his remaining|הַנּֽוֹתָרִים֒\rb* \rb sons|בָּנָיו֮\rb*, \rb Eleazar|אֶ֠לְעָזָר\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and Ithamar|אִ֨יתָמָ֥ר׀\rb*, “\rb Take|קְח֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the grain offering|הַמִּנְחָ֗ה\rb* \rb that remains|הַנּוֹתֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb from the food offerings|מֵאִשֵּׁ֣י\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and eat it|וְאִכְל֥וּהָ\rb* \rb without leaven|מַצּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֣צֶל\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb it is|הִֽוא׃\rb* \rb most|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb holy|קָֽדָשִׁ֖ים\rb*. \v 13 \rb You shall eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֹתָהּ֙\rb* \rb it in a holy|קָדֹ֔שׁ\rb* \rb place|בְּמָק֣וֹם\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb it|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb is your share|חָקְךָ֤\rb*\rb |וְחָק־\rb* \rb and your sons’ share|בָּנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb of the food offerings|מֵאִשֵּׁ֖י\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*; \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb I have been commanded|צֻוֵּֽיתִי׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb And|וְאֵת֩\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb and your sons|וּבָנֶ֥יךָ\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb may eat|תֹּֽאכְלוּ֙\rb* \rb the breast|חֲזֵ֨ה\rb* \rb of the wave offering|הַתְּנוּפָ֜ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb and the thigh|שׁ֣וֹק\rb* \rb of the contribution|הַתְּרוּמָ֗ה\rb* \rb in a ceremonially clean|טָה֔וֹר\rb* \rb place|בְּמָק֣וֹם\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb these portions|חָקְךָ֤\rb*\rb |וְחָק־\rb* \rb have been assigned|נִתְּנ֔וּ\rb* \rb to you and your children|בָּנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |מִזִּבְחֵ֥י\rb* \rb from the peace offerings|שַׁלְמֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb They are to bring|יָבִ֔יאוּ\rb* \rb the thigh|שׁ֣וֹק\rb* \rb of the contribution|הַתְּרוּמָ֞ה\rb* \rb and the breast|וַחֲזֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the wave offering|הַתְּנוּפָ֗ה\rb*, \rb together with|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb the fat portions|הַחֲלָבִים֙\rb* \rb of the food offerings|אִשֵּׁ֤י\rb*, \rb to wave|לְהָנִ֥יף\rb* \rb as a wave offering|תְּנוּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb It will belong permanently|עוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb to|וְהָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb you and your children|וּלְבָנֶ֤יךָ\rb*,\rb |אִתְּךָ֙\rb*\rb |לְחָק־\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb Later|וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb*, \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb searched carefully|דָּרֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |דָּרַ֛שׁ\rb* \rb for the goat|שְׂעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּ֗את\rb*, \rb and behold|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb*, \rb it had been burned up|שֹׂרָ֑ף\rb*. \rb He was angry|וַ֠יִּקְצֹף\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֤ר\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and Ithamar|אִֽיתָמָר֙\rb*, \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb remaining|הַנּוֹתָרִ֖ם\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*, \rb and asked|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 17 “\rb Why|מַדּ֗וּעַ\rb* \rb didn’t you|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb eat|אֲכַלְתֶּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּאת֙\rb* \rb in the holy|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb place|בִּמְק֣וֹם\rb*? \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb it|הִ֑וא\rb*\rb |וְאֹתָ֣הּ׀\rb* \rb is most|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb holy|קָֽדָשִׁ֖ים\rb*; \rb it was given|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb to take away|לָשֵׂאת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the guilt|עֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of the congregation|הָעֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb by making atonement|לְכַפֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb for them|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb Since|הֵ֚ן\rb* \rb its blood|דָּמָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb was not|לֹא־\rb* \rb brought|הוּבָ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb inside|פְּנִ֑ימָה\rb* \rb the holy place|הַקֹּ֖דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb you should have eaten|אָכ֨וֹל\rb*\rb |תֹּאכְל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֛הּ\rb* \rb it in the sanctuary area|בַּקֹּ֖דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I commanded|צִוֵּֽיתִי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 19 \rb But Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb* \rb replied|וַיְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb*, “\rb Behold|הֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb this very day|הַ֠יּוֹם\rb* \rb they presented|הִקְרִ֨יבוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their sin offering|חַטָּאתָ֤ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and their burnt offering|עֹֽלָתָם֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*. \rb Since these things|כָּאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb have happened to me|וַתִּקְרֶ֥אנָה\rb*,\rb |אֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb if I had eaten|וְאָכַ֤לְתִּי\rb* \rb the sin offering|חַטָּאת֙\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*, \rb would it have been acceptable|הַיִּיטַ֖ב\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*?”
\p \v 20 \rb And when Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb heard this explanation|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb*, \rb he was satisfied|וַיִּיטַ֖ב\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינָֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\c 11
\s1 Clean and Unclean Animals
\p \v 1 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb spoke again|וַיְדַבֵּ֧ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*, \rb telling|לֵאמֹ֥ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵהֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Say|דַּבְּר֛וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb |זֹ֤את\rb* \rb Of all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the beasts|הַבְּהֵמָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*, \rb these ones|הַֽחַיָּה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you may eat|תֹּאכְל֔וּ\rb*: \v 3 \rb You may eat|תֹּאכֵֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb any|כֹּ֣ל׀\rb* \rb animal|בַּבְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb that has a split|שֶׁ֙סַע֙\rb*\rb |פְּרָסֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |מַפְרֶ֣סֶת\rb* \rb hoof|פַּרְסָ֗ה\rb* \rb completely divided|וְשֹׁסַ֤עַת\rb* \rb and that chews|מַעֲלַ֥ת\rb* \rb the cud|גֵּרָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb But|אַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb of those|אֶת־\rb* \rb that only chew|מִֽמַּעֲלֵי֙\rb* \rb the cud|הַגֵּרָ֔ה\rb* \rb or only have a divided|וּמִמַּפְרִיסֵ֖י\rb* \rb hoof|הַפַּרְסָ֑ה\rb*,\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb you are not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to eat|תֹֽאכְל֔וּ\rb* \rb the following|זֶה֙\rb*:\f + \fr 11:4 \ft The precise identification of some of the birds and animals in this chapter is uncertain.\f*
\b 
\li1 \rb The camel|הַ֠גָּמָל\rb*, \rb though|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb chews|מַעֲלֵ֨ה\rb* \rb the cud|גֵרָ֜ה\rb*, \rb does not|אֵינֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb have a divided|מַפְרִ֔יס\rb* \rb hoof|וּפַרְסָה֙\rb*; \rb it|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is unclean|טָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 5 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb The rock badger|הַשָּׁפָ֗ן\rb*,\f + \fr 11:5 \ft Or \fqa The coney \ft or \fqa The hyrax\f* \rb though|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb chews|מַעֲלֵ֤ה\rb* \rb the cud|גֵרָה֙\rb*, \rb does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb have a divided|יַפְרִ֑יס\rb* \rb hoof|וּפַרְסָ֖ה\rb*; \rb it|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is unclean|טָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 6 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb The rabbit|הָאַרְנֶ֗בֶת\rb*, \rb though|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb chews|מַעֲלַ֤ת\rb* \rb the cud|גֵּרָה֙\rb*, \rb does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb have a divided|הִפְרִ֑יסָה\rb* \rb hoof|וּפַרְסָ֖ה\rb*; \rb it|הִ֖וא\rb* \rb is unclean|טְמֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*.
