\p \v 39 \rb If|וְכִ֤י\rb* \rb an|מִן־\rb* \rb animal|הַבְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |הִ֥יא\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb may eat|לְאָכְלָ֑ה\rb* \rb dies|יָמוּת֙\rb*, \rb anyone who touches|הַנֹּגֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb the carcass|בְּנִבְלָתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb will be unclean|יִטְמָ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 40 \rb Whoever eats|וְהָֽאֹכֵל֙\rb* \rb from the carcass|מִנִּבְלָתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb must wash|יְכַבֵּ֥ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb and will be unclean|וְטָמֵ֣א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָ֑רֶב\rb*, \rb and anyone who picks up|וְהַנֹּשֵׂא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the carcass|נִבְלָתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb must wash|יְכַבֵּ֥ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb and will be unclean|וְטָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*.
\p \v 41 \rb Every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb creature|הַשֶּׁ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb that moves|הַשֹּׁרֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb along|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb is detestable|שֶׁ֥קֶץ\rb*; \rb it|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be eaten|יֵאָכֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 42 \rb Do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכְל֖וּם\rb* \rb any creature|הַשֶּׁ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb that moves|הַשֹּׁרֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb along|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb whether|כֹּל֩\rb* \rb it crawls|הוֹלֵ֨ךְ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its belly|גָּח֜וֹן\rb* \rb or|וְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb walks|הוֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֗ע\rb* \rb or|עַ֚ד\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb more|מַרְבֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb feet|רַגְלַ֔יִם\rb*;\rb |לְכָל־\rb* \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb such creatures|הֵֽם׃\rb* \rb are detestable|שֶׁ֥קֶץ\rb*.
\p \v 43 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb defile|תְּשַׁקְּצוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb yourselves|נַפְשֹׁ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb by any|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb crawling creature|הַשֶּׁ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |הַשֹּׁרֵ֑ץ\rb*; \rb do not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb become unclean|תִֽטַּמְּאוּ֙\rb* \rb or defiled|וְנִטְמֵתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb by them|בָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 44 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶם֒\rb*; \rb consecrate yourselves, therefore|וְהִתְקַדִּשְׁתֶּם֙\rb*, \rb and be|וִהְיִיתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb holy|קְדֹשִׁ֔ים\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I|אָ֑נִי\rb* \rb am holy|קָד֖וֹשׁ\rb*.\f + \fr 11:44 \ft Here and in verse 45; cited in 1 Peter 1:16\f* \rb You must not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb defile|תְטַמְּאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb yourselves|נַפְשֹׁ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb by any|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb creature|הַשֶּׁ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb that crawls|הָרֹמֵ֥שׂ\rb* \rb along|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 45 \rb For|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb who brought you up|הַֽמַּעֲלֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb so that I would be|לִהְיֹ֥ת\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God|לֵאלֹהִ֑ים\rb*; \rb therefore be|וִהְיִיתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb holy|קְדֹשִׁ֔ים\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I|אָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb am holy|קָד֖וֹשׁ\rb*.
\p \v 46 \rb This|זֹ֣את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַ֤ת\rb* \rb regarding animals|הַבְּהֵמָה֙\rb*, \rb birds|וְהָע֔וֹף\rb*, \rb all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb living|הַֽחַיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb creatures|נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb that move|הָרֹמֶ֖שֶׂת\rb* \rb in the water|בַּמָּ֑יִם\rb*, \rb and all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb creatures|נֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb* \rb that crawl|הַשֹּׁרֶ֥צֶת\rb* \rb along|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 47 \rb You must distinguish|לְהַבְדִּ֕יל\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the unclean|הַטָּמֵ֖א\rb* \rb and the clean|הַטָּהֹ֑ר\rb*,\rb |וּבֵ֤ין\rb* \rb between|וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb animals|הַֽחַיָּה֙\rb* \rb that may be eaten|הַֽנֶּאֱכֶ֔לֶת\rb*\rb |וּבֵין֙\rb* \rb and those|הַֽחַיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb may not|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |תֵאָכֵֽל׃פ\rb*.’”
\c 12
\s1 Purification after Childbirth
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Say|דַּבֵּ֞ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb A woman who|אִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb becomes pregnant|תַזְרִ֔יעַ\rb* \rb and gives birth to|וְיָלְדָ֖ה\rb* \rb a son|זָכָ֑ר\rb* \rb will be unclean|וְטָֽמְאָה֙\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb as she is during the days|כִּימֵ֛י\rb* \rb of her menstruation|נִדַּ֥ת\rb*\rb |דְּוֺתָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |תִּטְמָֽא׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb And on the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֑י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb the flesh|בְּשַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb of the boy’s foreskin|עָרְלָתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb is to be circumcised|יִמּ֖וֹל\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb The woman shall continue|תֵּשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in purification|טָהֳרָ֑ה\rb* \rb from her bleeding|בִּדְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb for thirty-three|וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יוֹם֙\rb*. \rb She must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb touch|תִגָּ֗ע\rb* \rb anything|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb sacred|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb or go|תָבֹ֔א\rb* \rb into|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the sanctuary|הַמִּקְדָּשׁ֙\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of her purification|טָהֳרָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb are complete|מְלֹ֖את\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb If, however|וְאִם־\rb*, \rb she gives birth to|תֵלֵ֔ד\rb* \rb a daughter|נְקֵבָ֣ה\rb*, \rb the woman will be unclean|וְטָמְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb for two weeks|שְׁבֻעַ֖יִם\rb* \rb as she is during her menstruation|כְּנִדָּתָ֑הּ\rb*. \rb Then she must continue|תֵּשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb purification|טָהֳרָֽה׃\rb* \rb from her bleeding|דְּמֵ֥י\rb* \rb for sixty-six|וְשִׁשִּׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |יוֹם֙\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb When the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of her purification|טָהֳרָ֗הּ\rb* \rb are complete|וּבִמְלֹ֣את׀\rb*, \rb whether for a son|לְבֵן֮\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb for a daughter|לְבַת֒\rb*, \rb she is to bring|תָּבִ֞יא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֥תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹֽהֶל־\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֖ד\rb* \rb a year-old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שְׁנָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb lamb|כֶּ֤בֶשׂ\rb* \rb for a burnt offering|לְעֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb and a young|וּבֶן־\rb* \rb pigeon|יוֹנָ֥ה\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb a turtledove|תֹ֖ר\rb* \rb for a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֑את\rb*. \v 7 \rb And the priest will present them|וְהִקְרִיב֞וֹ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb for her|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb*; \rb and she shall be ceremonially cleansed|וְטָהֲרָ֖ה\rb* \rb from her flow|מִמְּקֹ֣ר\rb* \rb of blood|דָּמֶ֑יהָ\rb*. \rb This|זֹ֤את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַת֙\rb* \rb for a woman giving birth|הַיֹּלֶ֔דֶת\rb*, \rb whether to a male|לַזָּכָ֖ר\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb to a female|לַנְּקֵבָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb she cannot|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb afford|תִמְצָ֣א\rb*\rb |דֵּ֣י\rb*\rb |יָדָהּ֮\rb* \rb a lamb|שֶׂה֒\rb*, \rb she shall bring|וְלָקְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּֽי־\rb* \rb turtledoves|תֹרִ֗ים\rb* \rb or|א֤וֹ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb young|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb pigeons|יוֹנָ֔ה\rb*,\f + \fr 12:8 \ft Cited in Luke 2:24\f* \rb one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb for a burnt offering|לְעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and the other|וְאֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb for a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֑את\rb*. \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb will make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb for her|עָלֶ֛יהָ\rb*, \rb and she will be clean|וְטָהֵֽרָה׃פ\rb*.’”
\c 13
\s1 Laws about Skin Diseases
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb someone|אָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb has|יִהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb a swelling|שְׂאֵ֤ת\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb rash|סַפַּ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb bright spot|בַהֶ֔רֶת\rb* \rb on his skin|בְעוֹר־\rb*\rb |בְּשָׂרוֹ֙\rb* \rb that may be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb an infectious|צָרָ֑עַת\rb* \rb skin|בְעוֹר־\rb*\rb |בְּשָׂר֖וֹ\rb* \rb disease|לְנֶ֣גַע\rb*,\f + \fr 13:2 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa tzaraath\ft , traditionally translated as \fqa leprosy\ft , were used for various skin diseases; here and throughout verses 3–46.\f* \rb he must be brought|וְהוּבָא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb or|א֛וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֥ד\rb* \rb of his sons|מִבָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb who is a priest|הַכֹּהֲנִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to examine|וְרָאָ֣ה\rb* \rb the infection|הַנֶּ֣גַע\rb* \rb on his skin|בְּעֽוֹר־\rb*\rb |הַ֠בָּשָׂר\rb*, \rb and if the hair|וְשֵׂעָ֨ר\rb* \rb in the infection|בַּנֶּ֜גַע\rb* \rb has turned|הָפַ֣ךְ׀\rb* \rb white|לָבָ֗ן\rb* \rb and the sore|הַנֶּ֙גַע֙\rb* \rb appears|וּמַרְאֵ֤ה\rb* \rb to be deeper|עָמֹק֙\rb* \rb than the skin|מֵע֣וֹר\rb*\rb |בְּשָׂר֔וֹ\rb*,\rb |נֶ֥גַע\rb* \rb it|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb is a skin disease|צָרַ֖עַת\rb*. \rb After the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb examines him|וְרָאָ֥הוּ\rb*, \rb he must pronounce him unclean|וְטִמֵּ֥א\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb If, however|וְאִם־\rb*, \rb the spot|בַּהֶרֶת֩\rb* \rb on his skin|בְּע֣וֹר\rb*\rb |בְּשָׂר֗וֹ\rb* \rb is white|לְבָנָ֨ה\rb*\rb |הִ֜וא\rb* \rb and does not|אֵין־\rb* \rb appear|מַרְאֶ֣הָ\rb* \rb to be deeper|וְעָמֹק֙\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb the skin|הָע֔וֹר\rb*, \rb and the hair in it|וּשְׂעָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb turned|הָפַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb white|לָבָ֑ן\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall isolate|וְהִסְגִּ֧יר\rb* \rb the infected person|הַנֶּ֖גַע\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb On the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִי֒\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֮\rb* \rb is to reexamine him|וְרָאָ֣הוּ\rb*, \rb and if|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb he sees|בְּעֵינָ֔יו\rb* \rb that the infection|הַנֶּ֙גַע֙\rb* \rb is unchanged|עָמַ֣ד\rb* \rb and has not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb spread|פָשָׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֖גַע\rb* \rb on the skin|בָּע֑וֹר\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb must isolate him|וְהִסְגִּיר֧וֹ\rb* \rb for another|שֵׁנִֽית׃\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb*. \v 6 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb will examine him|וְרָאָה֩\rb* \rb again|שֵׁנִית֒\rb* \rb on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִי֮\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb and if|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb the sore|הַנֶּ֔גַע\rb* \rb has faded|כֵּהָ֣ה\rb* \rb and has not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb spread|פָשָׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֖גַע\rb* \rb on the skin|בָּע֑וֹר\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb shall pronounce him clean|וְטִהֲר֤וֹ\rb*; \rb it|הִ֔יא\rb* \rb is a rash|מִסְפַּ֣חַת\rb*. \rb The person must wash|וְכִבֶּ֥ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb and be clean|וְטָהֵֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the rash|הַמִּסְפַּ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb spreads further|פָּשֹׂ֨ה\rb*\rb |תִפְשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb on his skin|בָּע֔וֹר\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֧י\rb* \rb he has shown himself|הֵרָאֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb for his cleansing|לְטָהֳרָת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb he must present himself|וְנִרְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb again|שֵׁנִ֖ית\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb will reexamine him|וְרָאָה֙\rb*, \rb and if|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb the rash|הַמִּסְפַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb has spread|פָּשְׂתָ֥ה\rb* \rb on the skin|בָּע֑וֹר\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb must pronounce him unclean|וְטִמְּא֥וֹ\rb*; \rb it|הִֽוא׃פ\rb* \rb is a skin disease|צָרַ֥עַת\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb When|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb anyone|בְּאָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb develops|תִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb a skin disease|נֶ֣גַע\rb*, \rb he must be brought|וְהוּבָ֖א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb will examine him|וְרָאָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and if|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb there is a white|לְבָנָה֙\rb* \rb swelling|שְׂאֵת־\rb* \rb on the skin|בָּע֔וֹר\rb* \rb that|וְהִ֕יא\rb* \rb has turned|הָפְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb the hair|שֵׂעָ֣ר\rb* \rb white|לָבָ֑ן\rb*,\rb |וּמִֽחְיַ֛ת\rb* \rb and there is raw|חַ֖י\rb* \rb flesh|בָּשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb in the swelling|בַּשְׂאֵֽת׃\rb*, \v 11 \rb it|הִוא֙\rb* \rb is a chronic|נוֹשֶׁ֤נֶת\rb* \rb skin disease|צָרַ֨עַת\rb*\rb |בְּע֣וֹר\rb*\rb |בְּשָׂר֔וֹ\rb* \rb and the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb must pronounce him unclean|וְטִמְּא֖וֹ\rb*. \rb He need not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb isolate him|יַסְגִּרֶ֔נּוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is unclean|טָמֵ֖א\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the skin disease|הַצָּרַ֙עַת֙\rb* \rb breaks out|פָּר֨וֹחַ\rb*\rb |תִּפְרַ֤ח\rb* \rb all over his skin|בָּע֔וֹר\rb* \rb so that it|הַצָּרַ֗עַת\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb covers|וְכִסְּתָ֣ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the skin|ע֣וֹר\rb* \rb of the infected person|הַנֶּ֔גַע\rb* \rb from head|מֵרֹאשׁ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb foot|רַגְלָ֑יו\rb*,\rb |לְכָל־\rb* \rb as far as the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb* \rb can see|מַרְאֵ֖ה\rb*,\rb |עֵינֵ֥י\rb* \v 13 \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb shall examine him|וְרָאָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and if|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb the disease|הַצָּרַ֙עַת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has covered|כִסְּתָ֤ה\rb* \rb his entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb body|בְּשָׂר֔וֹ\rb*, \rb he is to pronounce the infected person|הַנָּ֑גַע\rb* \rb clean|וְטִהַ֖ר\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Since it has all turned|הָפַ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |כֻּלּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb white|לָבָ֖ן\rb*, \rb he|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is clean|טָה֥וֹר\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb But whenever|וּבְי֨וֹם\rb* \rb raw|חַ֖י\rb* \rb flesh|בָּשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb appears|הֵרָא֥וֹת\rb* \rb on someone|בּ֛וֹ\rb*, \rb he will be unclean|יִטְמָֽא׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb When the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sees|וְרָאָ֧ה\rb* \rb the raw|הַחַ֖י\rb* \rb flesh|הַבָּשָׂ֥ר\rb*, \rb he must pronounce him unclean|וְטִמְּא֑וֹ\rb*. \rb The raw|הַחַ֛י\rb* \rb flesh|הַבָּשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb is unclean|טָמֵ֥א\rb*; \rb it|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is a skin disease|צָרַ֥עַת\rb*.\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb* \v 16 \rb But|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb if|כִ֥י\rb* \rb the raw|הַחַ֖י\rb* \rb flesh|הַבָּשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb changes|יָשׁ֛וּב\rb* \rb and turns|וְנֶהְפַּ֣ךְ\rb* \rb white|לְלָבָ֑ן\rb*, \rb he must go|וּבָ֖א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb will reexamine him|וְרָאָ֙הוּ֙\rb*, \rb and if|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb the infection|הַנֶּ֖גַע\rb* \rb has turned|נֶהְפַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb white|לְלָבָ֑ן\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to pronounce the infected person|הַנֶּ֖גַע\rb* \rb clean|וְטִהַ֧ר\rb*; \rb then he|הֽוּא׃פ\rb* \rb is clean|טָה֥וֹר\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a boil|שְׁחִ֑ין\rb* \rb appears|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb on someone’s skin|בְעֹר֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וּבָשָׂ֕ר\rb* \rb and it heals|וְנִרְפָּֽא׃\rb*, \v 19 \rb and a white|לְבָנָ֔ה\rb* \rb swelling|שְׂאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb a reddish-white|לְבָנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲדַמְדָּ֑מֶת\rb* \rb spot|בַהֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb develops|וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb where|בִּמְק֤וֹם\rb* \rb the boil was|הַשְּׁחִין֙\rb*, \rb he must present himself|וְנִרְאָ֖ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb shall examine it|וְרָאָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and if|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb it appears|מַרְאֶ֙הָ֙\rb* \rb to be beneath|שָׁפָ֣ל\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the skin|הָע֔וֹר\rb* \rb and the hair in it|וּשְׂעָרָ֖הּ\rb* \rb has turned|הָפַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb white|לָבָ֑ן\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb*\rb |נֶֽגַע־\rb* \rb shall pronounce him unclean|וְטִמְּא֧וֹ\rb*; \rb it|הִ֖וא\rb* \rb is a diseased infection|צָרַ֥עַת\rb* \rb that has broken out|פָּרָֽחָה׃\rb* \rb in the boil|בַּשְּׁחִ֥ין\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb But when|וְאִ֣ם׀\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb examines it|יִרְאֶ֣נָּה\rb*, \rb if|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb there is no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb white|לָבָ֔ן\rb* \rb hair|שֵׂעָ֣ר\rb* \rb in it|בָּהּ֙\rb*, \rb and it is not|אֵינֶ֛נָּה\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb beneath|וּשְׁפָלָ֥ה\rb* \rb the skin|הָע֖וֹר\rb*\rb |וְהִ֣יא\rb* \rb and has faded|כֵהָ֑ה\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb shall isolate him|וְהִסְגִּיר֥וֹ\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb it spreads any further|פָּשֹׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |תִפְשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb on the skin|בָּע֑וֹר\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb must pronounce him unclean|וְטִמֵּ֧א\rb*; \rb it|הִֽוא׃\rb* \rb is an infection|נֶ֥גַע\rb*. \v 23 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the spot|הַבַּהֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb remains|תַּעֲמֹ֤ד\rb* \rb unchanged|תַּחְתֶּ֜יהָ\rb* \rb and does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb spread|פָשָׂ֔תָה\rb*, \rb it|הִ֑וא\rb* \rb is only the scar|צָרֶ֥בֶת\rb* \rb from the boil|הַשְּׁחִ֖ין\rb*, \rb and the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃ס\rb* \rb shall pronounce him clean|וְטִהֲר֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb there is|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a burn|מִכְוַת־\rb*\rb |אֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb on someone’s skin|בְעֹר֖וֹ\rb*\rb |בָשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb and the raw|מִֽחְיַ֣ת\rb* \rb area of the burn|הַמִּכְוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |בַּהֶ֛רֶת\rb* \rb becomes|וְֽהָיְתָ֞ה\rb* \rb reddish-white|לְבָנָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֲדַמְדֶּ֖מֶת\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb white|לְבָנָֽה׃\rb*, \v 25 \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֡ן\rb* \rb must examine it|וְרָאָ֣ה\rb*.\rb |אֹתָ֣הּ\rb* \rb If|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb the hair|שֵׂעָ֨ר\rb* \rb in the spot|בַּבַּהֶ֗רֶת\rb* \rb has turned|נֶהְפַּךְ֩\rb* \rb white|לָבָ֜ן\rb* \rb and the spot appears|וּמַרְאֶ֙הָ֙\rb* \rb to be deeper|עָמֹ֣ק\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb the skin|הָע֔וֹר\rb*, \rb it|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb is a disease|צָרַ֣עַת\rb* \rb that has broken out|פָּרָ֑חָה\rb* \rb in the burn|בַּמִּכְוָ֖ה\rb*. \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*\rb |נֶ֥גַע\rb* \rb must pronounce him unclean|וְטִמֵּ֤א\rb*;\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb it|הִֽוא׃\rb* \rb is a diseased infection|צָרַ֖עַת\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb But if|וְאִ֣ם׀\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb examines it|יִרְאֶ֣נָּה\rb* \rb and there is|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb white|לָבָ֔ן\rb* \rb hair|שֵׂעָ֣ר\rb* \rb in the spot|בַּבֶּהֶ֙רֶת֙\rb*, \rb and it is not|אֵינֶ֛נָּה\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb beneath|וּשְׁפָלָ֥ה\rb* \rb the skin|הָע֖וֹר\rb*\rb |וְהִ֣וא\rb* \rb but has faded|כֵהָ֑ה\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb shall isolate him|וְהִסְגִּיר֥וֹ\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb On the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֑י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb is to reexamine him|וְרָאָ֥הוּ\rb*, \rb and if|אִם־\rb* \rb it has spread further|פָּשֹׂ֤ה\rb*\rb |תִפְשֶׂה֙\rb* \rb on the skin|בָּע֔וֹר\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb*\rb |נֶ֥גַע\rb* \rb must pronounce him unclean|וְטִמֵּ֤א\rb*; \rb it|הִֽוא׃\rb* \rb is a diseased infection|צָרַ֖עַת\rb*. \v 28 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the spot|הַבַּהֶ֜רֶת\rb* \rb is unchanged|תַעֲמֹ֨ד\rb*\rb |תַּחְתֶּיהָ֩\rb* \rb and has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb spread|פָשְׂתָ֤ה\rb* \rb on the skin|בָעוֹר֙\rb* \rb but has faded|כֵהָ֔ה\rb*, \rb it|וְהִ֣וא\rb* \rb is a swelling|שְׂאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb from the burn|הַמִּכְוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb is to pronounce him clean|וְטִֽהֲרוֹ֙\rb*; \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it|הִ֑וא\rb* \rb is only the scar|צָרֶ֥בֶת\rb* \rb from the burn|הַמִּכְוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |הִֽוא׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|וְאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb has|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb an infection|נָ֑גַע\rb* \rb on the head|בְּרֹ֖אשׁ\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb chin|בְזָקָֽן׃\rb*, \v 30 \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall examine|וְרָאָ֨ה\rb* \rb the infection|הַנֶּ֗גַע\rb*, \rb and if|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb it appears|מַרְאֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb to be deeper|עָמֹ֣ק\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb the skin|הָע֔וֹר\rb* \rb and|וּב֛וֹ\rb* \rb the hair in it|שֵׂעָ֥ר\rb* \rb is yellow|צָהֹ֖ב\rb* \rb and thin|דָּ֑ק\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb must pronounce him unclean|וְטִמֵּ֨א\rb*\rb |אֹת֤וֹ\rb*; \rb it|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is a scaly outbreak|נֶ֣תֶק\rb*, \rb an infectious disease|צָרַ֧עַת\rb* \rb of the head|הָרֹ֛אשׁ\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb chin|הַזָּקָ֖ן\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb But if|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb examines|יִרְאֶ֨ה\rb* \rb the scaly|הַנֶּ֗תֶק\rb* \rb infection|נֶ֣גַע\rb* \rb and|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb it does not|אֵין־\rb* \rb appear|מַרְאֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb to be deeper|עָמֹ֣ק\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb the skin|הָע֔וֹר\rb*, \rb and there is no|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb black|שָׁחֹ֖ר\rb* \rb hair|וְשֵׂעָ֥ר\rb* \rb in it|בּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall isolate|וְהִסְגִּ֧יר\rb* \rb the infected person|הַנֶּ֖תֶק\rb*\rb |נֶ֥גַע\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb On the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִי֒\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to reexamine|וְרָאָ֨ה\rb* \rb the infection|הַנֶּגַע֮\rb*, \rb and if|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb the scaly outbreak|הַנֶּ֔תֶק\rb* \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb spread|פָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb and there is|הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb yellow|צָהֹ֑ב\rb* \rb hair|שֵׂעָ֣ר\rb* \rb in it|ב֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and it|הַנֶּ֔תֶק\rb* \rb does not|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb appear|וּמַרְאֵ֣ה\rb* \rb to be deeper|עָמֹ֖ק\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb the skin|הָעֽוֹר׃\rb*, \v 33 \rb then the person must shave himself|וְהִ֨תְגַּלָּ֔ח\rb* \rb except for|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |יְגַלֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb the scaly area|הַנֶּ֖תֶק\rb*. \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֧ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall isolate|וְהִסְגִּ֨יר\rb* \rb him|הַנֶּ֛תֶק\rb* \rb for another|שֵׁנִֽית׃\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb*. \v 34 \rb On the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֗י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall examine|וְרָאָה֩\rb* \rb the scaly outbreak|הַנֶּ֜תֶק\rb*, \rb and if|וְ֠הִנֵּה\rb* \rb it|הַנֶּ֙תֶק֙\rb* \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb spread|פָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb on the skin|בָּע֔וֹר\rb* \rb and does not|אֵינֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb appear to be|וּמַרְאֵ֕הוּ\rb* \rb deeper|עָמֹ֖ק\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb the skin|הָע֑וֹר\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb is to pronounce him clean|וְטִהַ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb*. \rb He must wash|וְכִבֶּ֥ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֖יו\rb*, \rb and he will be clean|וְטָהֵֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 35 \rb If, however|וְאִם־\rb*, \rb the scaly outbreak|הַנֶּ֖תֶק\rb* \rb spreads further|פָּשֹׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |יִפְשֶׂ֛ה\rb* \rb on the skin|בָּע֑וֹר\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb his cleansing|טָהֳרָתֽוֹ׃\rb*, \v 36 \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb is to examine him|וְרָאָ֙הוּ֙\rb*, \rb and if|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb the scaly outbreak|הַנֶּ֖תֶק\rb* \rb has spread|פָּשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb on the skin|בָּע֑וֹר\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb need not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb look for|יְבַקֵּ֧ר\rb* \rb yellow|הַצָּהֹ֖ב\rb* \rb hair|לַשֵּׂעָ֥ר\rb*; \rb the person|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is unclean|טָמֵ֥א\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb If, however|וְאִם־\rb*, \rb in his sight|בְּעֵינָיו֩\rb* \rb the scaly outbreak|הַנֶּ֜תֶק\rb* \rb is unchanged|עָמַ֨ד\rb* \rb and black|שָׁחֹ֧ר\rb* \rb hair|וְשֵׂעָ֨ר\rb* \rb has grown|צָֽמַח־\rb* \rb in it|בּ֛וֹ\rb*, \rb then it|הַנֶּ֖תֶק\rb* \rb has healed|נִרְפָּ֥א\rb*. \rb He|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb is clean|טָה֣וֹר\rb*, \rb and the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃ס\rb* \rb is to pronounce him clean|וְטִהֲר֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 38 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a man|וְאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb a woman|אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb has white|לְבָנֹֽת׃\rb* \rb spots|בֶּהָרֹ֑ת\rb*\rb |בֶּהָרֹ֖ת\rb* \rb on the skin|בְעוֹר־\rb*\rb |בְּשָׂרָ֖ם\rb*, \v 39 \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb shall examine them|וְרָאָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and if|וְהִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb the spots|בֶּהָרֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |בְעוֹר־\rb*\rb |בְּשָׂרָ֛ם\rb* \rb are dull|כֵּה֣וֹת\rb* \rb white|לְבָנֹ֑ת\rb*, \rb it|ה֛וּא\rb* \rb is a harmless rash|בֹּ֥הַק\rb* \rb that has broken out|פָּרַ֥ח\rb* \rb on the skin|בָּע֖וֹר\rb*; \rb the person|הֽוּא׃ס\rb* \rb is clean|טָה֥וֹר\rb*.
\p \v 40 \rb Now if|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb a man|וְאִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb loses his hair|יִמָּרֵ֖ט\rb*\rb |רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb and is bald|קֵרֵ֥חַ\rb*, \rb he is still|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb clean|טָה֥וֹר\rb*. \v 41 \rb Or if|וְאִם֙\rb*\rb |רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb* \rb his hairline|מִפְּאַ֣ת\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb recedes|יִמָּרֵ֖ט\rb* \rb and he|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is bald on his forehead|גִּבֵּ֥חַ\rb*, \rb he is still|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb clean|טָה֥וֹר\rb*. \v 42 \rb But if|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb there is|יִהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb a reddish-white|לָבָ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֲדַמְדָּ֑ם\rb* \rb sore|נֶ֖גַע\rb* \rb on the bald head|בַקָּרַ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb forehead|בַגַּבַּ֔חַת\rb*, \rb it|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb is an infectious disease|צָרַ֤עַת\rb* \rb breaking out|פֹּרַ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb on it|בְּקָרַחְתּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |א֥וֹ\rb*\rb |בְגַבַּחְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 43 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb is to examine him|וְרָאָ֨ה\rb*,\rb |אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb and if|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the swelling|שְׂאֵת־\rb* \rb of the infection|הַנֶּ֙גַע֙\rb* \rb on his bald head|בְּקָרַחְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb forehead|בְגַבַּחְתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb is reddish-white|לְבָנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲדַמְדֶּ֔מֶת\rb* \rb like|כְּמַרְאֵ֥ה\rb* \rb a skin|ע֥וֹר\rb* \rb disease|צָרַ֖עַת\rb*\rb |בָּשָֽׂר׃\rb*, \v 44 \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb is diseased|צָר֥וּעַ\rb*; \rb he|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is unclean|טָמֵ֣א\rb*.\rb |ה֑וּא\rb* \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb must pronounce him unclean|טַמֵּ֧א\rb*\rb |יְטַמְּאֶ֛נּוּ\rb* \rb because of the infection|נִגְעֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb on his head|בְּרֹאשׁ֥וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 45 \rb A diseased person|הַנֶּ֗גַע\rb*\rb |וְהַצָּר֜וּעַ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |בּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb must wear torn clothes|בְּגָדָ֞יו\rb*\rb |יִהְי֤וּ\rb*\rb |פְרֻמִים֙\rb* \rb and let his hair|וְרֹאשׁוֹ֙\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb hang loose|פָר֔וּעַ\rb*,\f + \fr 13:45 \ft Or \fqa uncover his head\f*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and he must cover|יַעְטֶ֑ה\rb* \rb his mouth|שָׂפָ֖ם\rb* \rb and cry out|יִקְרָֽא׃\rb*, ‘\rb Unclean|וְטָמֵ֥א׀\rb*, \rb unclean|טָמֵ֖א\rb*!’ \v 46 \rb As|כָּל־\rb* \rb long as|יְמֵ֞י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb he has the infection|הַנֶּ֥גַע\rb*, \rb he remains|יִטְמָ֖א\rb*\rb |בּ֛וֹ\rb*\rb |ה֑וּא\rb*\rb |בָּדָ֣ד\rb* \rb unclean|טָמֵ֣א\rb*. \rb He must live alone|יֵשֵׁ֔ב\rb* \rb in a place|מוֹשָׁבֽוֹ׃ס\rb* \rb outside|מִח֥וּץ\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb*.
\s1 Laws about Mildew
\p \v 47 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb any fabric|וְהַבֶּ֕גֶד\rb* \rb is|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |ב֖וֹ\rb* \rb contaminated|נֶ֣גַע\rb* \rb with mildew|צָרָ֑עַת\rb*\f + \fr 13:47 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa tzaraath\ft , traditionally translated as \fqa leprosy \ft regarding skin diseases, are translated as \fqa mildew \ft regarding blemishes on garments, utensils, or buildings; here and throughout the remainder of this chapter.\f*— \rb any wool|צֶ֔מֶר\rb* \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb*\rb |בְּבֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb linen|פִּשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb* \rb garment|בְּבֶ֣גֶד\rb*, \v 48 \rb |א֤וֹ\rb* \rb any weave|בִֽשְׁתִי֙\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb knit|בְעֵ֔רֶב\rb* \rb of linen|לַפִּשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb or wool|וְלַצָּ֑מֶר\rb*, \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb any article of leather|בְע֔וֹר\rb*\rb |א֖וֹ\rb*\rb |בְּכָל־\rb*\rb |מְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb*\rb |עֽוֹר׃\rb*— \v 49 \rb and if the mark|הַנֶּ֜גַע\rb* \rb in the fabric|בַּבֶּגֶד֩\rb*, \rb leather|בָע֜וֹר\rb*,\rb |אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb weave|בַשְּׁתִ֤י\rb*,\rb |אוֹ־\rb* \rb knit|בָעֵ֙רֶב֙\rb*, \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb*\rb |בְכָל־\rb* \rb leather|ע֔וֹר\rb* \rb article|כְּלִי־\rb* \rb is|וְהָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb green|יְרַקְרַ֣ק׀\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb red|אֲדַמְדָּ֗ם\rb*, \rb then it is|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb contaminated|נֶ֥גַע\rb* \rb with mildew|צָרַ֖עַת\rb* \rb and must be shown|וְהָרְאָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 50 \rb And the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to examine|וְרָאָ֥ה\rb* \rb the mildew|הַנָּ֑גַע\rb* \rb and isolate|וְהִסְגִּ֥יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the contaminated fabric|הַנֶּ֖גַע\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 51 \rb On the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֗י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the priest shall reexamine|וְרָאָ֨ה\rb* \rb it|אֶת־\rb*, \rb and if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the mildew|הַנֶּ֜גַע\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֙גַע֙\rb* \rb has spread|פָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb in the fabric|בַּ֠בֶּגֶד\rb*, \rb weave|בַשְּׁתִ֤י\rb*,\rb |אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb knit|בָעֵ֙רֶב֙\rb*,\rb |א֣וֹ\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb leather|בָע֔וֹר\rb*, \rb then regardless of|לְכֹ֛ל\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb it|הָע֖וֹר\rb* \rb is used|יֵעָשֶׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |לִמְלָאכָ֑ה\rb*, \rb it|הַנֶּ֖גַע\rb* \rb is a harmful|מַמְאֶ֛רֶת\rb* \rb mildew|צָרַ֧עַת\rb*; \rb the article|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is unclean|טָמֵ֥א\rb*. \v 52 \rb He is to burn|וְשָׂרַ֨ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the fabric|הַבֶּ֜גֶד\rb*, \rb weave|הַשְּׁתִ֣י׀\rb*,\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb knit|הָעֵ֗רֶב\rb*, \rb whether|א֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |ב֖וֹ\rb* \rb the contaminated item is|הַנָּ֑גַע\rb* \rb wool|בַּצֶּ֙מֶר֙\rb* \rb or linen|בַפִּשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |א֚וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb leather|הָע֔וֹר\rb*\rb |כְּלִ֣י\rb*. \rb Since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the mildew|צָרַ֤עַת\rb* \rb is harmful|מַמְאֶ֙רֶת֙\rb*, \rb the article|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb must be burned up|בָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |תִּשָּׂרֵֽף׃\rb*.
\p \v 53 \rb But when|וְאִם֮\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֒\rb* \rb reexamines it|יִרְאֶ֣ה\rb*, \rb if|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb the mildew|הַנֶּ֔גַע\rb* \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb spread|פָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb in the fabric|בַּבֶּ֕גֶד\rb*, \rb weave|בַשְּׁתִ֖י\rb*,\rb |א֥וֹ\rb* \rb knit|בָעֵ֑רֶב\rb*,\rb |א֖וֹ\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb*\rb |בְּכָל־\rb* \rb leather|עֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb article|כְּלִי־\rb*, \v 54 \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb is to order|וְצִוָּה֙\rb* \rb the|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |בּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb contaminated article|הַנָּ֑גַע\rb* \rb to be washed|וְכִ֨בְּס֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb and isolated|וְהִסְגִּיר֥וֹ\rb* \rb for another|שֵׁנִֽית׃\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַת־\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb*. \v 55 \rb After|אַחֲרֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb it has been washed|הֻכַּבֵּ֣ס\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb is to reexamine it|וְרָאָ֨ה\rb*, \rb and if|וְ֠הִנֵּה\rb* \rb the mildewed|הַנֶּ֗גַע\rb* \rb article|הַנֶּ֤גַע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb changed|הָפַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb in appearance|עֵינוֹ֙\rb*, \rb it|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is unclean|טָמֵ֣א\rb*. \rb Even though the mildew|וְהַנֶּ֣גַע\rb* \rb has not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb spread|פָשָׂ֔ה\rb*, \rb you must burn it|תִּשְׂרְפֶ֑נּוּ\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb*, \rb whether|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb the rot is|פְּחֶ֣תֶת\rb* \rb on the front|בְגַבַּחְתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb back|בְּקָרַחְתּ֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 56 \rb If|וְאִם֮\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֒\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb examines it|רָאָ֣ה\rb* \rb and the mildew|הַנֶּ֔גַע\rb* \rb has faded|כֵּהָ֣ה\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb it has been washed|הֻכַּבֵּ֣ס\rb*,\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb he must cut the contaminated section out|וְקָרַ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the fabric|הַבֶּ֙גֶד֙\rb*, \rb leather|הָע֔וֹר\rb*,\rb |א֣וֹ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb weave|הַשְּׁתִ֖י\rb*,\rb |א֥וֹ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb knit|הָעֵֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 57 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb it reappears|תֵּרָאֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |ע֜וֹד\rb* \rb in the fabric|בַּ֠בֶּגֶד\rb*, \rb weave|בַשְּׁתִ֤י\rb*, \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb knit|בָעֵ֙רֶב֙\rb*,\rb |א֣וֹ\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb on any|בְכָל־\rb* \rb leather|ע֔וֹר\rb* \rb article|כְּלִי־\rb*, \rb it|הִ֑וא\rb* \rb is spreading|פֹּרַ֖חַת\rb*. \rb You must burn|תִּשְׂרְפֶ֔נּוּ\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |בּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb the contaminated|הַנָּֽגַע׃\rb* \rb article|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*.
\p \v 58 \rb If the mildew|הַנָּ֑גַע\rb* \rb disappears|וְסָ֥ר\rb* \rb from|מֵהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb the fabric|וְהַבֶּ֡גֶד\rb*, \rb weave|הַשְּׁתִ֨י\rb*, \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb knit|הָעֵ֜רֶב\rb*,\rb |אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb any|כָל־\rb* \rb leather|הָעוֹר֙\rb* \rb article|כְּלִ֤י\rb* \rb after|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb washing|תְּכַבֵּ֔ס\rb*, \rb then it is to be washed|וְכֻבַּ֥ס\rb* \rb again|שֵׁנִ֖ית\rb*, \rb and it will be clean|וְטָהֵֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 59 \rb This|זֹ֠את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַ֨ת\rb* \rb concerning a mildew|צָרַ֜עַת\rb* \rb contamination|נֶֽגַע־\rb* \rb in wool|הַצֶּ֣מֶר׀\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb linen|הַפִּשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb fabric|בֶּ֥גֶד\rb*,\rb |א֤וֹ\rb* \rb weave|הַשְּׁתִי֙\rb*, \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb knit|הָעֵ֔רֶב\rb*, \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb leather|ע֑וֹר\rb* \rb article|כְּלִי־\rb*, \rb for pronouncing it clean|לְטַהֲר֖וֹ\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb unclean|לְטַמְּאֽוֹ׃פ\rb*.”
\c 14
\s1 Cleansing from Skin Diseases
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb This|זֹ֤את\rb* \rb is|תִּֽהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb the law|תּוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb for the one afflicted with a skin disease|הַמְּצֹרָ֔ע\rb*\f + \fr 14:2 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa tzaraath\ft , traditionally translated as \fqa leprosy\ft , were used for various skin diseases; also in verses 3, 7, 32, 54, and 57.\f* \rb on the day|בְּי֖וֹם\rb* \rb of his cleansing|טָהֳרָת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb when he is brought|וְהוּבָ֖א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb is to go|וְיָצָא֙\rb* \rb outside|מִח֖וּץ\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb* \rb to examine him|וְרָאָה֙\rb*,\rb |הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb and if|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb the skin disease|הַצָּרַ֖עַת\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the afflicted person|הַצָּרֽוּעַ׃\rb* \rb has healed|נִרְפָּ֥א\rb*\rb |נֶֽגַע־\rb*, \v 4 \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb shall order|וְצִוָּה֙\rb* \rb that two|שְׁתֵּֽי־\rb* \rb live|חַיּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb clean|טְהֹר֑וֹת\rb* \rb birds|צִפֳּרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb cedar|אֶ֔רֶז\rb* \rb wood|וְעֵ֣ץ\rb*, \rb scarlet yarn|וּשְׁנִ֥י\rb*\rb |תוֹלַ֖עַת\rb*, \rb and hyssop|וְאֵזֹֽב׃\rb* \rb be brought|וְלָקַ֧ח\rb* \rb for the one to be cleansed|לַמִּטַּהֵ֛ר\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb shall command|וְצִוָּה֙\rb* \rb that one|הָאֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb of the birds|הַצִּפּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb be slaughtered|וְשָׁחַ֖ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb fresh|חַיִּֽים׃\rb* \rb water|מַ֥יִם\rb*\f + \fr 14:5 \ft Or \fqa flowing water \ft or \fqa living water\ft ; here and in verses 6, 50, 51, and 52\f* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb a clay|חֶ֖רֶשׂ\rb* \rb pot|כְּלִי־\rb*. \v 6 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb And he is to take|יִקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the live|הַֽחַיָּה֙\rb* \rb bird|הַצִּפֹּ֤ר\rb* \rb together with the cedar|הָאֶ֛רֶז\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb wood|עֵ֥ץ\rb*, \rb scarlet yarn|שְׁנִ֥י\rb*\rb |הַתּוֹלַ֖עַת\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and hyssop|הָאֵזֹ֑ב\rb*, \rb and dip|וְטָבַ֨ל\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb them|וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb into the blood|בְּדַם֙\rb*\rb |הַצִּפֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb of the bird|הַצִּפֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb that was slaughtered|הַשְּׁחֻטָ֔ה\rb* \rb over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the fresh|הַֽחַיִּֽים׃\rb* \rb water|הַמַּ֥יִם\rb*. \v 7 \rb Seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb he shall sprinkle|וְהִזָּ֗ה\rb*\rb |עַ֧ל\rb* \rb the one to be cleansed|הַמִּטַּהֵ֛ר\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the skin disease|הַצָּרַ֖עַת\rb*. \rb Then he shall pronounce him clean|וְטִ֣הֲר֔וֹ\rb* \rb and release|וְשִׁלַּ֛ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the live|הַֽחַיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb bird|הַצִּפֹּ֥ר\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb the open|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb field|הַשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb The one being cleansed|הַמִּטַּהֵ֨ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb must wash|וְכִבֶּס֩\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֜יו\rb*, \rb shave off|וְגִלַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his hair|שְׂעָר֗וֹ\rb*, \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֤ץ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמַּ֙יִם֙\rb*; \rb then he will be ceremonially clean|וְטָהֵ֔ר\rb*. \rb Afterward|וְאַחַ֖ר\rb*, \rb he may enter|יָב֣וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb*, \rb but he must remain|וְיָשַׁ֛ב\rb* \rb outside|מִח֥וּץ\rb* \rb his tent|לְאָהֳל֖וֹ\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb On the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֜י\rb* \rb day|בַיּ֨וֹם\rb*\rb |וְהָיָה֩\rb* \rb he must shave off|יְגַלַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his hair|שְׂעָר֗וֹ\rb* —\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֤וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his beard|זְקָנוֹ֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb his eyebrows|גַּבֹּ֣ת\rb*\rb |עֵינָ֔יו\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the rest|כָּל־\rb* \rb of his hair|שְׂעָר֖וֹ\rb*.\rb |יְגַלֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb He must wash|וְכִבֶּ֣ס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֗יו\rb* \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֧ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb himself|בְּשָׂר֛וֹ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמַּ֖יִם\rb*, \rb and he will be clean|וְטָהֵֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb On the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֗י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb he is to bring|יִקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb unblemished|תְּמִימִ֔ים\rb* \rb male lambs|כְבָשִׂים֙\rb*, \rb an|אַחַ֛ת\rb* \rb unblemished|תְּמִימָ֑ה\rb* \rb ewe lamb|וְכַבְשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb a year old|בַּת־\rb*\rb |שְׁנָתָ֖הּ\rb*, \rb a grain offering|מִנְחָה֙\rb* \rb of three-tenths of an ephah|וּשְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֹנִ֗ים\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֤לֶת\rb*\f + \fr 14:10 \fqa Three-tenths of an ephah \ft is approximately 6 dry quarts or 6.6 liters (probably about 7.6 pounds or 3.5 kilograms of flour).\f* \rb mixed|בְּלוּלָ֣ה\rb* \rb with olive oil|בַשֶּׁ֔מֶן\rb*, \rb and one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb log|וְלֹ֥ג\rb* \rb of olive oil|שָֽׁמֶן׃\rb*.\f + \fr 14:10 \ft Or \fqa one log of oil\ft ; that is, approximately 0.33 quarts or 0.31 liters; also in verses 12, 15, 21, and 24\f* \v 11 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb who performs the cleansing|הַֽמְטַהֵ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb shall present|וְהֶעֱמִ֞יד\rb* \rb the one|הָאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to be cleansed|הַמִּטַּהֵ֖ר\rb*, \rb together with these offerings|וְאֹתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to take|וְלָקַ֨ח\rb* \rb one|הָאֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb of the male lambs|הַכֶּ֣בֶשׂ\rb* \rb and present|וְהִקְרִ֥יב\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb it as a guilt offering|לְאָשָׁ֖ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb along with the log|לֹ֣ג\rb* \rb of olive oil|הַשָּׁ֑מֶן\rb*; \rb and he must wave|וְהֵנִ֥יף\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb as a wave offering|תְּנוּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Then he is to slaughter|וְשָׁחַ֣ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the lamb|הַכֶּ֗בֶשׂ\rb* \rb in the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb area|בִּמְק֣וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּ֛את\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb are slaughtered|יִשְׁחַ֧ט\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Like|כִּ֡י\rb* \rb the sin offering|כַּ֠חַטָּאת\rb*, \rb the guilt offering|הָאָשָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb belongs to the priest|לַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*; \rb it|הוּא֙\rb* \rb is most|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb holy|קָֽדָשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵן֮\rb* \rb is to take|וְלָקַ֣ח\rb* \rb some of the blood|מִדַּ֣ם\rb* \rb from the guilt offering|הָאָשָׁם֒\rb* \rb and put it|וְנָתַן֙\rb*\rb |הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the right|הַיְמָנִ֑ית\rb* \rb earlobe|אֹ֥זֶן\rb*\rb |תְּנ֛וּךְ\rb* \rb of the one to be cleansed|הַמִּטַּהֵ֖ר\rb*, \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the thumb|בֹּ֤הֶן\rb* \rb of his right|הַיְמָנִ֔ית\rb* \rb hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb*, \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the big toe|בֹּ֥הֶן\rb* \rb of his right|הַיְמָנִֽית׃\rb* \rb foot|רַגְל֖וֹ\rb*. \v 15 \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb shall take|וְלָקַ֥ח\rb* \rb some of the log|מִלֹּ֣ג\rb* \rb of olive oil|הַשָּׁ֑מֶן\rb*, \rb pour|וְיָצַ֛ק\rb* \rb it into|עַל־\rb* \rb his|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb left|הַשְּׂמָאלִֽית׃\rb* \rb palm|כַּ֥ף\rb*, \v 16 \rb |הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb dip|וְטָבַ֤ל\rb* \rb his right|הַיְמָנִ֔ית\rb* \rb forefinger|אֶצְבָּע֣וֹ\rb* \rb into|מִן־\rb* \rb the oil|הַשֶּׁ֕מֶן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb his left|הַשְּׂמָאלִ֑ית\rb* \rb palm|כַּפּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and sprinkle|וְהִזָּ֨ה\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb the oil|הַשֶּׁ֧מֶן\rb* \rb with his finger|בְּאֶצְבָּע֛וֹ\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb And the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb is to put|יִתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb some|עַל־\rb* \rb of the oil|הַשֶּׁ֜מֶן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb remaining|וּמִיֶּ֨תֶר\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb his palm|כַּפּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb on the right|הַיְמָנִ֔ית\rb* \rb earlobe|אֹ֤זֶן\rb*\rb |תְּנ֞וּךְ\rb* \rb of the one to be cleansed|הַמִּטַּהֵר֙\rb*, \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the thumb|בֹּ֤הֶן\rb* \rb of his right|הַיְמָנִ֔ית\rb* \rb hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb*, \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the big toe|בֹּ֥הֶן\rb* \rb of his right|הַיְמָנִ֑ית\rb* \rb foot|רַגְל֖וֹ\rb*, \rb on top of|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the blood|דַּ֥ם\rb* \rb of the guilt offering|הָאָשָֽׁם׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb The rest|וְהַנּוֹתָ֗ר\rb* \rb of the oil|בַּשֶּׁ֙מֶן֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb in his|עַל־\rb* \rb palm|כַּ֣ף\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb is to put|יִתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the one to be cleansed|הַמִּטַּהֵ֑ר\rb*,\rb |הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb to make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb for him|עָלָ֛יו\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to sacrifice|וְעָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb the sin offering|הַ֣חַטָּ֔את\rb* \rb and make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֕ר\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the one to be cleansed|הַמִּטַּהֵ֖ר\rb* \rb from his uncleanness|מִטֻּמְאָת֑וֹ\rb*. \rb After that|וְאַחַ֖ר\rb*, \rb the priest shall slaughter|יִשְׁחַ֥ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָֽה׃\rb* \v 20 \rb |הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and offer|וְהֶעֱלָ֧ה\rb* \rb it|הָעֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb on the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חָה\rb*, \rb with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the grain offering|הַמִּנְחָ֖ה\rb*,\rb |הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb to make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb for him|עָלָ֛יו\rb*, \rb and he will be clean|וְטָהֵֽר׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb If, however|וְאִם־\rb*, \rb the person|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb is poor|דַּ֣ל\rb* \rb and cannot|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb afford these offerings|יָדוֹ֮\rb*\rb |מַשֶּׂגֶת֒\rb*, \rb he is to take|וְ֠לָקַח\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb male lamb|כֶּ֣בֶשׂ\rb* \rb as a guilt offering|אָשָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb to be waved|לִתְנוּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb to make atonement|לְכַפֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb for him|עָלָ֑יו\rb*, \rb along with a tenth of an ephah|וְעִשָּׂר֨וֹן\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֜לֶת\rb*\f + \fr 14:21 \fqa A tenth of an ephah \ft is approximately 2 dry quarts or 2.2 liters (probably about 2.6 pounds or 1.2 kilograms of flour).\f*\rb |אֶחָ֨ד\rb* \rb mixed|בָּל֥וּל\rb* \rb with olive oil|בַּשֶּׁ֛מֶן\rb* \rb for a grain offering|לְמִנְחָ֖ה\rb*, \rb a log|וְלֹ֥ג\rb* \rb of olive oil|שָֽׁמֶן׃\rb*, \v 22 \rb and two|וּשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb turtledoves|תֹרִ֗ים\rb* \rb or|א֤וֹ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb young|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb pigeons|יוֹנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb whichever|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he can afford|תַּשִּׂ֖יג\rb*\rb |יָד֑וֹ\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb to be|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb a sin offering|חַטָּ֔את\rb* \rb and the other|וְהָאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb a burnt offering|עֹלָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb On the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֛י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֧וֹם\rb* \rb he is to bring|וְהֵבִ֨יא\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb for his cleansing|לְטָהֳרָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֥תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹֽהֶל־\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֖ד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall take|וְלָקַ֧ח\rb* \rb the lamb|כֶּ֥בֶשׂ\rb* \rb for the guilt offering|הָאָשָׁ֖ם\rb*, \rb along with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the log|לֹ֣ג\rb* \rb of olive oil|הַשָּׁ֑מֶן\rb*, \rb and wave|וְהֵנִ֨יף\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֧ם\rb*\rb |הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb as a wave offering|תְּנוּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
