\s1 Signs of Home Contamination
\p \v 33 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 34 “\rb When|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you enter|תָבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb am giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb as your possession|לַאֲחֻזָּ֑ה\rb*, \rb and I put|וְנָתַתִּי֙\rb* \rb a contamination|נֶ֣גַע\rb* \rb of mildew|צָרַ֔עַת\rb*\f + \fr 14:34 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa tzaraath\ft , traditionally translated as \fqa leprosy \ft regarding skin diseases, are translated as \fqa mildew \ft regarding blemishes on garments, utensils, or buildings; here and throughout the remainder of this chapter.\f* \rb into a house|בְּבֵ֖ית\rb* \rb in that land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲחֻזַּתְכֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 35 \rb the owner|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb of the house|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb shall come|וּבָא֙\rb* \rb and tell|וְהִגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb the priest|לַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb Something like mildew|כְּנֶ֕גַע\rb* \rb has appeared|נִרְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb in my|לִ֖י\rb* \rb house|בַּבָּֽיִת׃\rb*.’
\p \v 36 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb must order that|וְצִוָּ֨ה\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֗יִת\rb* \rb be cleared|וּפִנּ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|בְּטֶ֨רֶם\rb* \rb he|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb enters it|יָבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to examine|לִרְא֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the mildew|הַנֶּ֔גַע\rb*, \rb so that nothing|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the house|בַּבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb will become unclean|יִטְמָ֖א\rb*. \rb After|וְאַ֥חַר\rb* \rb this|כֵּ֛ן\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb shall go in|יָבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to inspect|לִרְא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb He is to examine|וְרָאָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|הַנֶּ֗גַע\rb*, \rb and if|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the mildew|הַנֶּ֙גַע֙\rb* \rb on the walls|בְּקִירֹ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb consists of green|יְרַקְרַקֹּ֔ת\rb* \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb* \rb red|אֲדַמְדַּמֹּ֑ת\rb* \rb depressions|שְׁקַֽעֲרוּרֹת֙\rb* \rb that appear|וּמַרְאֵיהֶ֥ן\rb* \rb to be beneath|שָׁפָ֖ל\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the surface of the wall|הַקִּֽיר׃\rb*, \v 38 \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb shall go outside|וְיָצָ֧א\rb*\rb |הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the doorway|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb of the house|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb and close|וְהִסְגִּ֥יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it up|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 39 \rb On the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֑י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb is to return|וְשָׁ֥ב\rb* \rb and inspect the house|וְרָאָ֕ה\rb*. \rb If|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb the mildew|הַנֶּ֖גַע\rb* \rb has spread|פָּשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb on the walls|בְּקִירֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*, \v 40 \rb he|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb must order|וְצִוָּה֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |בָּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb the contaminated|הַנָּ֑גַע\rb* \rb stones|הָ֣אֲבָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb be pulled out|וְחִלְּצוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and thrown|וְהִשְׁלִ֤יכוּ\rb*\rb |אֶתְהֶן֙\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb an unclean|טָמֵֽא׃\rb* \rb place|מָק֖וֹם\rb* \rb outside|מִח֣וּץ\rb* \rb the city|לָעִ֔יר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*. \v 41 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he shall have the inside|הַבַּ֛יִת\rb* \rb of the house|מִבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb scraped|יַקְצִ֥עַ\rb* \rb completely|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb and the plaster|הֶֽעָפָר֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb is scraped off|הִקְצ֔וּ\rb* \rb dumped|וְשָׁפְכ֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb an unclean|טָמֵֽא׃\rb* \rb place|מָק֖וֹם\rb* \rb outside|מִח֣וּץ\rb* \rb the city|לָעִ֔יר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*.
