\p \v 43 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the mildew|הַנֶּ֙גַע֙\rb*\rb |וּפָרַ֣ח\rb* \rb reappears|יָשׁ֤וּב\rb* \rb in the house|בַּבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb after|אַחַ֖ר\rb* \rb the stones|הָאֲבָנִ֑ים\rb* \rb have been torn out|חִלֵּ֣ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and|וְאַחֲרֵ֛י\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*\rb |וְאַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb has been scraped|הִקְצ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and replastered|הִטּֽוֹחַ׃\rb*, \v 44 \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb must come|וּבָא֙\rb* \rb and inspect it|וְרָאָ֕ה\rb*.
\p \rb If|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb the mildew|הַנֶּ֖גַע\rb* \rb has spread|פָּשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb in the house|בַּבָּ֑יִת\rb*, \rb it is|הִ֛וא\rb* \rb a destructive|מַמְאֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb mildew|צָרַ֨עַת\rb*; \rb the house|בַּבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb is unclean|טָמֵ֥א\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb*. \v 45 \rb It|הַבַּ֗יִת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb must be torn down|וְנָתַ֣ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with its stones|אֲבָנָיו֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb its timbers|עֵצָ֔יו\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb plaster|עֲפַ֣ר\rb*, \rb and taken|וְהוֹצִיא֙\rb* \rb outside|מִח֣וּץ\rb* \rb the city|לָעִ֔יר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb an unclean|טָמֵֽא׃\rb* \rb place|מָק֖וֹם\rb*. \v 46 \rb Anyone who enters|וְהַבָּא֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb during any|כָּל־\rb* \rb of the days|יְמֵ֖י\rb* \rb that it is closed up|הִסְגִּ֣יר\rb*\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb will be unclean|יִטְמָ֖א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 47 \rb And anyone who sleeps|וְהַשֹּׁכֵ֣ב\rb* \rb in the house|בַּבַּ֔יִת\rb*\rb |יְכַבֵּ֖ס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |בְּגָדָ֑יו\rb* \rb or eats|וְהָאֹכֵ֣ל\rb* \rb in it|בַּבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb must wash|יְכַבֵּ֖ס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָֽיו׃\rb*.
\s1 Cleansing a Home
\p \v 48 \rb If, however|וְאִם־\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb comes|בֹּ֨א\rb*\rb |יָבֹ֜א\rb* \rb and inspects it|וְרָאָה֙\rb*, \rb and|וְ֠הִנֵּה\rb* \rb the mildew|הַנֶּ֙גַע֙\rb* \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb spread|פָשָׂ֤ה\rb*\rb |בַּבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the house|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb has been replastered|הִטֹּ֣חַ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall pronounce the house|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb clean|וְטִהַ֤ר\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the mildew|הַנָּֽגַע׃\rb* \rb is gone|נִרְפָּ֖א\rb*.
\p \v 49 \rb He is to take|וְלָקַ֛ח\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb birds|צִפֳּרִ֑ים\rb*, \rb cedar|אֶ֔רֶז\rb* \rb wood|וְעֵ֣ץ\rb*, \rb scarlet yarn|וּשְׁנִ֥י\rb*\rb |תוֹלַ֖עַת\rb*, \rb and hyssop|וְאֵזֹֽב׃\rb* \rb to purify|לְחַטֵּ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*; \v 50 \rb and he shall slaughter|וְשָׁחַ֖ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb one|הָאֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb of the birds|הַצִּפֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb over|אֶל־\rb* \rb fresh|חַיִּֽים׃\rb* \rb water|מַ֥יִם\rb* \rb in a clay|חֶ֖רֶשׂ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb pot|כְּלִי־\rb*.
\p \v 51 \rb Then he shall take|וְלָקַ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the cedar|הָ֠אֶרֶז\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb wood|עֵֽץ־\rb*, \rb the hyssop|הָ֨אֵזֹ֜ב\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb the scarlet yarn|שְׁנִ֣י\rb*\rb |הַתּוֹלַ֗עַת\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֮\rb* \rb and the live|הַֽחַיָּה֒\rb* \rb bird|הַצִּפֹּ֣ר\rb*, \rb dip|וְטָבַ֣ל\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb in the blood|בְּדַם֙\rb* \rb of the slaughtered|הַשְּׁחוּטָ֔ה\rb* \rb bird|הַצִּפֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb and the fresh|הַֽחַיִּ֑ים\rb* \rb water|וּבַמַּ֖יִם\rb*, \rb and sprinkle|וְהִזָּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 52 \rb And he shall cleanse|וְחִטֵּ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb with the bird’s|הַצִּפּ֔וֹר\rb* \rb blood|בְּדַם֙\rb*, \rb the fresh|הַֽחַיִּ֑ים\rb* \rb water|וּבַמַּ֖יִם\rb*, \rb the live|הַחַיָּ֗ה\rb* \rb bird|וּבַצִּפֹּ֣ר\rb*, \rb the cedar|הָאֶ֛רֶז\rb* \rb wood|וּבְעֵ֥ץ\rb*, \rb the hyssop|וּבָאֵזֹ֖ב\rb*, \rb and the scarlet yarn|וּבִשְׁנִ֥י\rb*\rb |הַתּוֹלָֽעַת׃\rb*.
\p \v 53 \rb Finally, he is to release|וְשִׁלַּ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the live|הַֽחַיָּ֛ה\rb* \rb bird|הַצִּפֹּ֧ר\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the open|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb fields|הַשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb* \rb outside|מִח֥וּץ\rb* \rb the city|לָעִ֖יר\rb*.\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb In this way he will make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*, \rb and it will be clean|וְטָהֵֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 54 \rb This|זֹ֖את\rb* \rb is the law|הַתּוֹרָ֑ה\rb* \rb for any|לְכָל־\rb* \rb infectious skin disease|הַצָּרַ֖עַת\rb*\rb |נֶ֥גַע\rb*, \rb for a scaly outbreak|וְלַנָּֽתֶק׃\rb*, \v 55 \rb for mildew|וּלְצָרַ֥עַת\rb* \rb in clothing|הַבֶּ֖גֶד\rb* \rb or in a house|וְלַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*, \v 56 \rb and for a swelling|וְלַשְׂאֵ֥ת\rb*, \rb rash|וְלַסַּפַּ֖חַת\rb*, \rb or spot|וְלַבֶּהָֽרֶת׃\rb*, \v 57 \rb to determine|לְהוֹרֹ֕ת\rb* \rb when|בְּי֥וֹם\rb*\rb |וּבְי֣וֹם\rb* \rb something is clean|הַטָּהֹ֑ר\rb* \rb or unclean|הַטָּמֵ֖א\rb*. \rb This|זֹ֥את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַ֖ת\rb* \rb regarding skin diseases and mildew|הַצָּרָֽעַת׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 14:57 \ft The Hebrew translated here as \fqa skin diseases and mildew \ft is one singular term; see the footnotes for verses 2 and 34.\f*”
\c 15
\s1 The Uncleanness of Men
\p \v 1 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Say|דַּבְּרוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb*,\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb* ‘\rb When|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb any|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb man|אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb has|יִהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb a bodily|מִבְּשָׂר֔וֹ\rb* \rb discharge|זָ֣ב\rb*, \rb the discharge|זוֹב֖וֹ\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is unclean|טָמֵ֥א\rb*. \v 3 \rb This|וְזֹ֛את\rb* \rb uncleanness|טֻמְאָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb is|תִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb from his discharge|בְּזוֹב֑וֹ\rb*, \rb whether his body|בְּשָׂר֞וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb allows|רָ֣ר\rb* \rb the discharge to flow|זוֹב֗וֹ\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb blocks it|הֶחְתִּ֤ים\rb*\rb |בְּשָׂרוֹ֙\rb*. \rb So his discharge|מִזּוֹב֔וֹ\rb* \rb will bring about|הִֽוא׃\rb* \rb uncleanness|טֻמְאָת֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Any|כָּל־\rb* \rb bed|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֗ב\rb* \rb on|עָלָ֛יו\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the man with the discharge|הַזָּ֖ב\rb* \rb lies|יִשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb will be unclean|יִטְמָ֑א\rb*, \rb and any|וְכָֽל־\rb* \rb furniture|הַכְּלִ֛י\rb* \rb on|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he sits|יֵשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb will be unclean|יִטְמָֽא׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Anyone|וְאִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb touches|יִגַּ֖ע\rb* \rb his bed|בְּמִשְׁכָּב֑וֹ\rb* \rb must wash|יְכַבֵּ֧ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֛יו\rb* \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמַּ֖יִם\rb*, \rb and he will be unclean|וְטָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb Whoever sits|וְהַיֹּשֵׁב֙\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb furniture|הַכְּלִ֔י\rb* \rb on|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the man with the discharge|הַזָּ֑ב\rb* \rb was sitting|יֵשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb must wash|יְכַבֵּ֧ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֛יו\rb* \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמַּ֖יִם\rb*, \rb and he will be unclean|וְטָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Whoever touches|וְהַנֹּגֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb the body|בִּבְשַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of the man with a discharge|הַזָּ֑ב\rb* \rb must wash|יְכַבֵּ֧ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֛יו\rb* \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמַּ֖יִם\rb*, \rb and he will be unclean|וְטָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb the man with the discharge|הַזָּ֖ב\rb* \rb spits|יָרֹ֛ק\rb* \rb on one who is clean|בַּטָּה֑וֹר\rb*, \rb that person must wash|וְכִבֶּ֧ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֛יו\rb* \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמַּ֖יִם\rb*, \rb and he will be unclean|וְטָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb saddle|הַמֶּרְכָּ֗ב\rb* \rb on|עָלָ֛יו\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the man with the discharge|הַזָּ֖ב\rb* \rb rides|יִרְכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb will be unclean|יִטְמָֽא׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb Whoever|וְכָל־\rb* \rb touches|הַנֹּגֵ֗עַ\rb* \rb anything|בְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb under him|תַחְתָּ֔יו\rb* \rb will be unclean|יִטְמָ֖א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָ֑רֶב\rb*, \rb and whoever carries|וְהַנּוֹשֵׂ֣א\rb* \rb such things|אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb must wash|יְכַבֵּ֧ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֛יו\rb* \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמַּ֖יִם\rb*, \rb and he will be unclean|וְטָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb If the man with the discharge|הַזָּ֔ב\rb* \rb touches|יִגַּע־\rb* \rb anyone|וְכֹ֨ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb without|לֹא־\rb* \rb first rinsing|שָׁטַ֣ף\rb* \rb his hands|וְיָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb with water|בַּמָּ֑יִם\rb*, \rb the one who was touched must wash|וְכִבֶּ֧ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֛יו\rb* \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמַּ֖יִם\rb*, \rb and he will be unclean|וְטָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb Any clay|חֶ֛רֶשׂ\rb* \rb pot|וּכְלִי־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the man with the discharge|הַזָּ֖ב\rb* \rb touches|יִגַּע־\rb* \rb must be broken|יִשָּׁבֵ֑ר\rb*, \rb and any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb wooden|עֵ֔ץ\rb* \rb utensil|כְּלִי־\rb* \rb must be rinsed|יִשָּׁטֵ֖ף\rb* \rb with water|בַּמָּֽיִם׃\rb*.
\s1 The Cleansing of Men
\p \v 13 \rb When|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb the man|הַזָּב֙\rb* \rb has been cleansed|יִטְהַ֤ר\rb* \rb from his discharge|מִזּוֹב֔וֹ\rb*, \rb he must count off|וְסָ֨פַר\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֛ים\rb* \rb for his|ל֜וֹ\rb* \rb cleansing|לְטָהֳרָת֖וֹ\rb*, \rb wash|וְכִבֶּ֣ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֧ץ\rb* \rb himself|בְּשָׂר֛וֹ\rb* \rb in fresh|חַיִּ֖ים\rb* \rb water|בְּמַ֥יִם\rb*,\f + \fr 15:13 \ft Or \fqa flowing water \ft or \fqa living water\f* \rb and he shall be clean|וְטָהֵֽר׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb On the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֗י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb he is to take|יִֽקַּֽח־\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb turtledoves|תֹרִ֔ים\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb young|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb pigeons|יוֹנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb come|וּבָ֣א׀\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֙תַח֙\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb*, \rb and give them|וּנְתָנָ֖ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb is to sacrifice|וְעָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb as a sin offering|חַטָּ֔את\rb* \rb and the other|וְהָאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb as a burnt offering|עֹלָ֑ה\rb*. \rb In this way the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb will make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb for|עָלָ֧יו\rb* \rb the man before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb because of his discharge|מִזּוֹבֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |תֵצֵ֥א\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb a man|וְאִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb has an emission|שִׁכְבַת־\rb* \rb of semen|זָ֑רַע\rb*, \rb he must bathe|וְרָחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb his whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb body|בְּשָׂר֖וֹ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמַּ֛יִם\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and he will be unclean|וְטָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb clothing|בֶּ֣גֶד\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb or leather|ע֔וֹר\rb* \rb on|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb there is|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb an emission|שִׁכְבַת־\rb* \rb of semen|זָ֑רַע\rb* \rb must be washed|וְכֻבַּ֥ס\rb* \rb with water|בַּמַּ֖יִם\rb*, \rb and it will remain unclean|וְטָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃פ\rb*. \v 18 \rb If a man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb lies with|יִשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb a woman|וְאִשָּׁ֕ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb and there is an emission|שִׁכְבַת־\rb* \rb of semen|זָ֑רַע\rb*, \rb both must bathe|וְרָחֲצ֣וּ\rb* \rb with water|בַמַּ֔יִם\rb*, \rb and they will remain unclean|וְטָמְא֖וּ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*.
\s1 The Uncleanness of Women
\p \v 19 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a woman|וְאִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb has|תִהְיֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |זֹבָ֖הּ\rb* \rb a discharge|זָבָ֔ה\rb* \rb consisting|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb of blood|דָּ֛ם\rb* \rb from her body|בִּבְשָׂרָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb she will be|תִּהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb unclean due to her menstruation|בְנִדָּתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֤ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִים֙\rb*, \rb and anyone|וְכָל־\rb* \rb who touches|הַנֹּגֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb her|בָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb will be unclean|יִטְמָ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb Anything|וְכֹל֩\rb* \rb on|עָלָ֛יו\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb she lies|תִּשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb*\rb |וְכֹ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb or sits|תֵּשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb during her menstruation|בְּנִדָּתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb will be unclean|יִטְמָ֑א\rb*,\rb |עָלָ֖יו\rb*\rb |יִטְמָֽא׃\rb* \v 21 \rb and anyone|וְכָל־\rb* \rb who touches|הַנֹּגֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb her bed|בְּמִשְׁכָּבָ֑הּ\rb* \rb must wash|יְכַבֵּ֧ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֛יו\rb* \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמַּ֖יִם\rb*, \rb and he will be unclean|וְטָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Whoever|וְכָל־\rb* \rb touches|הַנֹּגֵ֔עַ\rb* \rb any|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb furniture|כְּלִ֖י\rb* \rb on|עָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb she was sitting|תֵּשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb must wash|יְכַבֵּ֧ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֛יו\rb* \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמַּ֖יִם\rb*, \rb and he will be unclean|וְטָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb And whether|וְאִ֨ם\rb* \rb it is|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb a bed|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֜ב\rb* \rb or|א֧וֹ\rb* \rb furniture|הַכְּלִ֛י\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb she|הִ֥וא\rb* \rb was sitting|יֹשֶֽׁבֶת־\rb*\rb |עָלָ֖יו\rb*, \rb whoever touches|בְּנָגְעוֹ־\rb* \rb it|ב֑וֹ\rb* \rb will be unclean|יִטְמָ֖א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb If|וְאִ֡ם\rb* \rb a man|אִ֜ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֗הּ\rb* \rb lies with|שָׁכֹב֩\rb* \rb her|יִשְׁכַּ֨ב\rb* \rb and her menstrual flow|נִדָּתָהּ֙\rb* \rb touches|וּתְהִ֤י\rb* \rb him|עָלָ֔יו\rb*, \rb he will be unclean|וְטָמֵ֖א\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb bed|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֛ב\rb* \rb on|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he lies|יִשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb will become unclean|יִטְמָֽא׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a woman|וְאִשָּׁ֡ה\rb* \rb has a discharge|יָזוּב֩\rb*\rb |ז֨וֹב\rb* \rb of her blood|דָּמָ֜הּ\rb* \rb for many|רַבִּ֗ים\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb at a time|עֶת־\rb* \rb other than|בְּלֹא֙\rb* \rb her menstrual period|נִדָּתָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb if|כִֽי־\rb* \rb it continues|תָז֖וּב\rb* \rb beyond|עַל־\rb* \rb her period|נִדָּתָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb she|הִֽוא׃\rb* \rb will be|תִּהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb unclean|טְמֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֞י\rb* \rb of her unclean|טֻמְאָתָ֗הּ\rb* \rb discharge|ז֣וֹב\rb*, \rb just as she is during the days|כִּימֵ֧י\rb* \rb of her menstruation|נִדָּתָ֛הּ\rb*. \v 26 \rb Any|כָּל־\rb* \rb bed|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֞ב\rb* \rb on|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb she lies|תִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb or any|כָּל־\rb* \rb furniture|הַכְּלִי֙\rb* \rb on|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb she sits|תֵּשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb during the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of her discharge|זוֹבָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |יִֽהְיֶה־\rb*\rb |נִדָּתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb unclean|טָמֵ֣א\rb*\rb |וְכָֽל־\rb*, \rb like her bed|כְּמִשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb during her menstrual period|כְּטֻמְאַ֖ת\rb*\rb |נִדָּתָֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb Anyone|וְכָל־\rb* \rb who touches|הַנּוֹגֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb these things|בָּ֖ם\rb* \rb will be unclean|יִטְמָ֑א\rb*; \rb he must wash|וְכִבֶּ֧ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֛יו\rb* \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמַּ֖יִם\rb*, \rb and he will be unclean|וְטָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*.
\s1 The Cleansing of Women
\p \v 28 \rb When|וְאִֽם־\rb* \rb a woman is cleansed|טָהֲרָ֖ה\rb* \rb of her discharge|מִזּוֹבָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb she must count off|וְסָ֥פְרָה\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and after that|וְאַחַ֥ר\rb* \rb she will be ceremonially clean|תִּטְהָֽר׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb On the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֗י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb she is to take|תִּֽקַּֽח־\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb turtledoves|תֹרִ֔ים\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb young|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb pigeons|יוֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and bring|וְהֵבִיאָ֤ה\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to sacrifice|וְעָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb one|הָאֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb as a sin offering|חַטָּ֔את\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the other|הָאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb as a burnt offering|עֹלָ֑ה\rb*. \rb In this way the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb will make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb for her|עָלֶ֤יהָ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb for her unclean|טֻמְאָתָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb discharge|מִזּ֖וֹב\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb You must keep|וְהִזַּרְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the children|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Israel separate|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb from their uncleanness|מִטֻּמְאָתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb so that they do not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb die|יָמֻ֙תוּ֙\rb*\rb |בְּטֻמְאָתָ֔ם\rb* \rb by defiling|בְּטַמְּאָ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My tabernacle|מִשְׁכָּנִ֖י\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is among them|בְּתוֹכָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb This|זֹ֥את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of him who has a discharge|הַזָּ֑ב\rb*, \rb of the man who|וַאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb has|תֵּצֵ֥א\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֛נּוּ\rb* \rb an emission|שִׁכְבַת־\rb* \rb of semen|זֶ֖רַע\rb* \rb whereby|בָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb he is unclean|לְטָמְאָה־\rb*, \v 33 \rb of a woman|וְהַדָּוָה֙\rb* \rb in her menstrual period|בְּנִדָּתָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb of any male|לַזָּכָ֖ר\rb* \rb or female|וְלַנְּקֵבָ֑ה\rb* \rb who has a discharge|וְהַזָּב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |זוֹב֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and of a man|וּלְאִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb lies|יִשְׁכַּ֖ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb an unclean woman|טְמֵאָֽה׃פ\rb*.’”
\c 16
\s1 The Day of Atonement
\p \v 1 \rb Now the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the death|מ֔וֹת\rb* \rb of two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֑ן\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb when they approached|בְּקָרְבָתָ֥ם\rb* \rb the presence|לִפְנֵי־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וַיָּמֻֽתוּ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb*: “\rb Tell|דַּבֵּר֮\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִיךָ֒\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb to enter|יָבֹ֤א\rb* \rb freely|בְכָל־\rb*\rb |עֵת֙\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Most Holy Place|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb*\f + \fr 16:2 \ft Or \fqa the Holy Place\ft ; also in verses 16, 17, 20, 23, and 27\f* \rb behind|מִבֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb the veil|לַפָּרֹ֑כֶת\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb front|פְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the mercy seat|הַכַּפֹּ֜רֶת\rb*\f + \fr 16:2 \ft Or \fqa atonement cover\ft ; here and throughout this chapter\f*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָרֹן֙\rb*, \rb or else|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb he will die|יָמ֔וּת\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I appear|אֵרָאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb in the cloud|בֶּֽעָנָ֔ן\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb the mercy seat|הַכַּפֹּֽרֶת׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb This is how|בְּזֹ֛את\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb is to enter|יָבֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Holy Place|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb*: \rb with a young bull|בְּפַ֧ר\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בָּקָ֛ר\rb* \rb for a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֖את\rb* \rb and a ram|וְאַ֥יִל\rb* \rb for a burnt offering|לְעֹלָֽה׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb He is to wear|יִלְבָּ֗שׁ\rb* \rb the sacred|קֹ֜דֶשׁ\rb* \rb linen|בַּ֨ד\rb* \rb tunic|כְּתֹֽנֶת־\rb*, \rb with linen|בַד֮\rb* \rb undergarments|וּמִֽכְנְסֵי־\rb*\rb |יִהְי֣וּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |בְּשָׂרוֹ֒\rb*. \rb He must tie|יַחְגֹּ֔ר\rb* \rb a linen|בַּד֙\rb* \rb sash|וּבְאַבְנֵ֥ט\rb* \rb around him|בַּ֖ד\rb* \rb and put on the linen|יִצְנֹ֑ף\rb* \rb turban|וּבְמִצְנֶ֥פֶת\rb*. \rb These|הֵ֔ם\rb* \rb are holy|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb garments|בִּגְדֵי־\rb*, \rb and he must bathe|וְרָחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb himself|בְּשָׂר֖וֹ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמַּ֛יִם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before he wears them|וּלְבֵשָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb And|וּמֵאֵ֗ת\rb* \rb he shall take|יִקַּ֛ח\rb* \rb from the congregation|עֲדַת֙\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb male goats|שְׂעִירֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עִזִּ֖ים\rb* \rb for a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֑את\rb* \rb and one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb ram|וְאַ֥יִל\rb* \rb for a burnt offering|לְעֹלָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to present|וְהִקְרִ֧יב\rb* \rb the bull|פַּ֥ר\rb* \rb for his sin offering|הַחַטָּ֖את\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb and make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb for|בַּעֲד֖וֹ\rb* \rb himself|וּבְעַ֥ד\rb* \rb and his household|בֵּיתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Then he shall take|וְלָקַ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb goats|הַשְּׂעִירִ֑ם\rb* \rb and present|וְהֶעֱמִ֤יד\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb After Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֛ן\rb* \rb casts|וְנָתַ֧ן\rb* \rb lots|גּוֹרָל֑וֹת\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb goats|הַשְּׂעִירִ֖ם\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָד֙\rb*\rb |גּוֹרָ֤ל\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְגוֹרָ֥ל\rb* \rb and the other|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb for the scapegoat|לַעֲזָאזֵֽל׃\rb*,\f + \fr 16:8 \ft Literally \fqa the other to Azazel\ft ; similarly twice in verse 10 and once in verse 26\f* \v 9 \rb he|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall present|וְהִקְרִ֤יב\rb* \rb the goat|הַשָּׂעִ֔יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb chosen|עָלָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָלָ֛יו\rb* \rb by lot|הַגּוֹרָ֖ל\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and sacrifice|וְעָשָׂ֖הוּ\rb* \rb it as a sin offering|חַטָּֽאת׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb But the goat|וְהַשָּׂעִ֗יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb chosen|עָלָ֨ה\rb* \rb by|עָלָ֤יו\rb* \rb lot|הַגּוֹרָל֙\rb* \rb as the scapegoat|לַעֲזָאזֵ֔ל\rb* \rb shall be presented|יָֽעֳמַד־\rb* \rb alive|חַ֛י\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb to make atonement|לְכַפֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb by sending|לְשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb it into the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּֽרָה׃\rb* \rb as the scapegoat|לַעֲזָאזֵ֖ל\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb When Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb presents|וְהִקְרִ֨יב\rb* \rb the bull|פַּ֤ר\rb* \rb for his sin offering|הַֽחַטָּאת֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb and makes atonement|וְכִפֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb for himself|בַּֽעֲד֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וּבְעַ֣ד\rb* \rb and his household|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb*, \rb he is to slaughter|וְשָׁחַ֛ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bull|פַּ֥ר\rb* \rb for his own sin offering|הַֽחַטָּ֖את\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*. \v 12 \rb Then he must take|וְלָקַ֣ח\rb* \rb a censer|הַ֠מַּחְתָּה\rb* \rb full|מְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb of burning|אֵ֞שׁ\rb* \rb coals|גַּֽחֲלֵי־\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֤ל\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb before|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and two handfuls|וּמְלֹ֣א\rb*\rb |חָפְנָ֔יו\rb* \rb of finely ground|דַּקָּ֑ה\rb* \rb fragrant|סַמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb incense|קְטֹ֥רֶת\rb*, \rb and take them|וְהֵבִ֖יא\rb* \rb inside|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb the veil|לַפָּרֹֽכֶת׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb He is to put|וְנָתַ֧ן\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the incense|הַקְּטֹ֛רֶת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the fire|הָאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and the cloud|עֲנַ֣ן\rb* \rb of incense|הַקְּטֹ֗רֶת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will cover|וְכִסָּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the mercy seat|הַכַּפֹּ֛רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb the Testimony|הָעֵד֖וּת\rb*,\f + \fr 16:13 \fqa The Testimony \ft refers to the stone tablets in the ark of the covenant inscribed with the Ten Commandments.\f* \rb so that he will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb die|יָמֽוּת׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb And he is to take|וְלָקַח֙\rb* \rb some of the bull’s|הַפָּ֔ר\rb* \rb blood|מִדַּ֣ם\rb* \rb and sprinkle|וְהִזָּ֧ה\rb* \rb it with his finger|בְאֶצְבָּע֛וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the east|קֵ֑דְמָה\rb* \rb side|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the mercy seat|הַכַּפֹּ֖רֶת\rb*; \rb then he shall sprinkle|יַזֶּ֧ה\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb it|הַדָּ֖ם\rb* \rb with his finger|בְּאֶצְבָּעֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb seven|שֶֽׁבַע־\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֛ים\rb* \rb before|וְלִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the mercy seat|הַכַּפֹּ֗רֶת\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Aaron shall then slaughter|וְשָׁחַ֞ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the goat|שְׂעִ֤יר\rb* \rb for the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּאת֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb for the people|לָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and bring|וְהֵבִיא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its blood|דָּמ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb behind|מִבֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb the veil|לַפָּרֹ֑כֶת\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and with its blood|דָּמ֗וֹ\rb* \rb he must do|וְעָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb he did|עָשָׂה֙\rb* \rb with the bull’s|הַפָּ֔ר\rb* \rb blood|לְדַ֣ם\rb*: \rb He is to sprinkle|וְהִזָּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb it against|עַל־\rb* \rb the mercy seat|הַכַּפֹּ֖רֶת\rb* \rb and in front|וְלִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of it|הַכַּפֹּֽרֶת׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb So he shall make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the Most Holy Place|הַקֹּ֗דֶשׁ\rb* \rb because of the impurities|מִטֻּמְאֹת֙\rb* \rb and rebellious acts|וּמִפִּשְׁעֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb in regard to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb their sins|חַטֹּאתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb He is to do|יַעֲשֶׂה֙\rb* \rb the same|וְכֵ֤ן\rb* \rb for the Tent|לְאֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb* \rb which abides|הַשֹּׁכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb among them|אִתָּ֔ם\rb* \rb in the midst|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb of their impurities|טֻמְאֹתָֽם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb No|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb one|אָדָ֞ם\rb* \rb may be|יִהְיֶ֣ה׀\rb* \rb in the Tent|בְּאֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֗ד\rb* \rb from the time Aaron goes in|בְּבֹא֛וֹ\rb* \rb to make atonement|לְכַפֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb in the Most Holy Place|בַּקֹּ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb he leaves|צֵאת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb after he has made atonement|וְכִפֶּ֤ר\rb* \rb for himself|בַּעֲדוֹ֙\rb*,\rb |וּבְעַ֣ד\rb* \rb his household|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*,\rb |וּבְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb and the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֥ל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Then he shall go out|וְיָצָ֗א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֛חַ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is before|לִפְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb for it|עָלָ֑יו\rb*. \rb He is to take|וְלָקַ֞ח\rb* \rb some of the bull’s|הַפָּר֙\rb* \rb blood|מִדַּ֤ם\rb* \rb and some of the goat’s|הַשָּׂעִ֔יר\rb* \rb blood|וּמִדַּ֣ם\rb* \rb and put it|וְנָתַ֛ן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb all|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb the horns|קַרְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*. \v 19 \rb He is to sprinkle|וְהִזָּ֨ה\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֛ם\rb* \rb on it|עָלָ֧יו\rb* \rb with his finger|בְּאֶצְבָּע֖וֹ\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb to cleanse it|וְטִהֲר֣וֹ\rb* \rb and consecrate it|וְקִדְּשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb from the uncleanness|מִטֻּמְאֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb When Aaron has finished|וְכִלָּה֙\rb* \rb purifying|מִכַּפֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Most Holy Place|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֖ד\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb*, \rb he is to bring forward|וְהִקְרִ֖יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the live|הֶחָֽי׃\rb* \rb goat|הַשָּׂעִ֥יר\rb*. \v 21 \rb Then he|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to lay|וְסָמַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb both|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb hands|יָדוֹ\rb* \rb on|עַ֨ל\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the live|הַחַי֒\rb* \rb goat|הַשָּׂעִיר֮\rb* \rb and confess|וְהִתְוַדָּ֣ה\rb* \rb over|עָלָ֗יו\rb* \rb it|אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the iniquities|עֲוֺנֹת֙\rb* \rb and rebellious acts|פִּשְׁעֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb in regard to|לְכָל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their sins|חַטֹּאתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb He is to put|וְנָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the goat’s|הַשָּׂעִ֔יר\rb* \rb head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb and send it away|וְשִׁלַּ֛ח\rb* \rb into the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּֽרָה׃\rb* \rb by the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of a man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb appointed for the task|עִתִּ֖י\rb*. \v 22 \rb The goat|הַשָּׂעִ֥יר\rb* \rb will carry|וְנָשָׂ֨א\rb* \rb on|עָלָ֛יו\rb* \rb itself|אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their iniquities|עֲוֺנֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb a solitary|גְּזֵרָ֑ה\rb* \rb place|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb*, \rb and the man will release|וְשִׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it|הַשָּׂעִ֖יר\rb* \rb into the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*.
