\p \v 29 \rb This is to be|וְהָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb a permanent|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb statute|לְחֻקַּ֣ת\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb*: \rb On the tenth|בֶּֽעָשׂ֨וֹר\rb* \rb day|לַחֹ֜דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the seventh|הַ֠שְּׁבִיעִי\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb you shall humble|תְּעַנּ֣וּ\rb* \rb yourselves|נַפְשֹֽׁתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*\f + \fr 16:29 \ft Or \fqa afflict your souls \ft or \fqa deny yourselves\ft ; also in verse 31\f* \rb and not do|תַעֲשׂ֔וּ\rb* \rb any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb work|מְלָאכָה֙\rb* — \rb whether the native|הָֽאֶזְרָ֔ח\rb* \rb or the foreigner|וְהַגֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb who resides|הַגָּ֥ר\rb* \rb among you|בְּתוֹכְכֶֽם׃\rb* — \v 30 \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb on this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb day|בַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb atonement will be made|יְכַפֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb for you|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to cleanse|לְטַהֵ֣ר\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and you will be clean|תִּטְהָֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb from all|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb your sins|חַטֹּ֣אתֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*. \v 31 \rb It|הִיא֙\rb* \rb is a Sabbath|שַׁבַּ֨ת\rb* \rb of complete rest|שַׁבָּת֥וֹן\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb that you may humble|וְעִנִּיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb yourselves|נַפְשֹׁתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*; \rb it is a permanent|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb statute|חֻקַּ֖ת\rb*.
