\p \v 17 \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb have sexual relations with both|עֶרְוַ֥ת\rb*\rb |תְגַלֵּ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb a woman|אִשָּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb and her daughter|וּבִתָּ֖הּ\rb*. \rb You are not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb to marry|תִקַּח֙\rb* \rb her son’s|בְּנָ֞הּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb or her daughter’s|בַּת־\rb* \rb daughter|בִּתָּ֗הּ\rb* \rb and have sexual relations with her|לְגַלּ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |עֶרְוָתָ֔הּ\rb*. \rb They|הֵ֖נָּה\rb* \rb are close relatives|שַׁאֲרָ֥ה\rb*; \rb it|הִֽוא\rb* \rb is depraved|זִמָּ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb take|תִקָּ֑ח\rb* \rb your wife’s|וְאִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb sister|אֲחֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb as a rival wife|לִצְרֹ֗ר\rb* \rb and have sexual relations with her|לְגַלּ֧וֹת\rb*\rb |עֶרְוָתָ֛הּ\rb* \rb while your wife is still alive|בְּחַיֶּֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb approach|תִקְרַ֔ב\rb* \rb a woman|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to have sexual relations with her|לְגַלּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |עֶרְוָתָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb during her menstrual period|בְּנִדַּ֣ת\rb*\rb |טֻמְאָתָ֑הּ\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb lie|תִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb carnally|שְׁכָבְתְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |לְזָ֑רַע\rb* \rb with|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb your neighbor’s|עֲמִֽיתְךָ֔\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb and thus defile yourself|לְטָמְאָה־\rb* \rb with her|בָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb give|תִתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb any of your children|וּמִֽזַּרְעֲךָ֥\rb* \rb to be sacrificed|לְהַעֲבִ֣יר\rb*\f + \fr 18:21 \ft Hebrew \fqa to make them pass through (the fire)\f* \rb to Molech|לַמֹּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, \rb for you must not|וְלֹ֧א\rb* \rb profane|תְחַלֵּ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the name|שֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb You must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb lie|תִשְׁכַּ֖ב\rb* \rb with|וְאֶ֨ת־\rb* \rb a man|זָכָ֔ר\rb* \rb as with|מִשְׁכְּבֵ֣י\rb* \rb a woman|אִשָּׁ֑ה\rb*; \rb that|הִֽוא׃\rb* \rb is an abomination|תּוֹעֵבָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb lie|תִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb carnally|שְׁכָבְתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb with any|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb animal|בְּהֵמָ֛ה\rb*, \rb thus defiling yourself|לְטָמְאָה־\rb* \rb with it|בָ֑הּ\rb*; \rb a woman|וְאִשָּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb stand|תַעֲמֹ֞ד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֧י\rb* \rb an animal|בְהֵמָ֛ה\rb* \rb to mate with it|לְרִבְעָ֖הּ\rb*; \rb that|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is a perversion|תֶּ֥בֶל\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb defile|תִּֽטַּמְּא֖וּ\rb* \rb yourselves by any|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb of these practices|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb by all|בְכָל־\rb* \rb these things|אֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am driving out|מְשַׁלֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb before you|מִפְּנֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb have defiled themselves|נִטְמְא֣וּ\rb*. \v 25 \rb Even the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb has become defiled|וַתִּטְמָ֣א\rb*, \rb so I am punishing it|וָאֶפְקֹ֥ד\rb* \rb for its sin|עֲוֺנָ֖הּ\rb*, \rb and the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb will vomit out|וַתָּקִ֥א\rb* \rb its|אֶת־\rb* \rb inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb But you|אַתֶּ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb are to keep|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקֹּתַי֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטַ֔י\rb*, \rb and you must not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb commit|תַעֲשׂ֔וּ\rb* \rb any|מִכֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb abominations|הַתּוֹעֵבֹ֖ת\rb*— \rb neither your native-born|הָֽאֶזְרָ֔ח\rb* \rb nor the foreigner|וְהַגֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb who lives|הַגָּ֥ר\rb* \rb among you|בְּתוֹכְכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵֽׁי־\rb* \rb who were in the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb committed|עָשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb abominations|הַתּוֹעֵבֹ֣ת\rb*, \rb and the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb has become defiled|וַתִּטְמָ֖א\rb*. \v 28 \rb So if you defile|בְּטַֽמַּאֲכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*,\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb it will vomit you out|תָקִ֤יא\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb it spewed out|קָאָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּ֖וֹי\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb Therefore|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb anyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb commits|יַעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb any|מִכֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb abominations|הַתּוֹעֵב֖וֹת\rb* \rb must be cut off|וְנִכְרְת֛וּ\rb*\rb |הַנְּפָשׁ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |הָעֹשֹׂ֖ת\rb* \rb from among|מִקֶּ֥רֶב\rb* \rb his people|עַמָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb You must keep|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My charge|מִשְׁמַרְתִּ֗י\rb* \rb not|לְבִלְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb to practice|עֲשׂ֜וֹת\rb* \rb any of the abominable|הַתּֽוֹעֵבֹת֙\rb* \rb customs|מֵחֻקּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were practiced|נַעֲשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb so that you do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb defile yourselves|תִֽטַּמְּא֖וּ\rb* \rb by them|בָּהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃פ\rb*.”
\c 19
\s1 Commandments for Holiness
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Speak|דַּבֵּ֞ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֧ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵהֶ֖ם\rb*: \rb Be|תִּהְי֑וּ\rb* \rb holy|קְדֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*, \rb am holy|קָד֔וֹשׁ\rb*.\f + \fr 19:2 \ft Cited in 1 Peter 1:16\f*
\p \v 3 \rb Each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of you must respect|תִּירָ֔אוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his mother|אִמּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb and father|וְאָבִיו֙\rb*, \rb and you must keep|תִּשְׁמֹ֑רוּ\rb* \rb My Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתֹתַ֖י\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb turn|תִּפְנוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb idols|הָ֣אֱלִילִ֔ים\rb* \rb or make|תַעֲשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb molten|מַסֵּכָ֔ה\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb gods|וֵֽאלֹהֵי֙\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb When|וְכִ֧י\rb* \rb you sacrifice|תִזְבְּח֛וּ\rb*\rb |זֶ֥בַח\rb* \rb a peace offering|שְׁלָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb you shall offer it|תִּזְבָּחֻֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb for your acceptance|לִֽרְצֹנְכֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 6 \rb It shall be eaten|יֵאָכֵ֖ל\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֧וֹם\rb* \rb you sacrifice it|זִבְחֲכֶ֛ם\rb*, \rb or on the next day|וּמִֽמָּחֳרָ֑ת\rb*; \rb but what remains|וְהַנּוֹתָר֙\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb on the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֔י\rb* \rb day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb must be burned up|בָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |יִשָּׂרֵֽף׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb If|וְאִ֛ם\rb* \rb any of it is eaten|הֵאָכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |יֵאָכֵ֖ל\rb* \rb on the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֑י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb it|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is tainted|פִּגּ֥וּל\rb* \rb and will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be accepted|יֵרָצֶֽה׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Whoever eats|וְאֹֽכְלָיו֙\rb* \rb it will bear|יִשָּׂ֔א\rb* \rb his iniquity|עֲוֺנ֣וֹ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he has profaned|חִלֵּ֑ל\rb* \rb what is holy|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*. \rb That|הַהִ֖וא\rb* \rb person|הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb must be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb from his people|מֵעַמֶּֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\s1 Love Your Neighbor
\p \v 9 \rb When you reap|וּֽבְקֻצְרְכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the harvest|קְצִ֣יר\rb* \rb of your land|אַרְצְכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb you are not|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb to reap|תְכַלֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb to the very edges|פְּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb of your field|שָׂדְךָ֖\rb*\rb |לִקְצֹ֑ר\rb* \rb or gather|תְלַקֵּֽט׃\rb* \rb the gleanings|וְלֶ֥קֶט\rb* \rb of your harvest|קְצִֽירְךָ֖\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb*. \v 10 \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb strip your vineyard|וְכַרְמְךָ֙\rb* \rb bare|תְעוֹלֵ֔ל\rb* \rb or gather|תְלַקֵּ֑ט\rb* \rb its|כַּרְמְךָ֖\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb fallen grapes|וּפֶ֥רֶט\rb*. \rb Leave|תַּעֲזֹ֣ב\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb for the poor|לֶֽעָנִ֤י\rb* \rb and the foreigner|וְלַגֵּר֙\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb You must not|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb steal|תִּגְנֹ֑בוּ\rb*. \rb You must not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb lie|תְכַחֲשׁ֥וּ\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb or deceive|תְשַׁקְּר֖וּ\rb* \rb one|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb another|בַּעֲמִיתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb You must not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb swear|תִשָּׁבְע֥וּ\rb* \rb falsely|לַשָּׁ֑קֶר\rb* \rb by My name|בִשְׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb and so profane|וְחִלַּלְתָּ֛\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the name|שֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb You must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb defraud|תַעֲשֹׁ֥ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your neighbor|רֵֽעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb rob him|תִגְזֹ֑ל\rb*.
\p \rb You|אִתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb withhold|תָלִ֞ין\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning|בֹּֽקֶר׃\rb* \rb the wages|פְּעֻלַּ֥ת\rb* \rb due a hired hand|שָׂכִ֛יר\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb curse|תְקַלֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb the deaf|חֵרֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb or place|תִתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb a stumbling block|מִכְשֹׁ֑ל\rb* \rb before|וְלִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the blind|עִוֵּ֔ר\rb*,\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb but you shall fear|וְיָרֵ֥אתָ\rb* \rb your God|מֵּאֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb pervert|תַעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb*\rb |עָ֙וֶל֙\rb* \rb justice|בַּמִּשְׁפָּ֔ט\rb*; \rb you must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb show partiality|תִשָּׂ֣א\rb*\rb |פְנֵי־\rb* \rb to the poor|דָ֔ל\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb favoritism|תֶהְדַּ֖ר\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb to the rich|גָד֑וֹל\rb*; \rb you are to judge|תִּשְׁפֹּ֥ט\rb* \rb your neighbor|עֲמִיתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb fairly|בְּצֶ֖דֶק\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb go|תֵלֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb about spreading slander|רָכִיל֙\rb* \rb among your people|בְּעַמֶּ֔יךָ\rb*.
\p \rb You must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb endanger|תַעֲמֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the life|דַּ֣ם\rb*\f + \fr 19:16 \ft Literally \fqa blood\f* \rb of your neighbor|רֵעֶ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb You must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb harbor hatred|תִשְׂנָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb against your brother|אָחִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb in your heart|בִּלְבָבֶ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb Directly rebuke|הוֹכֵ֤חַ\rb*\rb |תּוֹכִ֙יחַ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your neighbor|עֲמִיתֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb so that you will not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb incur|תִשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb guilt|חֵֽטְא׃\rb* \rb on account of him|עָלָ֖יו\rb*. \v 18 \rb Do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb seek revenge|תִקֹּ֤ם\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb or bear a grudge|תִטֹּר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb against any|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your people|עַמֶּ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb but love|וְאָֽהַבְתָּ֥\rb* \rb your neighbor|לְרֵעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb as yourself|כָּמ֑וֹךָ\rb*.\f + \fr 19:18 \ft Cited in Matthew 5:43, Matthew 19:19, Matthew 22:39, Mark 12:31, Luke 10:27, Romans 13:9, Galatians 5:14, and James 2:8\f* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 Keep My Statutes
\p \v 19 \rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb You are to keep|תִּשְׁמֹרוּ֒\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקֹּתַי֮\rb*. \rb You shall not|לֹא־\rb* \rb crossbreed|תַרְבִּ֣יעַ\rb* \rb two different kinds|כִּלְאַ֔יִם\rb* \rb of livestock|בְּהֶמְתְּךָ֙\rb*; \rb you shall not sow|תִזְרַ֣ע\rb* \rb your fields|שָׂדְךָ֖\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb with two kinds|כִּלְאָ֑יִם\rb* \rb of seed|יַעֲלֶ֖ה\rb*; \rb and you shall not wear|עָלֶֽיךָ׃פ\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb clothing|וּבֶ֤גֶד\rb* \rb made of two kinds|כִּלְאַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb of material|שַֽׁעַטְנֵ֔ז\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|וְ֠אִישׁ\rb* \rb lies|יִשְׁכַּ֨ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שִׁכְבַת־\rb* \rb carnally|זֶ֗רַע\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֜ה\rb*\rb |וְהִ֤וא\rb* \rb with a slave girl|שִׁפְחָה֙\rb* \rb promised|נֶחֱרֶ֣פֶת\rb* \rb to another man|לְאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb but who has not|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |נִפְדָּ֔תָה\rb* \rb been redeemed|וְהָפְדֵּה֙\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb given|נִתַּן־\rb* \rb her|לָ֑הּ\rb* \rb freedom|חֻפְשָׁ֖ה\rb*, \rb there must be|תִּהְיֶ֛ה\rb* \rb due punishment|בִּקֹּ֧רֶת\rb*. \rb But they are not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to be put to death|יוּמְת֖וּ\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb she had not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb been freed|חֻפָּֽשָׁה׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb The man, however, must bring|וְהֵבִ֤יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a ram|אֵ֖יל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb as his guilt offering|אֲשָׁמוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אָשָֽׁם׃\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*. \v 22 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb shall make atonement|וְכִפֶּר֩\rb* \rb on his behalf|עָלָ֨יו\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb with the ram|בְּאֵ֤יל\rb* \rb of the guilt offering|הָֽאָשָׁם֙\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the sin|חַטָּאת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he has committed|חָטָ֑א\rb*, \rb and he will be forgiven|וְנִסְלַ֣ח\rb* \rb the sin|מֵחַטָּאת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he has committed|חָטָֽא׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb When|וְכִי־\rb* \rb you enter|תָבֹ֣אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb and plant|וּנְטַעְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb kind of tree|עֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb for food|מַאֲכָ֔ל\rb*, \rb you shall regard|וַעֲרַלְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the fruit|פִּרְי֑וֹ\rb* \rb as forbidden|עָרְלָת֖וֹ\rb*.\f + \fr 19:23 \ft Hebrew \fqa as uncircumcised\ft ; twice in this verse\f* \rb For three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֗ים\rb* \rb it will be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb forbidden|עֲרֵלִ֖ים\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb and must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be eaten|יֵאָכֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb In the fourth|הָרְבִיעִ֔ת\rb* \rb year|וּבַשָּׁנָה֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its fruit|פִּרְי֑וֹ\rb* \rb must be|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb consecrated|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb as a praise offering|הִלּוּלִ֖ים\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb But in the fifth|הַחֲמִישִׁ֗ת\rb* \rb year|וּבַשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb you may eat|תֹּֽאכְלוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its fruit|פִּרְי֔וֹ\rb*; \rb thus your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb harvest|תְּבוּאָת֑וֹ\rb* \rb will be increased|לְהוֹסִ֥יף\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb You must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb anything with|עַל־\rb* \rb blood still in it|הַדָּ֑ם\rb*.
\p \rb You must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb practice divination|תְנַחֲשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb sorcery|תְעוֹנֵֽנוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb cut off the hair|תַקִּ֔פוּ\rb* \rb at the sides|פְּאַ֖ת\rb* \rb of your head|רֹאשְׁכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb or clip off|תַשְׁחִ֔ית\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the edges|פְּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb of your beard|זְקָנֶֽךָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb You must not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb make any cuts|וְשֶׂ֣רֶט\rb*\rb |תִתְּנוּ֙\rb* \rb in your bodies|בִּבְשַׂרְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb for the dead|לָנֶ֗פֶשׁ\rb* \rb or put|תִתְּנ֖וּ\rb* \rb tattoo|קַֽעֲקַ֔ע\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb marks|וּכְתֹ֣בֶת\rb* \rb on yourselves|בָּכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb You must not|אַל־\rb* \rb defile|תְּחַלֵּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your daughter|בִּתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb by making her a prostitute|לְהַזְנוֹתָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb or|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb will be prostituted|תִזְנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb and filled|וּמָלְאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb with depravity|זִמָּֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb You must keep|תִּשְׁמֹ֔רוּ\rb* \rb My Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתֹתַ֣י\rb* \rb and have reverence for|תִּירָ֑אוּ\rb* \rb My sanctuary|וּמִקְדָּשִׁ֖י\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb You must not|אַל־\rb* \rb turn|תִּפְנ֤וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb mediums|הָאֹבֹת֙\rb* \rb or|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb spiritists|הַיִּדְּעֹנִ֔ים\rb*; \rb do not seek them out|תְּבַקְשׁ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אַל־\rb*, \rb or you will be defiled|לְטָמְאָ֣ה\rb* \rb by them|בָהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb You are to rise|תָּק֔וּם\rb* \rb in the presence|מִפְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the elderly|שֵׂיבָה֙\rb*, \rb honor|וְהָדַרְתָּ֖\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the aged|זָקֵ֑ן\rb*, \rb and fear|וְיָרֵ֥אתָ\rb* \rb your God|מֵּאֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb When|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a foreigner|גֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb resides|יָג֧וּר\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּךָ֛\rb* \rb in your land|בְּאַרְצְכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb you must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb oppress|תוֹנ֖וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 34 \rb You must treat|יִהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb the foreigner|הַגֵּ֣ר׀\rb* \rb living|הַגָּ֣ר\rb* \rb among you|אִתְּכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb as native-born|כְּאֶזְרָ֣ח\rb*\rb |מִכֶּם֩\rb* \rb and love|וְאָהַבְתָּ֥\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb as yourself|כָּמ֔וֹךָ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you were|הֱיִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb foreigners|גֵרִ֥ים\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 35 \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb use|תַעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb dishonest|עָ֖וֶל\rb* \rb measures|בַּמִּשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb* \rb of length|בַּמִּדָּ֕ה\rb*, \rb weight|בַּמִּשְׁקָ֖ל\rb*, \rb or volume|וּבַמְּשׂוּרָֽה׃\rb*. \v 36 \rb You shall maintain|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb honest|צֶ֣דֶק\rb* \rb scales|מֹ֧אזְנֵי\rb* \rb and|צֶ֗דֶק\rb* \rb weights|אַבְנֵי־\rb*, \rb an honest|צֶ֛דֶק\rb* \rb ephah|אֵ֥יפַת\rb*,\f + \fr 19:36 \fqa An ephah \ft is a dry measure of approximately 20 dry quarts or 22 liters.\f* \rb and an honest|צֶ֖דֶק\rb* \rb hin|וְהִ֥ין\rb*.\f + \fr 19:36 \fqa A hin \ft is a liquid measure of approximately 0.97 gallons or 3.67 liters.\f* \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb brought|הוֹצֵ֥אתִי\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb You must keep|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקֹּתַי֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטַ֔י\rb* \rb and follow|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\c 20
\s1 Punishments for Disobedience
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Tell|תֹּאמַר֒\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֘ל\rb*, ‘\rb Any|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אִישׁ֩\rb* \rb Israelite|מִבְּנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb or|וּמִן־\rb* \rb foreigner|הַגֵּ֣ר׀\rb* \rb living|הַגָּ֣ר\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb gives|יִתֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb any of his children|מִזַּרְע֛וֹ\rb* \rb to Molech|לַמֹּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb must be put to death|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָ֑ת\rb*. \rb The people|עַ֥ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb are to stone|יִרְגְּמֻ֥הוּ\rb* \rb him|בָאָֽבֶן׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb And I|וַאֲנִ֞י\rb* \rb will set|אֶתֵּ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My face|פָּנַי֙\rb* \rb against that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb man|בָּאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and cut him off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb from|מִקֶּ֣רֶב\rb* \rb his people|עַמּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb by giving|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb his offspring|מִזַּרְעוֹ֙\rb* \rb to Molech|לַמֹּ֔לֶךְ\rb*,\rb |לְמַ֗עַן\rb* \rb he has defiled|טַמֵּא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My sanctuary|מִקְדָּשִׁ֔י\rb* \rb and profaned|וּלְחַלֵּ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My holy|קָדְשִֽׁי׃\rb* \rb name|שֵׁ֥ם\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb And if|וְאִ֡ם\rb* \rb the people|עַ֨ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb ever hide|הַעְלֵ֣ם\rb*\rb |יַעְלִימֽוּ֩\rb* \rb their eyes|עֵֽינֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and fail|לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb to put to death|הָמִ֥ית\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb who|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb gives|בְּתִתּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb one of his children|מִזַּרְע֖וֹ\rb* \rb to Molech|לַמֹּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, \v 5 \rb then I|אֲנִ֧י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will set|וְשַׂמְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb My face|פָּנַ֛י\rb* \rb against that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb man|בָּאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb and his family|וּבְמִשְׁפַּחְתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and cut off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֨י\rb*\rb |אֹת֜וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb from among|מִקֶּ֥רֶב\rb* \rb their people|עַמָּֽם׃\rb* \rb both him and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who follow him|אַחֲרָ֗יו\rb* \rb in prostituting themselves|הַזֹּנִ֣ים\rb*\rb |לִזְנ֛וֹת\rb* \rb with|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb Molech|הַמֹּ֖לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Whoever|וְהַנֶּ֗פֶשׁ\rb* \rb turns|תִּפְנֶ֤ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb mediums|הָֽאֹבֹת֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb or spiritists|הַיִּדְּעֹנִ֔ים\rb* \rb to prostitute himself|לִזְנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb with them|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb I will also set|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb My face|פָּנַי֙\rb* \rb against that person|בַּנֶּ֣פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַהִ֔וא\rb* \rb and cut him off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb from|מִקֶּ֥רֶב\rb* \rb his people|עַמּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Consecrate yourselves|וְהִ֨תְקַדִּשְׁתֶּ֔ם\rb*, \rb therefore, and be|וִהְיִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb holy|קְדֹשִׁ֑ים\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb And you shall keep|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקֹּתַ֔י\rb* \rb and practice them|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֖ם\rb*.\rb |אֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb who sanctifies you|מְקַדִּשְׁכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb anyone|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אִ֗ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb curses|יְקַלֵּ֧ל\rb*\f + \fr 20:9 \ft Or \fqa dishonors \ft or \fqa reviles\ft ; similarly again in this verse\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֛יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb or mother|אִמּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb he must be put to death|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָ֑ת\rb*.\f + \fr 20:9 \ft Cited in Matthew 15:4 and Mark 7:10\f* \rb He has cursed|קִלֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֧יו\rb* \rb or mother|וְאִמּ֛וֹ\rb*; \rb his blood|דָּמָ֥יו\rb* \rb shall be upon him|בּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\s1 Punishments for Sexual Immorality
