\s1 Distinguish between Clean and Unclean
\p \v 22 \rb You are therefore to keep|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקֹּתַי֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and|כָּל־\rb* \rb ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטַ֔י\rb*\rb |וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֖ם\rb*,\rb |אֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb so that the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֜י\rb* \rb am bringing|מֵבִ֥יא\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb you to live|לָשֶׁ֥בֶת\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb vomit you out|תָקִ֤יא\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb*. \v 23 \rb You must not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb follow|תֵֽלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb the statutes|בְּחֻקֹּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּ֔וֹי\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am driving out|מְשַׁלֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb before you|מִפְּנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Because|כִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb they did|עָשׂ֔וּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these things|אֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb*, \rb I abhorred|וָאָקֻ֖ץ\rb* \rb them|בָּֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb But I have told|וָאֹמַ֣ר\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb that you|אַתֶּם֮\rb* \rb will inherit|תִּֽירְשׁ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their land|אַדְמָתָם֒\rb*, \rb since I|וַאֲנִ֞י\rb* \rb will give|אֶתְּנֶ֤נָּה\rb* \rb it to you|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb as an inheritance|לָרֶ֣שֶׁת\rb* —\rb |אֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb flowing|זָבַ֥ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָ֖ב\rb* \rb and honey|וּדְבָ֑שׁ\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has set you apart|הִבְדַּ֥לְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָֽעַמִּֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb You are therefore to distinguish|וְהִבְדַּלְתֶּ֞ם\rb* \rb between|בֵּֽין־\rb* \rb clean|הַטְּהֹרָה֙\rb* \rb and unclean|לַטְּמֵאָ֔ה\rb* \rb animals|הַבְּהֵמָ֤ה\rb* \rb and|וּבֵין־\rb*\rb |הַטָּמֵ֖א\rb* \rb birds|הָע֥וֹף\rb*\rb |לַטָּהֹ֑ר\rb*. \rb Do not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb become contaminated|תְשַׁקְּצ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |נַפְשֹֽׁתֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb by any animal|בַּבְּהֵמָ֣ה\rb* \rb or bird|וּבָע֗וֹף\rb*, \rb or by anything|וּבְכֹל֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb crawls|תִּרְמֹ֣שׂ\rb* \rb on the ground|הָֽאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb*; \rb I have set these|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb apart|הִבְדַּ֥לְתִּי\rb* \rb as unclean|לְטַמֵּֽא׃\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 26 \rb You are to be|וִהְיִ֤יתֶם\rb* \rb holy|קְדֹשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb to Me|לִי֙\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb am holy|קָד֖וֹשׁ\rb*, \rb and I have set you apart|וָאַבְדִּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the nations|הָֽעַמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb to be|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb My own|לִֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb A man|וְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb a woman|אִשָּׁ֗ה\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb who is|יִהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb a medium|א֛וֹב\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb spiritist|יִדְּעֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb must surely be put to death|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָ֑תוּ\rb*.\rb |בָּאֶ֛בֶן\rb* \rb They shall be stoned|יִרְגְּמ֥וּ\rb*;\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb their blood|דְּמֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb is upon them|בָּֽם׃פ\rb*.’”
\c 21
\s1 Holiness Required of Priests
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*, “\rb Speak|אֱמֹ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֑ן\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*, \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them that|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb a priest is not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to defile himself|יִטַּמָּ֖א\rb* \rb for a dead person|לְנֶ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb among his people|בְּעַמָּֽיו׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb except|כִּ֚י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb for his immediate|הַקָּרֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֑יו\rb* \rb family|לִשְׁאֵר֔וֹ\rb* — \rb his mother|לְאִמּ֣וֹ\rb*, \rb father|וּלְאָבִ֔יו\rb*, \rb son|וְלִבְנ֥וֹ\rb*, \rb daughter|וּלְבִתּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb or brother|וּלְאָחִֽיו׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb or his unmarried|הַבְּתוּלָה֙\rb* \rb sister|וְלַאֲחֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb who is near|הַקְּרוֹבָ֣ה\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, \rb since|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb she has|הָיְתָ֖ה\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb husband|לְאִ֑ישׁ\rb*\rb |לָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |יִטַּמָּֽא׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb He is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to defile himself|יִטַּמָּ֖א\rb* \rb for those related to him by marriage|בַּ֣עַל\rb*\rb |בְּעַמָּ֑יו\rb*, \rb and so profane himself|לְהֵ֖חַלּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Priests must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb make bald|יִקְרְחָה\rb*\rb |קָרְחָה֙\rb* \rb spots on their heads|בְּרֹאשָׁ֔ם\rb*, \rb shave off the edges|וּפְאַ֥ת\rb* \rb of their beards|זְקָנָ֖ם\rb*,\rb |לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |יְגַלֵּ֑חוּ\rb* \rb or make|יִשְׂרְט֖וּ\rb* \rb cuts|שָׂרָֽטֶת׃\rb* \rb in their bodies|וּבִ֨בְשָׂרָ֔ם\rb*.\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \v 6 \rb They must be|יִהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb holy|קְדֹשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb to their God|לֵאלֹ֣הֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb profane|יְחַלְּל֔וּ\rb* \rb the name|שֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb of their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Because|כִּי֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb they|הֵ֥ם\rb* \rb present|מַקְרִיבִ֖ם\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb the food offerings|אִשֵּׁ֨י\rb*, \rb the food|לֶ֧חֶם\rb* \rb of their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֛ם\rb*, \rb they must be|וְהָ֥יוּ\rb* \rb holy|קֹֽדֶשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb A priest must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb marry|יִקָּ֔חוּ\rb*\rb |וְאִשָּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb a woman|אִשָּׁ֨ה\rb* \rb defiled|וַחֲלָלָה֙\rb* \rb by prostitution|זֹנָ֤ה\rb* \rb or|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |יִקָּ֑חוּ\rb* \rb divorced|גְּרוּשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb by her husband|מֵאִישָׁ֖הּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the priest|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is holy|קָדֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb to his God|לֵאלֹהָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb You are to regard him as holy|וְקִדַּשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb presents|מַקְרִ֑יב\rb* \rb the food|לֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb of your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*. \rb He shall be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb holy|קָדֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb to you|לָּ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb am holy|קָד֔וֹשׁ\rb* — \rb I who set you apart|מְקַדִּשְׁכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb If|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb a priest’s|כֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb daughter|וּבַת֙\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb defiles herself|תֵחֵ֖ל\rb* \rb by prostituting herself|לִזְנ֑וֹת\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb she|הִ֣יא\rb* \rb profanes|מְחַלֶּ֔לֶת\rb* \rb her father|אָבִ֙יהָ֙\rb*; \rb she must be burned|תִּשָּׂרֵֽף׃ס\rb* \rb in the fire|בָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb The priest|וְהַכֹּהֵן֩\rb* \rb who is highest|הַגָּד֨וֹל\rb* \rb among his brothers|מֵאֶחָ֜יו\rb*, \rb who|אֲ‍ֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has had the anointing|הַמִּשְׁחָה֙\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֤מֶן\rb* \rb poured|יוּצַ֥ק\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֣וֹ׀\rb* \rb and has been ordained|וּמִלֵּ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |יָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb to wear|לִלְבֹּ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the priestly garments|הַבְּגָדִ֑ים\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb must not let|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb his hair|רֹאשׁוֹ֙\rb* \rb hang loose|יִפְרָ֔ע\rb*\f + \fr 21:10 \ft Or \fqa must not uncover his head\f* \rb or tear|יִפְרֹֽם׃\rb* \rb his garments|וּבְגָדָ֖יו\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb*. \v 11 \rb |וְעַ֛ל\rb* \rb He must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb go|יָבֹ֑א\rb* \rb near any|כָּל־\rb* \rb dead|מֵ֖ת\rb* \rb body|נַפְשֹׁ֥ת\rb*; \rb he must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb defile himself|יִטַּמָּֽא׃\rb*, \rb even for his father|לְאָבִ֥יו\rb* \rb or mother|וּלְאִמּ֖וֹ\rb*. \v 12 \rb |וּמִן־\rb* \rb He must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb leave|יֵצֵ֔א\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb*\rb |הַמִּקְדָּשׁ֙\rb* \rb or desecrate|יְחַלֵּ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the sanctuary|מִקְדַּ֣שׁ\rb* \rb of his God|אֱלֹהָ֑יו\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֡י\rb* \rb the consecration|נֵ֠זֶר\rb* \rb of the anointing|מִשְׁחַ֧ת\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֣מֶן\rb* \rb of his God|אֱלֹהָ֛יו\rb* \rb is on him|עָלָ֖יו\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb The woman|אִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb he|וְה֕וּא\rb* \rb marries|יִקָּֽח׃\rb* \rb must be a virgin|בִבְתוּלֶ֖יהָ\rb*. \v 14 \rb He is not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to marry|יִקָּ֑ח\rb*\rb |כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb a widow|אַלְמָנָ֤ה\rb*, \rb a divorced woman|וּגְרוּשָׁה֙\rb*, \rb or one defiled|וַחֲלָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb by prostitution|זֹנָ֔ה\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb He is to marry|יִקַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אִשָּֽׁה׃\rb* \rb a virgin|בְּתוּלָ֥ה\rb* \rb from his own people|מֵעַמָּ֖יו\rb*, \v 15 \rb so that he does not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb defile|יְחַלֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb his offspring|זַרְע֖וֹ\rb* \rb among his people|בְּעַמָּ֑יו\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb who sanctifies him|מְקַדְּשֽׁוֹ׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 Restrictions against Those with Blemishes
\p \v 16 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 17 “\rb Say|דַּבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb For the generations to come|לְדֹרֹתָ֗ם\rb*,\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb none|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb of your descendants|מִֽזַּרְעֲךָ֞\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb has|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a physical defect|מ֔וּם\rb* \rb may approach|יִקְרַ֔ב\rb* \rb to offer|לְהַקְרִ֖יב\rb* \rb the food|לֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb of his God|אֱלֹהָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb No|כָל־\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has any defect|מ֖וּם\rb* \rb may approach|יִקְרָ֑ב\rb* — \rb no man|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb who is blind|עִוֵּר֙\rb*, \rb lame|פִסֵּ֔חַ\rb*,\rb |א֥וֹ\rb* \rb disfigured|חָרֻ֖ם\rb*,\rb |א֥וֹ\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb deformed|שָׂרֽוּעַ׃\rb*; \v 19 \rb no man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a broken|שֶׁ֣בֶר\rb* \rb foot|רָ֑גֶל\rb* \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb*\rb |שֶׁ֥בֶר\rb* \rb hand|יָֽד׃\rb*, \v 20 \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb who is a hunchback|גִבֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb dwarf|דַ֔ק\rb*, \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb* \rb who has an eye|בְּעֵינ֑וֹ\rb* \rb defect|תְּבַלֻּ֣ל\rb*, \rb a festering rash|גָרָב֙\rb*,\rb |א֣וֹ\rb* \rb scabs|יַלֶּ֔פֶת\rb*,\rb |א֖וֹ\rb* \rb or|א֤וֹ\rb* \rb a crushed|מְר֥וֹחַ\rb* \rb testicle|אָֽשֶׁךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb No|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אִ֞ישׁ\rb* \rb descendant|מִזֶּ֙רַע֙\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has a defect|מ֗וּם\rb* \rb shall approach|יִגַּ֔שׁ\rb* \rb to present|לְהַקְרִ֖יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the food offerings|אִשֵּׁ֣י\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Since he has a defect|מ֣וּם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb*, \rb he is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to come near|יִגַּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb to offer|לְהַקְרִֽיב׃\rb* \rb the food|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb of his God|אֱלֹהָ֔יו\rb*. \v 22 \rb He may eat|יֹאכֵֽל׃\rb* \rb the most|מִקָּדְשֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb holy|הַקֳּדָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb food|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb of his God|אֱלֹהָ֔יו\rb* \rb as well as|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the holy food|הַקֳּדָשִׁ֖ים\rb*, \v 23 \rb but|אַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he has a defect|מ֣וּם\rb*,\rb |וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb he must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb go|יָבֹ֗א\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb near|אֶל־\rb* \rb the veil|הַפָּרֹ֜כֶת\rb* \rb or approach|יִגַּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֛חַ\rb*,\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb so as not to desecrate|יְחַלֵּל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My sanctuaries|מִקְדָּשַׁ֔י\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb who sanctifies them|מְקַדְּשָֽׁם׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 24 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb told|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb this to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֑יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\c 22
\s1 Restrictions against the Unclean
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Tell|דַּבֵּ֨ר\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֗יו\rb* \rb to treat with respect|וְיִנָּֽזְרוּ֙\rb* \rb the sacred offerings|מִקָּדְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb that the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |הֵ֧ם\rb* \rb have consecrated to Me|מַקְדִּשִׁ֛ים\rb*, \rb so that they do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb profane|יְחַלְּל֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My holy|קָדְשִׁ֑י\rb* \rb name|שֵׁ֣ם\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Tell|אֱמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb them that|אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb for the generations to come|לְדֹרֹ֨תֵיכֶ֜ם\rb*, \rb if any|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ׀\rb*\rb |מִכָּל־\rb* \rb of their descendants|זַרְעֲכֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb in a state of uncleanness|וְטֻמְאָת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |עָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb approaches|יִקְרַ֣ב\rb* \rb the sacred offerings|הַקֳּדָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb consecrate|יַקְדִּ֤ישׁוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb that|הַהִ֛וא\rb* \rb person|הַנֶּ֧פֶשׁ\rb* \rb must be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֞ה\rb* \rb from My presence|מִלְּפָנַ֖י\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb If a descendant|מִזֶּ֣רַע\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אִ֞ישׁ\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb*\rb |וְה֤וּא\rb* \rb has a skin disease|צָר֙וּעַ֙\rb*\f + \fr 22:4 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa tzaraath\ft , traditionally translated as \fqa leprosy\ft , were used for various skin diseases; see Leviticus 13.\f* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb a discharge|זָ֔ב\rb*, \rb he may not eat|יֹאכַ֔ל\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb the sacred offerings|בַּקֳּדָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he is clean|יִטְהָ֑ר\rb*. \rb Whoever touches|וְהַנֹּגֵ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb anything|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb defiled|טְמֵא־\rb* \rb by a corpse|נֶ֔פֶשׁ\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb by a man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has|תֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb an emission|שִׁכְבַת־\rb* \rb of semen|זָֽרַע׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb whoever|אִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb touches|יִגַּ֔ע\rb* \rb a|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb crawling creature|שֶׁ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |יִטְמָא־\rb* \rb or|א֤וֹ\rb* \rb a person|בְאָדָם֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb makes him unclean|יִטְמָא־\rb*, \rb whatever|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the uncleanness may be|טֻמְאָתֽוֹ׃\rb* — \v 6 \rb the man|נֶ֚פֶשׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb touches|תִּגַּע־\rb* \rb any of these|בּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb will remain unclean|וְטָמְאָ֖ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָ֑רֶב\rb*. \rb He must not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb eat|יֹאכַל֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the sacred offerings|הַקֳּדָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb unless|כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb he has bathed|רָחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb himself|בְּשָׂר֖וֹ\rb* \rb with water|בַּמָּֽיִם׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb When the sun|הַשֶּׁ֖מֶשׁ\rb* \rb has set|וּבָ֥א\rb*, \rb he will become clean|וְטָהֵ֑ר\rb*, \rb and then|וְאַחַר֙\rb* \rb he may eat|יֹאכַ֣ל\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the sacred offerings|הַקֳּדָשִׁ֔ים\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb are his food|לַחְמ֖וֹ\rb*. \v 8 \rb He must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb eat|יֹאכַ֖ל\rb* \rb anything found dead|נְבֵלָ֧ה\rb* \rb or torn by wild animals|וּטְרֵפָ֛ה\rb*, \rb which would make him unclean|לְטָמְאָה־\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb The priests must keep|וְשָׁמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My charge|מִשְׁמַרְתִּ֗י\rb*, \rb lest|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb they bear|יִשְׂא֤וּ\rb*\rb |עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb the guilt|חֵ֔טְא\rb* \rb and die|וּמֵ֥תוּ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they profane it|יְחַלְּלֻ֑הוּ\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb who sanctifies them|מְקַדְּשָֽׁם׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb No|לֹא־\rb* \rb one|וְכָל־\rb* \rb outside a priest’s family|זָ֖ר\rb* \rb may eat|יֹ֣אכַל\rb* \rb the sacred offering|קֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb nor|לֹא־\rb* \rb may the guest|תּוֹשַׁ֥ב\rb* \rb of a priest|כֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb or his hired hand|וְשָׂכִ֖יר\rb* \rb eat|יֹ֥אכַל\rb* \rb it|קֹֽדֶשׁ׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb But if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a priest|וְכֹהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb buys|יִקְנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a slave|נֶ֙פֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb with|קִנְיַ֣ן\rb* \rb his own money|כַּסְפּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb or if a slave|הֵ֖ם\rb* \rb is born|וִילִ֣יד\rb* \rb in his household|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*, \rb that slave|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb may eat|יֹ֣אכַל\rb*\rb |יֹאכְל֥וּ\rb* \rb his food|בְלַחְמֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb If|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the priest’s|כֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb daughter|וּבַת־\rb* \rb is married|תִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to a man|לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb other than a priest|זָ֑ר\rb*, \rb she|הִ֕וא\rb* \rb is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to eat|תֹאכֵֽל׃\rb* \rb of the sacred|הַקֳּדָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb contributions|בִּתְרוּמַ֥ת\rb*. \v 13 \rb But if|כִּ֨י\rb* \rb a priest’s|כֹּהֵן֩\rb* \rb daughter|וּבַת־\rb* \rb with no|אֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |לָהּ֒\rb* \rb children|וְזֶרַע֮\rb* \rb becomes|תִהְיֶ֜ה\rb* \rb widowed|אַלְמָנָ֣ה\rb* \rb or divorced|וּגְרוּשָׁ֗ה\rb* \rb and returns|וְשָׁבָ֞ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb her father’s|אָבִ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֤ית\rb*, \rb she may share|תֹּאכֵ֑ל\rb* \rb her father’s|אָבִ֖יהָ\rb* \rb food|מִלֶּ֥חֶם\rb* \rb as in her youth|כִּנְעוּרֶ֔יהָ\rb*. \rb But no|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb outsider|זָ֖ר\rb* \rb may share|יֹ֥אכַל\rb* \rb it|בּֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb anyone|וְאִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb eats|יֹאכַ֥ל\rb* \rb a sacred offering|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb in error|בִּשְׁגָגָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he must add|וְיָסַ֤ף\rb* \rb a fifth|חֲמִֽשִׁיתוֹ֙\rb* \rb to|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb its value and give|וְנָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb the sacred offering|הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb to the priest|לַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*. \v 15 \rb The priests must not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb profane|יְחַלְּל֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sacred offerings|קָדְשֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb that the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb present|יָרִ֖ימוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 16 \rb by allowing the people to eat|בְּאָכְלָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sacred offerings|קָדְשֵׁיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and thus to bear|וְהִשִּׂ֤יאוּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb the punishment|עֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb for guilt|אַשְׁמָ֔ה\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb who sanctifies them|מְקַדְּשָֽׁם׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 Worthy Offerings
\p \v 17 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 18 “\rb Speak|דַּבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֗יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶל֙\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֖\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb*, ‘\rb Any man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אִישׁ֩\rb* \rb of|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the house|מִבֵּ֨ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb or any foreign resident|הַגֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb presents|יַקְרִ֤יב\rb* \rb a gift|קָרְבָּנוֹ֙\rb*\rb |לְכָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb for a burnt offering|לְעֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb whether to fulfill a vow|נִדְרֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb or as a|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb freewill offering|נִדְבוֹתָ֔ם\rb*, \v 19 \rb must offer an unblemished|תָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb male|זָכָ֔ר\rb* \rb from the cattle|בַּבָּקָ֕ר\rb*, \rb sheep|בַּכְּשָׂבִ֖ים\rb*, \rb or goats|וּבָֽעִזִּֽים׃\rb* \rb in order for it to be accepted on your behalf|לִֽרְצֹנְכֶ֑ם\rb*. \v 20 \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb present|תַקְרִ֑יבוּ\rb* \rb anything|כֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb with|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb a defect|מ֖וּם\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb it will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb accepted|לְרָצ֖וֹן\rb* \rb on your behalf|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|וְאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb presents|יַקְרִ֤יב\rb*\rb |זֶֽבַח־\rb* \rb a peace offering|שְׁלָמִים֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb from the herd|בַּבָּקָ֖ר\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb flock|בַצֹּ֑אן\rb* \rb to fulfill|לְפַלֵּא־\rb* \rb a vow|נֶ֙דֶר֙\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb as a freewill offering|לִנְדָבָ֔ה\rb*, \rb it must be|יִֽהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb without blemish|תָּמִ֤ים\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb or defect|מ֖וּם\rb* \rb to be acceptable|לְרָצ֔וֹן\rb*. \v 22 \rb You are not|לֹא־\rb* \rb to present|תַקְרִ֥יבוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb any animal|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb that is blind|עַוֶּרֶת֩\rb*, \rb injured|שָׁב֜וּר\rb*, \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb maimed|חָר֣וּץ\rb*,\rb |אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb or|א֨וֹ\rb* \rb anything with a running sore|יַבֶּ֗לֶת\rb*,\rb |א֤וֹ\rb* \rb a festering rash|גָרָב֙\rb*,\rb |א֣וֹ\rb* \rb or a scab|יַלֶּ֔פֶת\rb*; \rb you must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb put|תִתְּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb any of these|מֵהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb as a food offering|וְאִשֶּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb You may present|תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb as a freewill offering|נְדָבָה֙\rb* \rb an ox|וְשׁ֥וֹר\rb*\f + \fr 22:23 \ft Or \fqa a bull \ft or \fqa a cow\f* \rb or sheep|וָשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb that has a deformed|שָׂר֣וּעַ\rb* \rb or stunted limb|וְקָל֑וּט\rb*, \rb but it is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb acceptable|יֵרָצֶֽה׃\rb* \rb in fulfillment of a vow|וּלְנֵ֖דֶר\rb*. \v 24 \rb You are not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to present|תַקְרִ֖יבוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb an animal whose testicles are bruised|וּמָע֤וּךְ\rb*, \rb crushed|וְכָתוּת֙\rb*, \rb torn|וְנָת֣וּק\rb*, \rb or cut|וְכָר֔וּת\rb*; \rb you are not to|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb sacrifice them|תַעֲשֽׂוּ׃\rb* \rb in your land|וּֽבְאַרְצְכֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 25 \rb |וּמִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb Neither you nor|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb a foreigner|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |נֵכָ֗ר\rb* \rb shall present|תַקְרִ֛יבוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb food|לֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb to your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb from any|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb such animal|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb*. \rb They will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be accepted|יֵרָצ֖וּ\rb* \rb on your behalf|לָכֶֽם׃פ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they are deformed|מָשְׁחָתָ֤ם\rb* \rb and flawed|מ֣וּם\rb*.’”
\p \v 26 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 27 “\rb When|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb an ox|שׁ֣וֹר\rb*,\f + \fr 22:27 \ft Or \fqa a calf\f* \rb a sheep|כֶ֤שֶׂב\rb*,\rb |אוֹ־\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb a goat|עֵז֙\rb* \rb is born|יִוָּלֵ֔ד\rb*, \rb it must remain|וְהָיָ֛ה\rb* \rb with|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb its mother|אִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb*. \rb From the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִי֙\rb* \rb day|וּמִיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb on|וָהָ֔לְאָה\rb*, \rb it will be acceptable as|יֵרָצֶ֕ה\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb presented|לְקָרְבַּ֥ן\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb But you must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb slaughter|תִשְׁחֲט֖וּ\rb* \rb an ox|וְשׁ֖וֹר\rb*\f + \fr 22:28 \ft Or \fqa a cow\f* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb a sheep|שֶׂ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֣וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb on the same|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb as its young|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb When|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb you sacrifice|תִזְבְּח֥וּ\rb* \rb a thank|תּוֹדָ֖ה\rb* \rb offering|זֶֽבַח־\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb offer it|תִּזְבָּֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb so that it may be acceptable on your behalf|לִֽרְצֹנְכֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 30 \rb It must be eaten|יֵאָכֵ֔ל\rb* \rb that same|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֤וֹם\rb*. \rb Do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb leave|תוֹתִ֥ירוּ\rb* \rb any of it|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning|בֹּ֑קֶר\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb You are to keep|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb My commandments|מִצְוֺתַ֔י\rb* \rb and practice|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb You must not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb profane|תְחַלְּלוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My holy|קָדְשִׁ֔י\rb* \rb name|שֵׁ֣ם\rb*. \rb I must be acknowledged as holy|וְנִ֨קְדַּשְׁתִּ֔י\rb* \rb among|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb who sanctifies you|מְקַדִּשְׁכֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 33 \rb who brought you out|הַמּוֹצִ֤יא\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb to be|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God|לֵאלֹהִ֑ים\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\c 23
\s1 Feasts and Sabbaths
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Speak|דַּבֵּ֞ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb*, ‘\rb These|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb are|הֵ֖ם\rb* \rb My appointed feasts|מוֹעֲדָֽי׃\rb*, \rb the feasts|מוֹעֲדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you are to proclaim|תִּקְרְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb as sacred|קֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb assemblies|מִקְרָאֵ֣י\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb For six|שֵׁ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִים֮\rb* \rb work|מְלָאכָה֒\rb* \rb may be done|תֵּעָשֶׂ֣ה\rb*, \rb but the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֗י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb is a Sabbath|שַׁבַּ֤ת\rb* \rb of complete rest|שַׁבָּתוֹן֙\rb*, \rb a day of sacred|קֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb assembly|מִקְרָא־\rb*. \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb do|תַעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb work|מְלָאכָ֖ה\rb*; \rb wherever|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb you live|מֽוֹשְׁבֹתֵיכֶֽם׃פ\rb*, \rb it|הִוא֙\rb* \rb is a Sabbath|שַׁבָּ֥ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*.
\s1 Passover and the Feast of Unleavened Bread
\p \v 4 \rb These|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb are the LORD’s|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb appointed feasts|מוֹעֲדֵ֣י\rb*, \rb the sacred|קֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb assemblies|מִקְרָאֵ֖י\rb* \rb you are to proclaim|תִּקְרְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb at their appointed times|בְּמוֹעֲדָֽם׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb The Passover|פֶּ֖סַח\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb begins at|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb twilight|הָעַרְבָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb on the fourteenth|בְּאַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֛ר\rb*\f + \fr 23:5 \ft Hebrew \fqa begins between the two evenings of the fourteenth\f* \rb day|לַחֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the first|הָרִאשׁ֗וֹן\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*. \v 6 \rb On the fifteenth|וּבַחֲמִשָּׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb day|יוֹם֙\rb* \rb of the same|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb month begins|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb the Feast|חַ֥ג\rb* \rb of Unleavened Bread|הַמַּצּ֖וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 23:6 \ft That is, the seven-day period after the Passover during which no leaven may be eaten; see Exodus 12:14–20.\f* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb For seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb you must eat|תֹּאכֵֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb unleavened bread|מַצּ֥וֹת\rb*. \v 7 \rb On the first|הָֽרִאשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb day|בַּיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb you are to hold|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb a sacred|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb assembly|מִקְרָא־\rb*; \rb you are not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to do|תַעֲשֽׂוּ׃\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb regular|עֲבֹדָ֖ה\rb* \rb work|מְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb*. \v 8 \rb For seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb you are to present|וְהִקְרַבְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*. \rb On the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִי֙\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb there shall be a sacred|קֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb assembly|מִקְרָא־\rb*; \rb you must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb do|תַעֲשֽׂוּ׃פ\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb regular|עֲבֹדָ֖ה\rb* \rb work|מְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb*.’”
\s1 The Feast of Firstfruits
\p \v 9 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 10 “\rb Speak|דַּבֵּ֞ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb*, ‘\rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you enter|תָבֹ֣אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am giving|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and you reap|וּקְצַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its harvest|קְצִירָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb you are to bring|וַהֲבֵאתֶ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb* \rb a sheaf|עֹ֛מֶר\rb* \rb of the firstfruits|רֵאשִׁ֥ית\rb* \rb of your harvest|קְצִירְכֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 11 \rb And he shall wave|וְהֵנִ֧יף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sheaf|הָעֹ֛מֶר\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb so that it may be accepted on your behalf|לִֽרְצֹנְכֶ֑ם\rb*; \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb* \rb is to wave it|יְנִיפֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb on the day after|מִֽמָּחֳרַת֙\rb* \rb the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֔ת\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb On the day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb you wave|הֲנִֽיפְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sheaf|הָעֹ֑מֶר\rb*, \rb you shall offer|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֕ם\rb* \rb a year-old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שְׁנָת֛וֹ\rb* \rb lamb|כֶּ֣בֶשׂ\rb* \rb without blemish|תָּמִ֧ים\rb* \rb as a burnt offering|לְעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*, \v 13 \rb along with its grain offering|וּמִנְחָתוֹ֩\rb* \rb of two-tenths of an ephah|שְׁנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֹנִ֜ים\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֣לֶת\rb*\f + \fr 23:13 \fqa Two-tenths of an ephah \ft is approximately 4 dry quarts or 4.4 liters (probably about 5.1 pounds or 2.3 kilograms of flour); also in verse 17.\f* \rb mixed|בְּלוּלָ֥ה\rb* \rb with oil|בַשֶּׁ֛מֶן\rb* — \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֑חַ\rb* \rb aroma|רֵ֣יחַ\rb* — \rb and its drink offering|וְנִסְכֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb of a quarter|רְבִיעִ֥ת\rb* \rb hin|הַהִֽין׃\rb* \rb of wine|יַ֖יִן\rb*.\f + \fr 23:13 \fqa A quarter hin \ft is approximately 0.97 quarts or 0.92 liters of wine.\f*
\p \v 14 \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb eat|תֹֽאכְל֗וּ\rb* \rb any bread|וְלֶחֶם֩\rb* \rb or roasted|וְקָלִ֨י\rb* \rb or new grain|וְכַרְמֶ֜ל\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb very|עֶ֙צֶם֙\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |עַ֚ד\rb* \rb you have brought|הֲבִ֣יאֲכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb this|אֶת־\rb* \rb offering|קָרְבַּ֖ן\rb* \rb to your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb This is to be a permanent|עוֹלָם֙\rb* \rb statute|חֻקַּ֤ת\rb* \rb for the generations to come|לְדֹרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb wherever|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb you live|מֹשְׁבֹֽתֵיכֶֽם׃ס\rb*.
\s1 The Feast of Weeks
\p \v 15 \rb From the day after|מִמָּחֳרַ֣ת\rb* \rb the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֔ת\rb*, \rb the day|מִיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb you brought|הֲבִ֣יאֲכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sheaf|עֹ֖מֶר\rb* \rb of the wave offering|הַתְּנוּפָ֑ה\rb*, \rb you are to count off|וּסְפַרְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb full|תְּמִימֹ֥ת\rb* \rb weeks|שַׁבָּת֖וֹת\rb*. \v 16 \rb You shall count off|תִּסְפְּר֖וּ\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb days|י֑וֹם\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb the day after|מִֽמָּחֳרַ֤ת\rb* \rb the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔ת\rb* \rb Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּת֙\rb*, \rb and then present|וְהִקְרַבְתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb an offering of new|חֲדָשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb grain|מִנְחָ֥ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Bring|תָּבִ֣יאּוּ׀\rb* \rb two|שְׁ֚תַּיִם\rb* \rb loaves of bread|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb from your dwellings|מִמּוֹשְׁבֹ֨תֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb as a wave offering|תְּנוּפָ֗ה\rb*, \rb each made from two-tenths of an ephah|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֹנִ֔ים\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֣לֶת\rb*,\rb |תִּהְיֶ֔ינָה\rb* \rb baked|תֵּאָפֶ֑ינָה\rb* \rb with leaven|חָמֵ֖ץ\rb*, \rb as the firstfruits|בִּכּוּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Along with|עַל־\rb* \rb the bread|הַלֶּ֗חֶם\rb* \rb you are to present|וְהִקְרַבְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֨ת\rb* \rb unblemished|תְּמִימִם֙\rb* \rb male lambs|כְּבָשִׂ֤ים\rb* \rb a year old|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb young bull|וּפַ֧ר\rb*,\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בָּקָ֛ר\rb* \rb and two|שְׁנָ֑יִם\rb* \rb rams|וְאֵילִ֣ם\rb*. \rb They will be|יִהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb a burnt offering|עֹלָה֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb together with their grain offerings|וּמִנְחָתָם֙\rb* \rb and drink offerings|וְנִסְכֵּיהֶ֔ם\rb* — \rb a food offering|אִשֵּׁ֥ה\rb*, \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb aroma|רֵֽיחַ־\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb You shall also prepare|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֛ם\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb male goat|שְׂעִיר־\rb*\rb |עִזִּ֥ים\rb* \rb as a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֑את\rb* \rb and two|וּשְׁנֵ֧י\rb* \rb male lambs|כְבָשִׂ֛ים\rb* \rb a year old|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb as a peace offering|שְׁלָמִֽים׃\rb*\rb |לְזֶ֥בַח\rb*. \v 20 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן׀\rb* \rb is to wave|וְהֵנִ֣יף\rb* \rb the lambs|אֹתָ֡ם\rb* \rb as a wave offering|תְּנוּפָה֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb together with|עַל֩\rb* \rb the bread|לֶ֨חֶם\rb* \rb of the firstfruits|הַבִּכּוּרִ֤ים\rb*.\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb The bread and the two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb lambs|כְּבָשִׂ֑ים\rb* \rb shall be|יִהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb holy|קֹ֛דֶשׁ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb for the priest|לַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb On that|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb same|בְּעֶ֣צֶם׀\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb you are to proclaim|וּקְרָאתֶ֞ם\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb a sacred|קֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb assembly|מִֽקְרָא־\rb*, \rb and|לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb you must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb do|תַעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb regular work|מְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb*\rb |עֲבֹדָ֖ה\rb*. \rb This is to be a permanent|עוֹלָ֛ם\rb* \rb statute|חֻקַּ֥ת\rb* \rb wherever|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb you live|מוֹשְׁבֹ֥תֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb for the generations to come|לְדֹרֹֽתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb When you reap|וּֽבְקֻצְרְכֶ֞ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the harvest|קְצִ֣יר\rb* \rb of your land|אַרְצְכֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb reap|בְּקֻצְרֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb all the way|תְכַלֶּ֞ה\rb* \rb to the edges|פְּאַ֤ת\rb* \rb of your field|שָֽׂדְךָ֙\rb* \rb or gather|תְלַקֵּ֑ט\rb* \rb the gleanings|וְלֶ֥קֶט\rb* \rb of your harvest|קְצִירְךָ֖\rb*.\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb Leave|תַּעֲזֹ֣ב\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb for the poor|לֶֽעָנִ֤י\rb* \rb and the foreign resident|וְלַגֵּר֙\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃ס\rb*.’”
\s1 The Feast of Trumpets
\p \v 23 \rb The LORD also|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 24 “\rb Speak|דַּבֵּ֛ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and say|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb On the first|בְּאֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb day|לַחֹ֗דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֜י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֨דֶשׁ\rb* \rb you are to have|יִהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb a day of rest|שַׁבָּת֔וֹן\rb*, \rb a sacred|קֹֽדֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb assembly|מִקְרָא־\rb* \rb announced|זִכְר֥וֹן\rb* \rb by trumpet blasts|תְּרוּעָ֖ה\rb*.\f + \fr 23:24 \ft Or \fqa a sacred assembly, a memorial of shouting\f* \v 25 \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb do|תַעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb regular work|מְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb*\rb |עֲבֹדָ֖ה\rb*, \rb but you are to present|וְהִקְרַבְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.’”
\s1 The Day of Atonement
\p \v 26 \rb Again the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 27 “\rb |אַ֡ךְ\rb* \rb The tenth|בֶּעָשׂ֣וֹר\rb* \rb day of this|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֨י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹדֶשׁ֩\rb* \rb is the Day|י֧וֹם\rb* \rb of Atonement|הַכִּפֻּרִ֣ים\rb*.\rb |ה֗וּא\rb* \rb You shall hold|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb a sacred|קֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb assembly|מִֽקְרָא־\rb* \rb and humble|וְעִנִּיתֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb yourselves|נַפְשֹׁתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*,\f + \fr 23:27 \ft Or \fqa afflict your souls \ft or \fqa deny yourselves\ft ; also in verse 32\f* \rb and present|וְהִקְרַבְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb On this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |בְּעֶ֖צֶם\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb you are not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to do|תַעֲשׂ֔וּ\rb* \rb any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb work|מְלָאכָה֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb it|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is the Day|י֤וֹם\rb* \rb of Atonement|כִּפֻּרִים֙\rb*, \rb when atonement is made|לְכַפֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb for you|עֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb If|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb anyone|כָל־\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֙פֶשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb does not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb humble himself|תְעֻנֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb on this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |בְּעֶ֖צֶם\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb he must be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֖ה\rb* \rb from his people|מֵֽעַמֶּֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb I will destroy|וְהַֽאֲבַדְתִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַהִ֖וא\rb* \rb from among|מִקֶּ֥רֶב\rb* \rb his people|עַמָּֽהּ׃\rb* \rb anyone|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֗פֶשׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb does|תַּעֲשֶׂה֙\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb work|מְלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \rb on this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |בְּעֶ֖צֶם\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb You are not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to do|תַעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb work at all|מְלָאכָ֖ה\rb*. \rb This is a permanent|עוֹלָם֙\rb* \rb statute|חֻקַּ֤ת\rb* \rb for the generations to come|לְדֹרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb wherever|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb you live|מֹֽשְׁבֹֽתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb It|הוּא֙\rb* \rb will be a Sabbath|שַׁבַּ֨ת\rb* \rb of complete rest|שַׁבָּת֥וֹן\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and you shall humble|וְעִנִּיתֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb yourselves|נַפְשֹׁתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb From the evening|בָּעֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb of the ninth|בְּתִשְׁעָ֤ה\rb* \rb day of the month|לַחֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb*\rb |עֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb the following evening|מֵעֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb you are to keep|תִּשְׁבְּת֖וּ\rb* \rb your Sabbath|שַׁבַּתְּכֶֽם׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 The Feast of Tabernacles
\p \v 33 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 34 “\rb Speak|דַּבֵּ֛ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and say|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb On the fifteenth|בַּחֲמִשָּׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֜ר\rb* \rb day|י֗וֹם\rb* \rb of the|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִי֙\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֤דֶשׁ\rb* \rb the Feast|חַ֧ג\rb* \rb of Tabernacles|הַסֻּכּ֛וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 23:34 \ft That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; also translated as \fqa the Feast of Booths \ft or \fqa the Feast of Shelters \ft and originally called \fqa the Feast of Ingathering\ft (see Exodus 23:16 and Exodus 34:22).\f* \rb to the LORD begins|לַיהֹוָֽה׃\rb*, \rb and it continues for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb*. \v 35 \rb On the first|הָרִאשׁ֖וֹן\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb there shall be a sacred|קֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb assembly|מִקְרָא־\rb*. \rb You must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb do|תַעֲשֽׂוּ׃\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb regular work|מְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb*\rb |עֲבֹדָ֖ה\rb*. \v 36 \rb For seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb you are to present|תַּקְרִ֥יבוּ\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb On the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֡י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb you are to hold|יִהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb a sacred|קֹדֶשׁ֩\rb* \rb assembly|מִקְרָא־\rb* \rb and present|וְהִקְרַבְתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*. \rb It is|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb a solemn assembly|עֲצֶ֣רֶת\rb*; \rb you must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb do|תַעֲשֽׂוּ׃\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb regular work|מְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb*\rb |עֲבֹדָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb These|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb are the LORD’s|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb appointed feasts|מוֹעֲדֵ֣י\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you are to proclaim|תִּקְרְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb as sacred|קֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb assemblies|מִקְרָאֵ֣י\rb* \rb for presenting|לְהַקְרִ֨יב\rb* \rb food offerings|אִשֶּׁ֜ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֗ה\rb* — \rb burnt offerings|עֹלָ֧ה\rb* \rb and grain offerings|וּמִנְחָ֛ה\rb*, \rb sacrifices|זֶ֥בַח\rb* \rb and drink offerings|וּנְסָכִ֖ים\rb*, \rb each on|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb its designated|י֥וֹם\rb* \rb day|בְּיוֹמֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 38 \rb These offerings are in addition to|מִלְּבַ֖ד\rb* \rb the offerings for the LORD’s|יְּהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וּמִלְּבַ֣ד\rb* \rb Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתֹ֣ת\rb*, \rb and in addition to your gifts|מַתְּנֽוֹתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*,\rb |וּמִלְּבַ֤ד\rb* \rb to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your vow offerings|נִדְרֵיכֶם֙\rb*,\rb |וּמִלְּבַד֙\rb* \rb and to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the freewill offerings|נִדְב֣וֹתֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you give|תִּתְּנ֖וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 39 \rb |אַ֡ךְ\rb* \rb On the fifteenth|בַּחֲמִשָּׁה֩\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֨ר\rb* \rb day|י֜וֹם\rb* \rb of the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֗י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb after you have gathered|בְּאָסְפְּכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the produce|תְּבוּאַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb you are to celebrate|תָּחֹ֥גּוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a feast|חַג־\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֑ים\rb*. \rb There shall be complete rest|שַׁבָּת֔וֹן\rb* \rb on the first|הָֽרִאשׁוֹן֙\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb and also|שַׁבָּתֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb on the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֖י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 40 \rb On the first|הָרִאשׁ֗וֹן\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb you are to gather|וּלְקַחְתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb the fruit|פְּרִ֨י\rb* \rb of majestic|הָדָר֙\rb* \rb trees|עֵ֤ץ\rb*, \rb the branches|כַּפֹּ֣ת\rb* \rb of palm trees|תְּמָרִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and the boughs|וַעֲנַ֥ף\rb* \rb of leafy|עָבֹ֖ת\rb* \rb trees|עֵץ־\rb* \rb and of willows|וְעַרְבֵי־\rb*\f + \fr 23:40 \ft Or \fqa poplars\f* \rb of the brook|נָ֑חַל\rb*. \rb And you are to rejoice|וּשְׂמַחְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֛י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 41 \rb You are to celebrate|וְחַגֹּתֶ֤ם\rb* \rb this|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb as a feast|חַ֣ג\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb each year|בַּשָּׁנָ֑ה\rb*. \rb This is a permanent|עוֹלָם֙\rb* \rb statute|חֻקַּ֤ת\rb* \rb for the generations to come|לְדֹרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*; \rb you are to celebrate|תָּחֹ֥גּוּ\rb* \rb it|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb in the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֖י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*.
\p \v 42 \rb You are to dwell|תֵּשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb in booths|בַּסֻּכֹּ֥ת\rb*\f + \fr 23:42 \ft Or \fqa tabernacles \ft or \fqa shelters\ft ; twice in this verse, and also in verse 43; see the footnote for verse 34.\f* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֑ים\rb*. \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the native-born|הָֽאֶזְרָח֙\rb* \rb of Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb must dwell|יֵשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb in booths|בַּסֻּכֹּֽת׃\rb*, \v 43 \rb so that|לְמַעַן֮\rb* \rb your descendants|דֹרֹֽתֵיכֶם֒\rb* \rb may know|יֵדְע֣וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I made the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb dwell|הוֹשַׁ֙בְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in booths|בַסֻּכּ֗וֹת\rb* \rb when I brought them out|בְּהוֹצִיאִ֥י\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 44 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb announced|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb* \rb the appointed feasts|מֹעֲדֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*.
\c 24
\s1 The Oil for the Lamps
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Command|צַ֞ו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb to bring|וְיִקְח֨וּ\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb pure|זָ֛ךְ\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֣מֶן\rb* \rb of pressed|כָּתִ֖ית\rb* \rb olives|זַ֥יִת\rb* \rb for the light|לַמָּא֑וֹר\rb*, \rb to keep the lamps|נֵ֖ר\rb* \rb burning|לְהַעֲלֹ֥ת\rb* \rb continually|תָּמִֽיד׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Outside|מִחוּץ֩\rb* \rb the veil|לְפָרֹ֨כֶת\rb* \rb of the Testimony|הָעֵדֻ֜ת\rb*\f + \fr 24:3 \fqa The Testimony \ft refers to the stone tablets in the ark of the covenant inscribed with the Ten Commandments.\f* \rb in the Tent|בְּאֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֗ד\rb*, \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb* \rb is to tend|יַעֲרֹךְ֩\rb* \rb the lamps|אֹת֨וֹ\rb* \rb continually|תָּמִ֑יד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb from evening|מֵעֶ֧רֶב\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning|בֹּ֛קֶר\rb*. \rb This is to be a permanent|עוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb statute|חֻקַּ֥ת\rb* \rb for the generations to come|לְדֹרֹֽתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb He shall tend|יַעֲרֹ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the lamps|הַנֵּר֑וֹת\rb* \rb on|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the pure gold|הַטְּהֹרָ֔ה\rb* \rb lampstand|הַמְּנֹרָ֣ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb continually|תָּמִֽיד׃פ\rb*.
\s1 The Showbread
\p \v 5 \rb You are also to take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֣\rb* \rb fine flour|סֹ֔לֶת\rb* \rb and bake|וְאָפִיתָ֣\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁתֵּ֥ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb loaves|חַלּ֑וֹת\rb*, \rb using|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb two-tenths of an ephah|שְׁנֵי֙\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֹנִ֔ים\rb* \rb for each|הָאֶחָֽת׃\rb* \rb loaf|הַֽחַלָּ֥ה\rb*,\f + \fr 24:5 \fqa Two-tenths of an ephah \ft is approximately 4 dry quarts or 4.4 liters (probably about 5.1 pounds or 2.3 kilograms of flour).\f* \v 6 \rb and set|וְשַׂמְתָּ֥\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb in two|שְׁתַּ֥יִם\rb* \rb rows|מַֽעֲרָכ֖וֹת\rb* — \rb six|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb per row|הַֽמַּעֲרָ֑כֶת\rb* — \rb on|עַ֛ל\rb* \rb the table|הַשֻּׁלְחָ֥ן\rb* \rb of pure gold|הַטָּהֹ֖ר\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb And you are to place|וְנָתַתָּ֥\rb* \rb pure|זַכָּ֑ה\rb* \rb frankincense|לְבֹנָ֣ה\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb* \rb each row|הַֽמַּעֲרֶ֖כֶת\rb*, \rb so that it may serve|וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb as a memorial portion|לְאַזְכָּרָ֔ה\rb* \rb for the bread|לַלֶּ֙חֶם֙\rb*, \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Every Sabbath day|בְּי֨וֹם\rb*\rb |הַשַּׁבָּ֜ת\rb*\rb |בְּי֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַשַּׁבָּ֗ת\rb* \rb the bread is to be set out|יַֽעַרְכֶ֛נּוּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |תָּמִ֑יד\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb on behalf of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb as a permanent|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb covenant|בְּרִ֥ית\rb*. \v 9 \rb It belongs to|וְהָֽיְתָה֙\rb* \rb Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּלְבָנָ֔יו\rb*, \rb who are to eat|וַאֲכָלֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb it in a holy|קָדֹ֑שׁ\rb* \rb place|בְּמָק֣וֹם\rb*; \rb for|כִּ֡י\rb* \rb it is|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb to him|ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb a most|קֹדֶשׁ֩\rb* \rb holy part|קָֽדָשִׁ֨ים\rb* \rb of the food offerings|מֵאִשֵּׁ֥י\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* — \rb his portion|חָק־\rb* \rb forever|עוֹלָֽם׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 Punishment for Blasphemy
\p \v 10 \rb Now the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of an Israelite|יִשְׂרְאֵלִ֔ית\rb*\rb |וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb mother|אִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and an Egyptian|מִצְרִ֔י\rb* \rb father|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb among|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and a fight broke out|וַיִּנָּצוּ֙\rb* \rb in the camp|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb between him|בֶּ֚ן\rb*\rb |הַיִּשְׂרְאֵלִ֔ית\rb* \rb and an Israelite|הַיִּשְׂרְאֵלִֽי׃\rb*\rb |וְאִ֖ישׁ\rb*. \v 11 \rb The son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of the Israelite|הַיִּשְׂרְאֵלִ֤ית\rb* \rb woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֨ה\rb* \rb blasphemed|וַ֠יִּקֹּב\rb* \rb the Name|הַשֵּׁם֙\rb* \rb with a curse|וַיְקַלֵּ֔ל\rb*. \rb So they brought|וַיָּבִ֥יאוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb*. \rb (His mother’s|אִמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb was Shelomith|שְׁלֹמִ֥ית\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Dibri|דִּבְרִ֖י\rb*, \rb of the tribe|לְמַטֵּה־\rb* \rb of Dan|דָֽן׃\rb*.)
\p \v 12 \rb They placed him|וַיַּנִּיחֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in custody|בַּמִּשְׁמָ֑ר\rb* \rb until the will|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb should be made clear|לִפְרֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 14 “\rb Take|הוֹצֵ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the blasphemer|הַֽמְקַלֵּ֗ל\rb*\f + \fr 24:14 \ft Literally \fqa the one who cursed\ft ; also in verse 23\f*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb outside|מִחוּץ֙\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb*, \rb and have all|כָֽל־\rb* \rb who heard|הַשֹּׁמְעִ֛ים\rb* \rb him|אֶת־\rb* \rb lay|וְסָמְכ֧וּ\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb*; \rb then have the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|הָעֵדָֽה׃\rb* \rb stone|וְרָגְמ֥וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb And you are to tell|תְּדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, ‘\rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb anyone|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb curses|יְקַלֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָ֖יו\rb*, \rb he shall bear the consequences|וְנָשָׂ֥א\rb* \rb of his sin|חֶטְאֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Whoever blasphemes|וְנֹקֵ֤ב\rb* \rb the name|שֵׁם־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb must surely be put to death|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָ֔ת\rb*; \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|הָעֵדָ֑ה\rb* \rb must surely stone|רָג֥וֹם\rb*\rb |יִרְגְּמוּ־\rb* \rb him|ב֖וֹ\rb*, \rb whether he is a foreign resident|כַּגֵּר֙\rb* \rb or native|כָּֽאֶזְרָ֔ח\rb*; \rb if he blasphemes|בְּנָקְבוֹ־\rb* \rb the Name|שֵׁ֖ם\rb*, \rb he must be put to death|יוּמָֽת׃\rb*.
\s1 An Eye for an Eye
\p \v 17 \rb And if|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb a man|וְאִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb takes the life|יַכֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb of anyone else|כָּל־\rb*\rb |נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אָדָ֑ם\rb*, \rb he must surely be put to death|מ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָֽת׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb Whoever kills|וּמַכֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb an animal|בְּהֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb must make restitution|יְשַׁלְּמֶ֑נָּה\rb* — \rb life|נֶֽפֶשׁ־\rb* \rb for|תַּ֥חַת\rb*\rb |נָֽפֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb life|נֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb*. \v 19 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb anyone|וְאִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb injures|יִתֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |מ֖וּם\rb* \rb his neighbor|בַּעֲמִית֑וֹ\rb*, \rb whatever|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he has done|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb must be done|יֵעָ֥שֶׂה\rb* \rb to him|לּֽוֹ׃\rb*: \v 20 \rb fracture|שֶׁ֚בֶר\rb* \rb for|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb fracture|שֶׁ֔בֶר\rb*, \rb eye|עַ֚יִן\rb* \rb for|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb eye|עַ֔יִן\rb*, \rb tooth|שֵׁ֖ן\rb* \rb for|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb tooth|שֵׁ֑ן\rb*.\f + \fr 24:20 \ft Cited in Matthew 5:38\f* \rb Just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb he injured|יִתֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |מוּם֙\rb* \rb the other person|בָּֽאָדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb the same|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb must be inflicted|יִנָּ֥תֶן\rb* \rb on him|בּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Whoever kills|וּמַכֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb an animal|בְהֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb must make restitution|יְשַׁלְּמֶ֑נָּה\rb*, \rb but whoever kills|וּמַכֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb a man|אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb must be put to death|יוּמָֽת׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb You are to have|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the same|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb standard of law|מִשְׁפַּ֤ט\rb* \rb for the foreign resident|כַּגֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb and the native|כָּאֶזְרָ֖ח\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֑ה\rb*; \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 23 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁה֮\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb*, \rb and they took|וַיּוֹצִ֣יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the blasphemer|הַֽמְקַלֵּ֗ל\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb outside|מִחוּץ֙\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and stoned|וַיִּרְגְּמ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb him|אָ֑בֶן\rb*. \rb So the Israelites|וּבְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb did|עָשׂ֔וּ\rb* \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃פ\rb*.
\c 25
\s1 The Seventh Year
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb Sinai|סִינַ֖י\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Speak|דַּבֵּ֞ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and say to them|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb*: \rb When|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you enter|תָבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am giving|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb the land itself|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb must observe|וְשָׁבְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb a Sabbath|שַׁבָּ֖ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb For six|שֵׁ֤שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִים֙\rb* \rb you may sow|תִּזְרַ֣ע\rb* \rb your field|שָׂדֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and prune|תִּזְמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb your vineyard|כַּרְמֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb and gather|וְאָסַפְתָּ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its crops|תְּבוּאָתָֽהּ׃\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖ים\rb*. \v 4 \rb But in the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֗ת\rb* \rb year|וּבַשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb there shall be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb a Sabbath|שַׁבַּ֤ת\rb* \rb of complete rest|שַׁבָּתוֹן֙\rb* \rb for the land|לָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* — \rb a Sabbath|שַׁבָּ֖ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*.
\p \rb You are not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to sow|תִזְרָ֔ע\rb* \rb your field|שָֽׂדְךָ֙\rb* \rb or prune|תִזְמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb your vineyard|וְכַרְמְךָ֖\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb*. \v 5 \rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb You are not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to reap|תִקְצ֔וֹר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the aftergrowth|סְפִ֤יחַ\rb* \rb of your harvest|קְצִֽירְךָ֙\rb* \rb or gather|תִבְצֹ֑ר\rb* \rb the grapes|עִנְּבֵ֥י\rb* \rb of your untended vines|נְזִירֶ֖ךָ\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb*. \rb The land|לָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb must have|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a year|שְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of complete rest|שַׁבָּת֖וֹן\rb*. \v 6 \rb Whatever the land|הָאָ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb yields|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb during the Sabbath year|שַׁבַּ֨ת\rb* \rb shall be|וְ֠הָיְתָה\rb* \rb food for you|לְאָכְלָ֔ה\rb*— \rb for yourself|לְךָ֖\rb*, \rb your manservant|וּלְעַבְדְּךָ֣\rb* \rb and maidservant|וְלַאֲמָתֶ֑ךָ\rb*, \rb the hired hand|וְלִשְׂכִֽירְךָ֙\rb* \rb or foreigner|וּלְתוֹשָׁ֣בְךָ֔\rb* \rb who stays|הַגָּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*, \v 7 \rb and for your livestock|וְלִ֨בְהֶמְתְּךָ֔\rb* \rb and the wild animals|וְלַֽחַיָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in your land|בְּאַרְצֶ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb All|כָל־\rb* \rb its growth|תְּבוּאָתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb may serve|תִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb as food|לֶאֱכֹֽל׃ס\rb*.
\s1 The Year of Jubilee
\p \v 8 \rb And you|לְךָ֗\rb* \rb shall count off|וְסָפַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֚בַע\rb* \rb Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb* — \rb seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וְהָי֣וּ\rb*\rb |לְךָ֗\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* —\rb |יְמֵי֙\rb* \rb so that the seven|שֶׁ֚בַע\rb* \rb Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of years|הַשָּׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb amount to forty-nine|וְאַרְבָּעִ֖ים\rb*\rb |תֵּ֥שַׁע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Then you are to sound|וְהַֽעֲבַרְתָּ֞\rb* \rb the horn|שׁוֹפַ֤ר\rb* \rb far and wide|תְּרוּעָה֙\rb* \rb on the tenth day|בֶּעָשׂ֖וֹר\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the seventh|הַשְּׁבִעִ֔י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the Day|בְּיוֹם֙\rb* \rb of Atonement|הַכִּפֻּרִ֔ים\rb*. \rb You shall sound|תַּעֲבִ֥ירוּ\rb* \rb it|שׁוֹפָ֖ר\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your land|אַרְצְכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb So you are to consecrate|וְקִדַּשְׁתֶּ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the fiftieth|הַחֲמִשִּׁים֙\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb year|שְׁנַ֤ת\rb* \rb and proclaim|וּקְרָאתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb liberty|דְּר֛וֹר\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb its inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֶ֑יהָ\rb*. \rb It|הִוא֙\rb* \rb shall be|תִּהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb Jubilee|יוֹבֵ֥ל\rb*, \rb when each|אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb of you is to return|וְשַׁבְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his property|אֲחֻזָּת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and|וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his clan|מִשְׁפַּחְתּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |תָּשֻֽׁבוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb The fiftieth|הַחֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb year|שְׁנַ֛ת\rb* \rb will be|תִּהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb a Jubilee|יוֹבֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |הִ֗וא\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֑ם\rb*; \rb you are not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to sow the land|תִזְרָ֔עוּ\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb reap|תִקְצְרוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its aftergrowth|סְפִיחֶ֔יהָ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or harvest|תִבְצְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the untended vines|נְזִרֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb it is|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb a Jubilee|יוֹבֵ֣ל\rb*; \rb it shall be|תִּהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb holy|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb You may eat only|תֹּאכְל֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the crops taken|תְּבוּאָתָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb directly from|מִן־\rb* \rb the field|הַ֨שָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb*.
\s1 Return of Property
\p \v 13 \rb In this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb Year|בִּשְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Jubilee|הַיּוֹבֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb each|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb of you shall return|תָּשֻׁ֕בוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his own property|אֲחֻזָּתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb you make a sale|תִמְכְּר֤וּ\rb*\rb |מִמְכָּר֙\rb* \rb to your neighbor|לַעֲמִיתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb a purchase|קָנֹ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb him|עֲמִיתֶ֑ךָ\rb*, \rb you must not|אַל־\rb* \rb take advantage|תּוֹנ֖וּ\rb* \rb of each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb other|אָחִֽיו׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb You are to buy|תִּקְנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb your neighbor|עֲמִיתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb according to the number|בְּמִסְפַּ֤ר\rb* \rb of years|שָׁנִים֙\rb* \rb since|אַחַ֣ר\rb* \rb the last Jubilee|הַיּוֹבֵ֔ל\rb*; \rb he is to sell|יִמְכָּר־\rb* \rb to you|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb according to the number|בְּמִסְפַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of harvest|תְבוּאֹ֖ת\rb* \rb years remaining|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb*. \v 16 \rb You shall increase|תַּרְבֶּה֙\rb* \rb the price|מִקְנָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb in proportion|לְפִ֣י׀\rb* \rb to a greater number|רֹ֣ב\rb* \rb of years|הַשָּׁנִ֗ים\rb*, \rb or decrease|מְעֹ֣ט\rb* \rb it|מִקְנָת֑וֹ\rb* \rb in proportion to|וּלְפִי֙\rb* \rb a lesser|תַּמְעִ֖יט\rb* \rb number of years|הַשָּׁנִ֔ים\rb*; \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb is selling|מֹכֵ֖ר\rb* \rb you|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb a given number of|מִסְפַּ֣ר\rb* \rb harvests|תְּבוּאֹ֔ת\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Do not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb take advantage|תוֹנוּ֙\rb* \rb of each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb other|עֲמִית֔וֹ\rb*, \rb but fear|וְיָרֵ֖אתָ\rb* \rb your God|מֵֽאֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb*; \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהֹוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\s1 The Blessing of Obedience
\p \v 18 \rb You are to keep|וַעֲשִׂיתֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקֹּתַ֔י\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb carefully|תִּשְׁמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb observe|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb My judgments|מִשְׁפָּטַ֥י\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb so that you may dwell|וִֽישַׁבְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb securely|לָבֶֽטַח׃\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*. \v 19 \rb Then the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb will yield|וְנָתְנָ֤ה\rb* \rb its fruit|פִּרְיָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb so that you can eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb your fill|לָשֹׂ֑בַע\rb* \rb and dwell|וִֽישַׁבְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb in safety|לָבֶ֖טַח\rb* \rb in the land|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Now|וְכִ֣י\rb* \rb you may wonder|תֹאמְר֔וּ\rb*, ‘\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb will we eat|נֹּאכַ֤֖ל\rb* \rb in the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֑ת\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb if|הֵ֚ן\rb* \rb we do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb sow|נִזְרָ֔ע\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or gather|נֶאֱסֹ֖ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our produce|תְּבוּאָתֵֽנוּ׃\rb*?’ \v 21 \rb But I will send|וְצִוִּ֤יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My blessing|בִּרְכָתִי֙\rb* \rb upon you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb in the sixth|הַשִּׁשִּׁ֑ית\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֖ה\rb*, \rb so that the land will yield|וְעָשָׂת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a crop|הַתְּבוּאָ֔ה\rb* \rb sufficient for three|לִשְׁלֹ֖שׁ\rb* \rb years|הַשָּׁנִֽים׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb While you are sowing|וּזְרַעְתֶּ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb in the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֔ת\rb* \rb year|הַשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb*, \rb you will be eating|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the previous|יָשָׁ֑ן\rb* \rb harvest|הַתְּבוּאָ֣ה\rb*,\rb |תֹּאכְל֖וּ\rb*\rb |יָשָֽׁן׃\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד׀\rb* \rb the ninth|הַתְּשִׁיעִ֗ת\rb* \rb year’s|הַשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb harvest|תְּב֣וּאָתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb comes in|בּוֹא֙\rb*.
\s1 The Law of Redemption
\p \v 23 \rb The land|וְהָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb must not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb be sold|תִמָּכֵר֙\rb* \rb permanently|לִצְמִתֻ֔ת\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb it|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb is Mine|לִ֖י\rb*, \rb and|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb are but foreigners|גֵרִ֧ים\rb* \rb and residents|וְתוֹשָׁבִ֛ים\rb* \rb with Me|עִמָּדִֽי׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb Thus for every|וּבְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb piece of property|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb you possess|אֲחֻזַּתְכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb you must provide for|תִּתְּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb the redemption|גְּאֻלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb of the land|לָאָֽרֶץ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb becomes impoverished|יָמ֣וּךְ\rb* \rb and sells|וּמָכַ֖ר\rb* \rb some of his property|מֵאֲחֻזָּת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb his nearest|הַקָּרֹ֣ב\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb of kin|גֹֽאֲלוֹ֙\rb* \rb may come|וּבָ֤א\rb* \rb and redeem|וְגָאַ֕ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb what his brother|אָחִֽיו׃\rb* \rb has sold|מִמְכַּ֥ר\rb*. \v 26 \rb Or if|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb a man|וְאִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb has|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb no one|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to redeem it|גֹּאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb for him|לּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb but he prospers|וְהִשִּׂ֣יגָה\rb*\rb |יָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb and acquires|וּמָצָ֖א\rb* \rb enough|כְּדֵ֥י\rb* \rb to redeem his land|גְאֻלָּתֽוֹ׃\rb*, \v 27 \rb he shall calculate|וְחִשַּׁב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the years|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb since its sale|מִמְכָּר֔וֹ\rb*, \rb repay|וְהֵשִׁיב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the balance|הָ֣עֹדֵ֔ף\rb* \rb to the man|לָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb to|ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he sold it|מָֽכַר־\rb*, \rb and return|וְשָׁ֖ב\rb* \rb to his property|לַאֲחֻזָּתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb But if|וְאִ֨ם\rb* \rb he cannot|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb obtain|מָֽצְאָ֜ה\rb*\rb |יָד֗וֹ\rb* \rb enough|דֵּי֮\rb* \rb to repay|הָשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֒\rb*, \rb what he sold|מִמְכָּר֗וֹ\rb* \rb will remain|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb in possession|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb of the buyer|הַקֹּנֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the Year|שְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Jubilee|הַיּוֹבֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb In the Jubilee|בַּיֹּבֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb however, it is to be released|וְיָצָא֙\rb*, \rb so that he may return|וְשָׁ֖ב\rb* \rb to his property|לַאֲחֻזָּתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|וְאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb sells|יִמְכֹּ֤ר\rb* \rb a house|בֵּית־\rb*\rb |מוֹשַׁב֙\rb* \rb in a walled|חוֹמָ֔ה\rb* \rb city|עִ֣יר\rb*, \rb he retains|וְהָיְתָה֙\rb* \rb his right of redemption|גְּאֻלָּת֔וֹ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb a full|תֹּ֖ם\rb* \rb year|שְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb after its sale|מִמְכָּר֑וֹ\rb*; \rb during that year|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb it may be|תִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb redeemed|גְאֻלָּתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb If|וְאִ֣ם\rb* \rb it is not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb redeemed|יִגָּאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb by the end|עַד־\rb*\rb |מְלֹ֣את\rb* \rb of|לוֹ֮\rb* \rb a full|תְמִימָה֒\rb*\rb |וְ֠קָם\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֣ה\rb*, \rb then the house|הַבַּ֨יִת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the walled|חֹמָ֗ה\rb* \rb city|בָּעִ֜יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |לֹא\rb* \rb is permanently|לַצְּמִיתֻ֛ת\rb* \rb transferred to its buyer|לַקֹּנֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb and his descendants|לְדֹרֹתָ֑יו\rb*. \rb It is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to be released|יֵצֵ֖א\rb* \rb in the Jubilee|בַּיֹּבֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb But houses|וּבָתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb in villages|הַחֲצֵרִ֗ים\rb* \rb with|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb no|אֵין־\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb walls|חֹמָה֙\rb* \rb around them|סָבִ֔יב\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb are to be considered|יֵחָשֵׁ֑ב\rb* \rb as open fields|שְׂדֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*. \rb They may be redeemed|גְּאֻלָּה֙\rb*, \rb and they shall be|תִּהְיֶה־\rb* \rb released|יֵצֵֽא׃\rb* \rb in the Jubilee|וּבַיֹּבֵ֖ל\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb As for the cities|וְעָרֵי֙\rb* \rb of the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb*, \rb the Levites|לַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb* \rb always|עוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb have|תִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the right to redeem|גְּאֻלַּ֥ת\rb* \rb their houses|בָּתֵּ֖י\rb* \rb in the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb they possess|אֲחֻזָּתָ֑ם\rb*. \v 33 \rb So whatever|וַאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb belongs to|מִן־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb may be redeemed|יִגְאַל֙\rb*— \rb a house|בַּ֛יִת\rb* \rb sold|מִמְכַּר־\rb* \rb in a city|וְעִ֥יר\rb* \rb they possess|אֲחֻזָּת֖וֹ\rb*— \rb and must be released|וְיָצָ֧א\rb* \rb in the Jubilee|בַּיֹּבֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the houses|בָתֵּ֞י\rb*\rb |הִ֚וא\rb* \rb in the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb* \rb are their possession|אֲחֻזָּתָ֔ם\rb* \rb among|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 34 \rb But the open|וּֽשְׂדֵ֛ה\rb* \rb pastureland|מִגְרַ֥שׁ\rb* \rb around their cities|עָרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb may not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be sold|יִמָּכֵ֑ר\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is their|לָהֶֽם׃ס\rb* \rb permanent|עוֹלָ֛ם\rb* \rb possession|אֲחֻזַּ֥ת\rb*.
\s1 Redemption of the Poor
\p \v 35 \rb Now if|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb your countryman|אָחִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb becomes destitute|יָמ֣וּךְ\rb* \rb and cannot support himself|וּמָ֥טָה\rb*\rb |יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb among you|עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb then you are to help|וְהֶֽחֱזַ֣קְתָּ\rb* \rb him|בּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb as you would a foreigner|גֵּ֧ר\rb* \rb or stranger|וְתוֹשָׁ֛ב\rb*, \rb so that he can continue to live|וָחַ֖י\rb* \rb among you|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 36 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb take|תִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb any interest|נֶ֣שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb or profit|וְתַרְבִּ֔ית\rb* \rb from him|מֵֽאִתּוֹ֙\rb*, \rb but fear|וְיָרֵ֖אתָ\rb* \rb your God|מֵֽאֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb that your countryman|אָחִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb may live|וְחֵ֥י\rb* \rb among you|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 37 \rb You must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb lend|תִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb him|אֶ֨ת־\rb* \rb your silver|כַּסְפְּךָ֔\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb at interest|בְּנֶ֑שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb or|לֹא־\rb* \rb sell him|תִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb your food|אָכְלֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb for profit|וּבְמַרְבִּ֖ית\rb*. \v 38 \rb I|אֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹ֣הֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb brought you|הוֹצֵ֥אתִי\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb to give|לָתֵ֤ת\rb* \rb you|לָכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb* \rb and to be|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God|לֵאלֹהִֽים׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Redemption of Bondmen
\p \v 39 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a countryman|אָחִ֛יךָ\rb* \rb among you|עִמָּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb becomes destitute|יָמ֥וּךְ\rb* \rb and sells himself|וְנִמְכַּר־\rb* \rb to you|לָ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb then you must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb force him|תַעֲבֹ֥ד\rb* \rb into|בּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb slave|עָֽבֶד׃\rb* \rb labor|עֲבֹ֥דַת\rb*. \v 40 \rb Let him stay|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb as a hired worker|כְּשָׂכִ֥יר\rb* \rb or temporary resident|כְּתוֹשָׁ֖ב\rb*; \rb he is to work|יַעֲבֹ֥ד\rb* \rb for|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb* \rb you until|עַד־\rb* \rb the Year|שְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Jubilee|הַיֹּבֵ֖ל\rb*. \v 41 \rb Then he|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb and his children|וּבָנָ֣יו\rb*\rb |עִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb are to be released|וְיָצָא֙\rb*\rb |מֵֽעִמָּ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb and he may return|וְשָׁב֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his clan|מִשְׁפַּחְתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |יָשֽׁוּב׃\rb* \rb the property|אֲחֻזַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֖יו\rb*.
\p \v 42 \rb Because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Israelites are|הֵ֔ם\rb* \rb My servants|עֲבָדַ֣י\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I brought|הוֹצֵ֥אתִי\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb they are not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to be sold|יִמָּכְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |מִמְכֶּ֥רֶת\rb* \rb as slaves|עָֽבֶד׃\rb*. \v 43 \rb You are not|לֹא־\rb* \rb to rule|תִרְדֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb over them|ב֖וֹ\rb* \rb harshly|בְּפָ֑רֶךְ\rb*, \rb but you shall fear|וְיָרֵ֖אתָ\rb* \rb your God|מֵאֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 44 \rb Your menservants|וְעַבְדְּךָ֥\rb* \rb and maidservants|וַאֲמָתְךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb shall come|יִהְיוּ־\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb around you|סְבִיבֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb from whom|מֵהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb you may purchase|תִּקְנ֖וּ\rb* \rb them|עֶ֥בֶד\rb*\rb |וְאָמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 45 \rb You may also|וְ֠גַם\rb* \rb purchase them|תִּקְנ֔וּ\rb* \rb from the|מִבְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb foreigners|הַתּוֹשָׁבִ֜ים\rb* \rb residing|הַגָּרִ֤ים\rb* \rb among you|עִמָּכֶם֙\rb*\rb |מֵהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb or their clans|וּמִמִּשְׁפַּחְתָּם֙\rb* \rb living among you|עִמָּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb are born|הוֹלִ֖ידוּ\rb* \rb in your land|בְּאַרְצְכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb These may become|וְהָי֥וּ\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb property|לַֽאֲחֻזָּֽה׃\rb*. \v 46 \rb You may leave|וְהִתְנַחֲלְתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb to your sons|לִבְנֵיכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb you to inherit|לָרֶ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb as property|אֲחֻזָּ֔ה\rb*; \rb you can make them slaves|תַּעֲבֹ֑דוּ\rb* \rb for life|לְעֹלָ֖ם\rb*. \rb But as for your brothers|וּבְאַ֨חֵיכֶ֤ם\rb*, \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb may rule|תִרְדֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb harshly|בְּפָֽרֶךְ׃ס\rb* \rb over his brother|בְּאָחִ֔יו\rb*.
\s1 Redemption of Servants
\p \v 47 \rb If|וְכִ֣י\rb* \rb a foreigner|גֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb residing|וְתוֹשָׁב֙\rb* \rb among you|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb prospers|תַשִּׂ֗יג\rb*\rb |יַ֣ד\rb*, \rb but your countryman|אָחִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb dwelling near him|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb becomes destitute|וּמָ֥ךְ\rb* \rb and sells himself|וְנִמְכַּ֗ר\rb* \rb to the foreigner|לְגֵ֤ר\rb*\rb |תּוֹשָׁב֙\rb*\rb |עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb to a member|לְעֵ֖קֶר\rb* \rb of his|גֵּֽר׃\rb* \rb clan|מִשְׁפַּ֥חַת\rb*, \v 48 \rb he retains|תִּהְיֶה־\rb* \rb the right of redemption|גְּאֻלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb he has sold himself|נִמְכַּ֔ר\rb*. \rb One|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb of his brothers|מֵאֶחָ֖יו\rb* \rb may redeem him|יִגְאָלֶֽנּוּ׃\rb*: \v 49 \rb either|אוֹ־\rb* \rb his uncle|דֹד֞וֹ\rb* \rb or|א֤וֹ\rb* \rb cousin|בֶן־\rb*\rb |דֹּדוֹ֙\rb*\rb |יִגְאָלֶ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb any close relative|מִשְּׁאֵ֧ר\rb*\rb |בְּשָׂר֛וֹ\rb* \rb from his clan|מִמִּשְׁפַּחְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb may redeem him|יִגְאָלֶ֑נּוּ\rb*. \rb Or if|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb he prospers|הִשִּׂ֥יגָה\rb*\rb |יָד֖וֹ\rb*, \rb he may redeem himself|וְנִגְאָֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 50 \rb He and|עִם־\rb* \rb his purchaser|קֹנֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb will then count the time|וְחִשַּׁב֙\rb* \rb from the year|מִשְּׁנַת֙\rb* \rb he sold|הִמָּ֣כְרוֹ\rb* \rb himself|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb up to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the Year|שְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Jubilee|הַיֹּבֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb The price|כֶּ֤סֶף\rb* \rb of his sale|מִמְכָּרוֹ֙\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb determined by the number|בְּמִסְפַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb based on|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb the daily|כִּימֵ֥י\rb* \rb wages of a hired hand|שָׂכִ֖יר\rb*. \v 51 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb many|רַבּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb years|בַּשָּׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb remain|ע֥וֹד\rb*, \rb he must pay|יָשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb for his redemption|גְּאֻלָּת֔וֹ\rb* \rb in proportion to|לְפִיהֶן֙\rb* \rb his purchase|מִקְנָתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb price|מִכֶּ֖סֶף\rb*. \v 52 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb only a few|מְעַ֞ט\rb* \rb years|בַּשָּׁנִ֛ים\rb* \rb remain|נִשְׁאַ֧ר\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the Year|שְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Jubilee|הַיֹּבֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb he is to calculate|וְחִשַּׁב־\rb*\rb |ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb and pay|יָשִׁ֖יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his redemption|גְּאֻלָּתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb according to|כְּפִ֣י\rb* \rb his remaining years|שָׁנָ֔יו\rb*. \v 53 \rb He shall be treated|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |עִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb like a man hired|כִּשְׂכִ֥יר\rb* \rb from year|שָׁנָ֛ה\rb* \rb to year|בְּשָׁנָ֖ה\rb*, \rb but a foreign owner must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb rule over him|יִרְדֶּ֥נּֽוּ\rb* \rb harshly|בְּפֶ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb in your sight|לְעֵינֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 54 \rb Even if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb he is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb redeemed|יִגָּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb in any of these ways|בְּאֵ֑לֶּה\rb*, \rb he|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb and his children|וּבָנָ֥יו\rb*\rb |עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb shall be released|וְיָצָא֙\rb* \rb in the Year|בִּשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Jubilee|הַיֹּבֵ֔ל\rb*. \v 55 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb are My|לִ֤י\rb* \rb servants|עֲבָדִ֔ים\rb*. \rb They|הֵ֔ם\rb* \rb are My servants|עֲבָדַ֣י\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I brought|הוֹצֵ֥אתִי\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.[’’]
\c 26
\s1 Additional Blessings of Obedience
\p \v 1 “\rb You must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb make|תַעֲשׂ֨וּ\rb* \rb idols|אֱלִילִ֗ם\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb or set up|תָקִ֣ימוּ\rb* \rb a carved image|וּפֶ֤סֶל\rb* \rb or sacred pillar|וּמַצֵּבָה֙\rb*; \rb you must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb place|תִתְּנוּ֙\rb* \rb a sculpted|מַשְׂכִּ֗ית\rb*\rb |לֹ֤א\rb* \rb stone|וְאֶ֣בֶן\rb* \rb in your land|בְּאַרְצְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to bow down|לְהִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֺ֖ת\rb* \rb to it|עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb You must keep|תִּשְׁמֹ֔רוּ\rb* \rb My Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתֹתַ֣י\rb* \rb and have reverence for|תִּירָ֑אוּ\rb* \rb My sanctuary|וּמִקְדָּשִׁ֖י\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you follow|תֵּלֵ֑כוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb My statutes|בְּחֻקֹּתַ֖י\rb* \rb and carefully keep|תִּשְׁמְר֔וּ\rb*\rb |וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb My commandments|מִצְוֺתַ֣י\rb*, \v 4 \rb I will give|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb you rains|גִשְׁמֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in their season|בְּעִתָּ֑ם\rb*, \rb and the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb will yield|וְנָתְנָ֤ה\rb* \rb its produce|יְבוּלָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb and the trees|וְעֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb will bear|יִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb their fruit|פִּרְיֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Your|לָכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb threshing|דַּ֙יִשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will continue|וְהִשִּׂ֨יג\rb* \rb until the grape harvest|בָּצִ֔יר\rb*, \rb and the grape harvest|וּבָצִ֖יר\rb* \rb will continue|יַשִּׂ֣יג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb until sowing time|זָ֑רַע\rb*; \rb you will have your fill of|לָשֹׂ֔בַע\rb* \rb food|לַחְמְכֶם֙\rb* \rb to eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb and will dwell|וִֽישַׁבְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb securely|לָבֶ֖טַח\rb* \rb in your land|בְּאַרְצְכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb And I will give|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb peace|שָׁלוֹם֙\rb* \rb to the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb and you will lie down|וּשְׁכַבְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb with nothing|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb to fear|מַחֲרִ֑יד\rb*. \rb I will rid|וְהִשְׁבַּתִּ֞י\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb of dangerous|רָעָה֙\rb* \rb animals|חַיָּ֤ה\rb*, \rb and no|לֹא־\rb* \rb sword|וְחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb will pass|תַעֲבֹ֥ר\rb* \rb through your land|בְּאַרְצְכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb You will pursue|וּרְדַפְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your enemies|אֹיְבֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and they will fall|וְנָפְל֥וּ\rb* \rb by the sword|לֶחָֽרֶב\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 8 \rb Five|חֲמִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb of you|מִכֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb will pursue|וְרָדְפ֨וּ\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵאָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and a hundred|וּמֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb of you|מִכֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb will pursue|יִרְדֹּ֑פוּ\rb* \rb ten thousand|רְבָבָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and your enemies|אֹיְבֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb will fall|וְנָפְל֧וּ\rb* \rb by the sword|לֶחָֽרֶב׃\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb I will turn|וּפָנִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb toward you|אֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and make you fruitful|וְהִפְרֵיתִ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and multiply|וְהִרְבֵּיתִ֖י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and I will establish|וַהֲקִימֹתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֖י\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb You will still be eating|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb the old|יָשָׁ֖ן\rb* \rb supply of grain|נוֹשָׁ֑ן\rb*\rb |וְיָשָׁ֕ן\rb* \rb when you need to clear it out|תּוֹצִֽיאוּ׃\rb* \rb to make room for|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the new|חָדָ֖שׁ\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb And I will make|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb My dwelling place|מִשְׁכָּנִ֖י\rb*\f + \fr 26:11 \ft Or \fqa My tabernacle\f* \rb among you|בְּתוֹכְכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and My soul|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb despise|תִגְעַ֥ל\rb*\f + \fr 26:11 \ft Or \fqa reject\ft ; also in verse 30\f* \rb you|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb I will walk|וְהִתְהַלַּכְתִּי֙\rb* \rb among you|בְּת֣וֹכְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and be|וְהָיִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God|לֵֽאלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and you|וְאַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb will be|תִּהְיוּ־\rb* \rb My|לִ֥י\rb* \rb people|לְעָֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 26:12 \ft Cited in 2 Corinthians 6:16\f* \v 13 \rb I|אֲנִ֞י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb brought|הוֹצֵ֤אתִי\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb so that you would no longer be|מִֽהְיֹ֥ת\rb* \rb slaves|עֲבָדִ֑ים\rb* \rb to the Egyptians|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*. \rb I broke|וָאֶשְׁבֹּר֙\rb* \rb the bars|מֹטֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of your yoke|עֻלְּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and enabled you to walk|וָאוֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in uprightness|קֽוֹמְמִיּֽוּת׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Punishments for Disobedience
\p \v 14 \rb If, however|וְאִם־\rb*, \rb you fail|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to obey|תִשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb Me|לִ֑י\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb and to carry out|תַעֲשׂ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb commandments|הַמִּצְוֺ֖ת\rb*, \v 15 \rb and if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you reject|תִּמְאָ֔סוּ\rb*\rb |וְאִ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My statutes|בְּחֻקֹּתַ֣י\rb*, \rb despise|תִּגְעַ֣ל\rb*\rb |נַפְשְׁכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb My ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטַ֖י\rb*, \rb and neglect|לְבִלְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb to carry out|עֲשׂוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My commandments|מִצְוֺתַ֔י\rb*, \rb and so break|לְהַפְרְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִֽי׃\rb*, \v 16 \rb then|אַף־\rb* \rb this is what|זֹּ֣את\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֞י\rb* \rb will do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֗ם\rb*: \rb I will bring|וְהִפְקַדְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb upon you|עֲלֵיכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb sudden terror|בֶּֽהָלָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb wasting disease|הַשַּׁחֶ֣פֶת\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb fever|הַקַּדַּ֔חַת\rb* \rb that will destroy|מְכַלּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb your sight|עֵינַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and drain|וּמְדִיבֹ֣ת\rb* \rb your life|נָ֑פֶשׁ\rb*. \rb You will sow|וּזְרַעְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb your seed|זַרְעֲכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb in vain|לָרִיק֙\rb*, \rb because your enemies|אֹיְבֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb will eat it|וַאֲכָלֻ֖הוּ\rb*. \v 17 \rb And I will set|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb My face|פָנַי֙\rb* \rb against you|בָּכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb so that you will be defeated|וְנִגַּפְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb by|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb your enemies|אֹיְבֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Those who hate you|שֹֽׂנְאֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb will rule|וְרָד֤וּ\rb* \rb over you|בָכֶם֙\rb*, \rb and you will flee|וְנַסְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb when no one|וְאֵין־\rb* \rb pursues|רֹדֵ֥ף\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb And if|וְאִ֨ם־\rb* \rb after|עַד־\rb* \rb all this|אֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb you will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb obey|תִשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb Me|לִ֑י\rb*, \rb I will proceed|וְיָסַפְתִּי֙\rb* \rb to punish|לְיַסְּרָ֣ה\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb sevenfold|שֶׁ֖בַע\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb your sins|חַטֹּאתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb I will break down|וְשָׁבַרְתִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your stubborn|עֻזְּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb pride|גְּא֣וֹן\rb* \rb and make|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your sky|שְׁמֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb like iron|כַּבַּרְזֶ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and your land|אַרְצְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb like bronze|כַּנְּחֻשָֽׁה׃\rb*, \v 20 \rb and your strength|כֹּחֲכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb will be spent|וְתַ֥ם\rb* \rb in vain|לָרִ֖יק\rb*. \rb For your land|אַרְצְכֶם֙\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb yield|תִתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb its|אֶת־\rb* \rb produce|יְבוּלָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb and the trees|וְעֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb bear|יִתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb their fruit|פִּרְיֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you walk|תֵּֽלְכ֤וּ\rb* \rb in hostility|קֶ֔רִי\rb* \rb toward Me|עִמִּי֙\rb* \rb and refuse|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |תֹאב֖וּ\rb* \rb to obey|לִשְׁמֹ֣עַֽ\rb* \rb Me|לִ֑י\rb*, \rb I will multiply|וְיָסַפְתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb your plagues|מַכָּ֔ה\rb* \rb seven times|שֶׁ֖בַע\rb*, \rb according to your sins|כְּחַטֹּאתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb I will send|וְהִשְׁלַחְתִּ֨י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb wild|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb* \rb animals|חַיַּ֤ת\rb* \rb against you|בָכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb to rob you of your children|וְשִׁכְּלָ֣ה\rb*,\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb destroy|וְהִכְרִ֙יתָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your livestock|בְּהֶמְתְּכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and reduce|וְהִמְעִ֖יטָה\rb* \rb your numbers|אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb until your roads|דַּרְכֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb lie desolate|וְנָשַׁ֖מּוּ\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb And if|וְאִ֨ם־\rb* \rb in spite of these|בְּאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb things you do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb accept My discipline|תִוָּסְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |לִ֑י\rb*, \rb but continue to walk|וַהֲלַכְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb in hostility|קֶֽרִי׃\rb* \rb toward Me|עִמִּ֖י\rb*, \v 24 \rb then I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb will act|וְהָלַכְתִּ֧י\rb*\rb |אַף־\rb* \rb with hostility|בְּקֶ֑רִי\rb* \rb toward you|עִמָּכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb I|אָ֔נִי\rb* \rb will strike|וְהִכֵּיתִ֤י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb sevenfold|שֶׁ֖בַע\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb your sins|חַטֹּאתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb And I will bring|וְהֵבֵאתִ֨י\rb* \rb a sword|חֶ֗רֶב\rb* \rb against you|עֲלֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb to execute|נֹקֶ֙מֶת֙\rb* \rb the vengeance|נְקַם־\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִ֔ית\rb*. \rb Though you withdraw|וְנֶאֱסַפְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb your cities|עָרֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb I will send|וְשִׁלַּ֤חְתִּי\rb* \rb a plague|דֶ֙בֶר֙\rb* \rb among you|בְּת֣וֹכְכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and you will be delivered|וְנִתַּתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of the enemy|אוֹיֵֽב׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb When I cut off|בְּשִׁבְרִ֣י\rb* \rb your|לָכֶם֮\rb* \rb supply|מַטֵּה־\rb*\f + \fr 26:26 \ft Hebrew \fqa staff\f* \rb of bread|לֶחֶם֒\rb*, \rb ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb women|נָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb will bake|וְ֠אָפוּ\rb* \rb your bread|לַחְמְכֶם֙\rb* \rb in a single|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb oven|בְּתַנּ֣וּר\rb* \rb and dole out|וְהֵשִׁ֥יבוּ\rb* \rb your bread|לַחְמְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb by weight|בַּמִּשְׁקָ֑ל\rb*, \rb so that you will eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb but not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb be satisfied|תִשְׂבָּֽעוּ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb But if|וְאִ֨ם־\rb* \rb in spite of all this|בְּזֹ֔את\rb* \rb you do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb obey|תִשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb Me|לִ֑י\rb*, \rb but continue to walk|וַהֲלַכְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb in hostility|בְּקֶֽרִי׃\rb* \rb toward Me|עִמִּ֖י\rb*, \v 28 \rb then I will walk|וְהָלַכְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb in fury|בַּחֲמַת־\rb* \rb against|קֶ֑רִי\rb* \rb you|עִמָּכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and I|אָ֔נִי\rb*, \rb even I|אַף־\rb*, \rb will punish|וְיִסַּרְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb sevenfold|שֶׁ֖בַע\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb your sins|חַטֹּאתֵיכֶם׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb You will eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb the flesh|בְּשַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of your own sons|בְּנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |תֹּאכֵֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb and|וּבְשַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb daughters|בְּנֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 30 \rb I will destroy|וְהִשְׁמַדְתִּ֞י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your high places|בָּמֹֽתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb cut down|וְהִכְרַתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your incense altars|חַמָּ֣נֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and heap|וְנָֽתַתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your lifeless bodies|פִּגְרֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the lifeless remains|פִּגְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of your idols|גִּלּוּלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*; \rb and My soul|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb will despise|וְגָעֲלָ֥ה\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb I will reduce|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your cities|עָֽרֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb to rubble|חָרְבָּ֔ה\rb* \rb and lay waste|וַהֲשִׁמּוֹתִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your sanctuaries|מִקְדְּשֵׁיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and I will refuse|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb to smell|אָרִ֔יחַ\rb* \rb the pleasing|נִיחֹֽחֲכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb aroma of your sacrifices|בְּרֵ֖יחַ\rb*. \v 32 \rb And I|אֲנִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will lay waste|וַהֲשִׁמֹּתִ֥י\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb so that your enemies|אֹֽיְבֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb who dwell|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in it|בָּֽהּ׃\rb* \rb will be appalled|וְשָֽׁמְמ֤וּ\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*. \v 33 \rb But|וְאֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb I will scatter|אֱזָרֶ֣ה\rb* \rb you among the nations|בַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb and will draw out|וַהֲרִיקֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb a sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb after you|אַחֲרֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb as your land|אַרְצְכֶם֙\rb* \rb becomes|וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb desolate|שְׁמָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb and your cities|וְעָרֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb are laid|יִהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb waste|חָרְבָּֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb Then|אָז֩\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb shall enjoy|תִּרְצֶ֨ה\rb* \rb its|אֶת־\rb* \rb Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתֹתֶ֗יהָ\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb it lies desolate|הֳשַׁמָּ֔ה\rb*, \rb while you|וְאַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb are in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of your enemies|אֹיְבֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb At that time|אָ֚ז\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb will rest|תִּשְׁבַּ֣ת\rb* \rb and enjoy|וְהִרְצָ֖ת\rb* \rb its|אֶת־\rb* \rb Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתֹתֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb As long as|כָּל־\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb it lies desolate|הָשַּׁמָּ֖ה\rb*, \rb the land will have the rest|תִּשְׁבֹּ֑ת\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb it did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb receive|שָׁבְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb during the Sabbaths|בְּשַׁבְּתֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb when you lived|בְּשִׁבְתְּכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb in it|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 36 \rb As for those of you who survive|וְהַנִּשְׁאָרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |בָּכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb I will send|וְהֵבֵ֤אתִי\rb* \rb a faintness|מֹ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb into their hearts|בִּלְבָבָ֔ם\rb* \rb in the lands|בְּאַרְצֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of their enemies|אֹיְבֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb so that even the sound|ק֚וֹל\rb* \rb of a windblown|נִדָּ֔ף\rb* \rb leaf|עָלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb will put them to flight|וְרָדַ֣ף\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֗ם\rb*. \rb And they will flee|וְנָס֧וּ\rb* \rb as one flees|מְנֻֽסַת־\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֛רֶב\rb*, \rb and fall|וְנָפְל֖וּ\rb* \rb when no one|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb pursues them|רֹדֵֽף׃\rb*. \v 37 \rb They will stumble|וְכָשְׁל֧וּ\rb* \rb over one|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb another|בְּאָחִ֛יו\rb* \rb as before|כְּמִפְּנֵי־\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֖רֶב\rb*, \rb though no one|אָ֑יִן\rb* \rb is behind them|וְרֹדֵ֣ף\rb*. \rb So|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb you will not|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb be|תִֽהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb able to stand|תְּקוּמָ֔ה\rb* \rb against|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb your enemies|אֹֽיְבֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 38 \rb You will perish|וַאֲבַדְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*, \rb and the land|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of your enemies|אֹיְבֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb will consume|וְאָכְלָ֣ה\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb*. \v 39 \rb Those of you who survive|וְהַנִּשְׁאָרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |בָּכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb in the lands|בְּאַרְצֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of your enemies|אֹיְבֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb will waste away|יִמַּ֙קּוּ֙\rb* \rb in their iniquity|בַּֽעֲוֺנָ֔ם\rb* \rb and|וְאַ֛ף\rb* \rb will decay|יִמָּֽקּוּ׃\rb* \rb in the sins|בַּעֲוֺנֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֥ם\rb*.
\s1 God Remembers Those Who Repent
\p \v 40 \rb But if they will confess|וְהִתְוַדּ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their iniquity|עֲוֺנָם֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and that|עֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb in the unfaithfulness|בְּמַעֲלָ֖ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they practiced|מָֽעֲלוּ־\rb* \rb against Me|בִ֑י\rb*, \rb by which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |וְאַ֕ף\rb* \rb they have also walked|הָֽלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb in hostility|בְּקֶֽרִי׃\rb* \rb toward Me|עִמִּ֖י\rb*— \v 41 \rb and|אַף־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb acted|אֵלֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb with hostility|בְּקֶ֔רִי\rb* \rb toward them|עִמָּם֙\rb* \rb and brought|וְהֵבֵאתִ֣י\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb into the land|בְּאֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of their enemies|אֹיְבֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*— \rb and|אוֹ־\rb*\rb |אָ֣ז\rb* \rb if their uncircumcised|הֶֽעָרֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְאָ֖ז\rb* \rb hearts|לְבָבָם֙\rb* \rb will be humbled|יִכָּנַ֗ע\rb* \rb and they will make amends|יִרְצ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for their iniquity|עֲוֺנָֽם׃\rb*, \v 42 \rb then I will remember|וְזָכַרְתִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֣י\rb* \rb with Jacob|יַעֲק֑וֹב\rb* \rb and|וְאַף֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֶזְכֹּ֖ר\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֨י\rb* \rb with Isaac|יִצְחָ֜ק\rb*\rb |וְאַ֨ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֧י\rb* \rb with Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb*, \rb and I will remember|אֶזְכֹּֽר׃\rb* \rb the land|וְהָאָ֥רֶץ\rb*.
\p \v 43 \rb For the land|וְהָאָרֶץ֩\rb* \rb will be abandoned|תֵּעָזֵ֨ב\rb* \rb by them|מֵהֶ֜ם\rb*, \rb and it will enjoy|וְתִ֣רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתֹתֶ֗יהָ\rb* \rb by lying desolate|בָּהְשַׁמָּה֙\rb* \rb without them|מֵהֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb And they|וְהֵ֖ם\rb* \rb will pay the penalty|יִרְצ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for their iniquity|עֲוֺנָ֑ם\rb*, \rb because|יַ֣עַן\rb*\rb |וּבְיַ֔עַן\rb* \rb they rejected|מָאָ֔סוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb My ordinances|בְּמִשְׁפָּטַ֣י\rb* \rb and abhorred|גָּעֲלָ֥ה\rb*\rb |נַפְשָֽׁם׃\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקֹּתַ֖י\rb*.
\p \v 44 \rb Yet|וְאַף־\rb* \rb in spite of|גַּם־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֠את\rb*, \rb when they are|בִּֽהְיוֹתָ֞ם\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of their enemies|אֹֽיְבֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb I will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb reject|מְאַסְתִּ֤ים\rb* \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb despise them|גְעַלְתִּים֙\rb* \rb so as to destroy them|לְכַלֹּתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and break|לְהָפֵ֥ר\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֖י\rb* \rb with them|אִתָּ֑ם\rb*; \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 45 \rb But for their sake|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb I will remember|וְזָכַרְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb with their fathers|רִאשֹׁנִ֑ים\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I brought out|הוֹצֵֽאתִי־\rb*\rb |אֹתָם֩\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֨רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֜יִם\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֗ם\rb*, \rb that I might be|לִהְיֹ֥ת\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb God|לֵאלֹהִ֖ים\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 46 \rb These|אֵ֠לֶּה\rb* \rb are the statutes|הַֽחֻקִּ֣ים\rb*, \rb ordinances|וְהַמִּשְׁפָּטִים֮\rb*, \rb and laws|וְהַתּוֹרֹת֒\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb established|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb between Himself|בֵּינ֕וֹ\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֖ין\rb* \rb and the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃פ\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb Sinai|סִינַ֖י\rb*.
\c 27
\s1 Rules about Valuations
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Speak|דַּבֵּ֞ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb*, ‘\rb When|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb someone|אִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb makes a special|יַפְלִ֖א\rb* \rb vow|נֶ֑דֶר\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb involving the value|בְּעֶרְכְּךָ֥\rb* \rb of persons|נְפָשֹׁ֖ת\rb*, \v 3 \rb if the valuation|עֶרְכְּךָ֙\rb* \rb concerns|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb a male|הַזָּכָ֔ר\rb*\rb |מִבֶּן֙\rb* \rb from twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb to|וְעַ֖ד\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb sixty|שִׁשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb years of age|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb then your valuation|עֶרְכְּךָ֗\rb* \rb shall be|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֛ים\rb* \rb shekels|שֶׁ֥קֶל\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֖סֶף\rb*,\f + \fr 27:3 \fqa 50 shekels \ft is approximately 1.26 pounds or 569.8 grams of silver; also in verse 16.\f* \rb according to the sanctuary|הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb shekel|בְּשֶׁ֥קֶל\rb*.\f + \fr 27:3 \fqa A shekel \ft weighed approximately 0.4 ounces or 11.4 grams; also in verse 25.\f* \v 4 \rb Or if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb it|הִ֑וא\rb* \rb is a female|נְקֵבָ֖ה\rb*, \rb then your valuation|עֶרְכְּךָ֖\rb* \rb shall be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb shekels|שָֽׁקֶל׃\rb*.\f + \fr 27:4 \fqa 30 shekels \ft is approximately 12 ounces or 342 grams of silver.\f* \v 5 \rb And if the person is|וְאִ֨ם\rb* \rb from five|חָמֵ֜שׁ\rb* \rb to|וְעַד֙\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb years of age|מִבֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֗ים\rb*, \rb then your valuation|עֶרְכְּךָ֛\rb* \rb for the male|הַזָּכָ֖ר\rb* \rb shall be|וְהָיָ֧ה\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֑ים\rb*,\f + \fr 27:5 \fqa 20 shekels \ft is approximately 8 ounces or 228 grams of silver.\f* \rb and for the female|וְלַנְּקֵבָ֖ה\rb* \rb ten|עֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 27:5 \fqa 10 shekels \ft is approximately 4 ounces or 114 grams of silver; also in verse 7.\f*
\p \v 6 \rb Now if the person is|וְאִ֣ם\rb*\rb |מִבֶּן־\rb* \rb from one month|חֹ֗דֶשׁ\rb* \rb to|וְעַד֙\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb five|חָמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years of age|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb then your valuation|עֶרְכְּךָ֙\rb* \rb for the male|הַזָּכָ֔ר\rb* \rb shall be|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb of silver|כָּ֑סֶף\rb*,\f + \fr 27:6 \fqa 5 shekels \ft is approximately 2 ounces or 57 grams of silver.\f* \rb and for the female|וְלַנְּקֵבָ֣ה\rb*\rb |עֶרְכְּךָ֔\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb of silver|כָּֽסֶף׃\rb*.\f + \fr 27:6 \fqa 3 shekels \ft is approximately 1.2 ounces or 34.2 grams of silver.\f* \v 7 \rb And if the person is|וְ֠אִם\rb*\rb |מִבֶּן־\rb* \rb sixty|שִׁשִּׁ֨ים\rb* \rb years of age|שָׁנָ֤ה\rb* \rb or older|וָמַ֙עְלָה֙\rb*,\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb then your valuation|עֶרְכְּךָ֔\rb* \rb shall be|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb fifteen|חֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb shekels|שָׁ֑קֶל\rb*\f + \fr 27:7 \fqa 15 shekels \ft is approximately 6 ounces or 171 grams of silver.\f* \rb for the male|זָכָ֔ר\rb* \rb and ten|עֲשָׂרָ֥ה\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִֽים׃\rb* \rb for the female|וְלַנְּקֵבָ֖ה\rb*. \v 8 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the one making the vow|הוּא֙\rb* \rb is too poor to pay|מָ֥ךְ\rb* \rb the valuation|מֵֽעֶרְכֶּ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb he is to present the person|וְהֶֽעֱמִידוֹ֙\rb*\f + \fr 27:8 \ft Or \fqa present himself\f* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb who|הַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb shall set the value|וְהֶעֱרִ֥יךְ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |הַכֹּהֵֽן׃ס\rb*\rb |יַעֲרִיכֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb according to|עַל־\rb*\rb |פִּ֗י\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the one making the vow|הַנֹּדֵ֔ר\rb* \rb can afford|תַּשִּׂיג֙\rb*\rb |יַ֣ד\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb If he vows|וְאִם־\rb* \rb an|מִמֶּ֛נָּה\rb* \rb animal|בְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb may be brought|יַקְרִ֧יבוּ\rb* \rb as an offering|קָרְבָּ֖ן\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb any|כֹּל֩\rb* \rb such animal|מִמֶּ֛נּוּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb given|יִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb shall be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb holy|קֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb He must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb replace it|יַחֲלִיפֶ֗נּוּ\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb or exchange it|יָמִ֥יר\rb*,\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb either good|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb for bad|בְּרָ֖ע\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb bad|רַ֣ע\rb* \rb for good|בְּט֑וֹב\rb*. \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb he does substitute|הָמֵ֨ר\rb*\rb |יָמִ֤יר\rb* \rb one animal|בְּהֵמָה֙\rb* \rb for another|בִּבְהֵמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb both that animal|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb and its substitute|וּתְמוּרָת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb will be|וְהָֽיָה־\rb* \rb holy|קֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb But if|וְאִם֙\rb* \rb the vow involves any|כָּל־\rb* \rb of the unclean|טְמֵאָ֔ה\rb* \rb animals|בְּהֵמָ֣ה\rb* \rb that|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb may not|לֹא־\rb* \rb be brought|יַקְרִ֧יבוּ\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֛נָּה\rb* \rb as an offering|קָרְבָּ֖ן\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb the animal|הַבְּהֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb must be presented|וְהֶֽעֱמִ֥יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb shall set its value|וְהֶעֱרִ֤יךְ\rb*, \rb whether high|ט֖וֹב\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb or low|רָ֑ע\rb*; \rb as the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb values it|כְּעֶרְכְּךָ֥\rb*, \rb the price|כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb will be set|יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb If, however, the owner|וְאִם־\rb* \rb decides to redeem the animal|גָּאֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |יִגְאָלֶ֑נָּה\rb*, \rb he must add|וְיָסַ֥ף\rb* \rb a fifth|חֲמִישִׁת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb its value|עֶרְכֶּֽךָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Now if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|וְאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb consecrates|יַקְדִּ֨שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּית֥וֹ\rb* \rb as holy|קֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb shall value it|וְהֶעֱרִיכוֹ֙\rb* \rb either as|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb good|ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb or|וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb bad|רָ֑ע\rb*. \rb The price will stand|יָקֽוּם׃\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb values|יַעֲרִ֥יךְ\rb* \rb it|אֹת֛וֹ\rb*. \v 15 \rb But if|וְאִ֨ם־\rb* \rb he who consecrated|הַמַּקְדִּ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb his house|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb* \rb redeems|יִגְאַ֖ל\rb* \rb it|אֶת־\rb*, \rb he must add|וְ֠יָסַף\rb* \rb a fifth|חֲמִישִׁ֧ית\rb* \rb to|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb the assessed|עֶרְכְּךָ֛\rb* \rb value|כֶּֽסֶף־\rb*, \rb and it will belong|וְהָ֥יָה\rb* \rb to him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb If|וְאִ֣ם׀\rb* \rb a man|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb consecrates|יַקְדִּ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb a parcel|מִשְּׂדֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of his land|אֲחֻזָּת֗וֹ\rb*, \rb then your valuation|עֶרְכְּךָ֖\rb* \rb shall be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb proportional|לְפִ֣י\rb* \rb to the seed required for it|זַרְע֑וֹ\rb* — \rb fifty|בַּחֲמִשִּׁ֖ים\rb* \rb shekels|שֶׁ֥קֶל\rb* \rb of silver|כָּֽסֶף׃\rb* \rb for every homer|חֹ֣מֶר\rb* \rb of barley|שְׂעֹרִ֔ים\rb* \rb seed|זֶ֚רַע\rb*.\f + \fr 27:16 \fqa A homer \ft is a dry measure of approximately 6.24 bushels or 220 liters (probably about 291 pounds or 132 kilograms of barley seed).\f* \v 17 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb he consecrates|יַקְדִּ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb his field|שָׂדֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb during the Year|מִשְּׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Jubilee|הַיֹּבֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb the price will stand|יָקֽוּם׃\rb* \rb according to your valuation|כְּעֶרְכְּךָ֖\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb he consecrates|יַקְדִּ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb his field|שָׂדֵהוּ֒\rb* \rb after|אַחַ֣ר\rb* \rb the Jubilee|הַיֹּבֵל֮\rb*, \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to calculate|וְחִשַּׁב־\rb* \rb the price|הַכֶּ֗סֶף\rb* \rb in proportion to|עַל־\rb*\rb |פִּ֤י\rb* \rb the years|הַשָּׁנִים֙\rb* \rb left|הַנּ֣וֹתָרֹ֔ת\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the next Year|שְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Jubilee|הַיֹּבֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb so that your valuation|מֵֽעֶרְכֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb will be reduced|וְנִגְרַ֖ע\rb*. \v 19 \rb And if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the one who consecrated|הַמַּקְדִּ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb decides to redeem it|גָּאֹ֤ל\rb*\rb |יִגְאַל֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he must add|וְ֠יָסַף\rb* \rb a fifth|חֲמִשִׁ֧ית\rb* \rb to|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb the assessed|עֶרְכְּךָ֛\rb* \rb value|כֶּֽסֶף־\rb*, \rb and it shall belong|וְקָ֥ם\rb* \rb to him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb If, however|וְאִם־\rb*, \rb he does not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb redeem|יִגְאַל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb*, \rb or if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb he has sold|מָכַ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to another|אַחֵ֑ר\rb* \rb man|לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb*, \rb it may no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb longer|עֽוֹד׃\rb* \rb be redeemed|יִגָּאֵ֖ל\rb*. \v 21 \rb When the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֜ה\rb* \rb is released|בְּצֵאת֣וֹ\rb* \rb in the Jubilee|בַיֹּבֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb it will become|וְהָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb holy|קֹ֛דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb like a field|כִּשְׂדֵ֣ה\rb* \rb devoted|הַחֵ֑רֶם\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*; \rb it becomes|תִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the property|אֲחֻזָּתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb of the priests|לַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Now if|וְאִם֙\rb* \rb a man consecrates|יַקְדִּ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb a field|שְׂדֵ֣ה\rb* \rb he has purchased|מִקְנָת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֕ר\rb* \rb is not|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb a part|מִשְּׂדֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of his own property|אֲחֻזָּת֑וֹ\rb*, \v 23 \rb then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb shall calculate|וְחִשַּׁב־\rb* \rb for him the value|מִכְסַ֣ת\rb*\rb |הָֽעֶרְכְּךָ֔\rb* \rb up to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the Year|שְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Jubilee|הַיֹּבֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and the man shall pay|וְנָתַ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the assessed value|הָעֶרְכְּךָ֙\rb* \rb on that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb as a sacred offering|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb In the Year|בִּשְׁנַ֤ת\rb* \rb of Jubilee|הַיּוֹבֵל֙\rb* \rb the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb shall return|יָשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb to the one from whom|לַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb it was bought|קָנָ֖הוּ\rb* —\rb |מֵאִתּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |לַאֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb the original owner|אֲחֻזַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb Every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb valuation|עֶרְכְּךָ֔\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb according to the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb shekel|בְּשֶׁ֣קֶל\rb*, \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb gerahs|גֵּרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb to the shekel|הַשָּֽׁקֶל׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 27:25 \fqa 20 gerahs \ft is equivalent to one shekel (approximately 0.4 ounces or 11.4 grams).\f*
\p \v 26 \rb But|אַךְ־\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb one|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb may consecrate|יַקְדִּ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb a firstborn|בְּכ֞וֹר\rb* \rb of the livestock|בִּבְהֵמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb because|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb a firstborn|יְבֻכַּ֤ר\rb* \rb belongs to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*. \rb Whether it is|אִם־\rb* \rb an ox|שׁ֣וֹר\rb* \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb a sheep|שֶׂ֔ה\rb*, \rb it is|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb the LORD’s|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*. \v 27 \rb But if|וְאִ֨ם\rb* \rb it is among the unclean|הַטְּמֵאָה֙\rb* \rb animals|בַּבְּהֵמָ֤ה\rb*, \rb then he may redeem|וּפָדָ֣ה\rb* \rb it according to your valuation|בְעֶרְכֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and add|וְיָסַ֥ף\rb* \rb a fifth|חֲמִשִׁת֖וֹ\rb* \rb of its value|עָלָ֑יו\rb*. \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb it is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb redeemed|יִגָּאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb then it shall be sold|וְנִמְכַּ֥ר\rb* \rb according to your valuation|בְּעֶרְכֶּֽךָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb |אַךְ־\rb* \rb Nothing|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb a man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb sets apart|חֵ֡רֶם\rb*\rb |יַחֲרִם֩\rb*\f + \fr 27:28 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD; similarly in verse 29.\f* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb from all he owns|מִכָּל־\rb* —\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb whether a man|מֵאָדָ֤ם\rb*, \rb an animal|וּבְהֵמָה֙\rb*, \rb or his inherited land|וּמִשְּׂדֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲחֻזָּת֔וֹ\rb* —\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb can be sold|יִמָּכֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb or redeemed|יִגָּאֵ֑ל\rb*; \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb so devoted|חֵ֕רֶם\rb* \rb is most|קֹֽדֶשׁ־\rb* \rb holy|קָֽדָשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb No|כָּל־\rb*\rb |חֵ֗רֶם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb person|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb set apart for destruction|יָחֳרַ֛ם\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb may be ransomed|יִפָּדֶ֑ה\rb*; \rb he must surely be put to death|מ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָֽת׃\rb*.
\s1 Instruction on Tithes
\p \v 30 \rb Thus any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb tithe|מַעְשַׂ֨ר\rb* \rb from the land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb*, \rb whether from the seed|מִזֶּ֤רַע\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb or the fruit|מִפְּרִ֣י\rb* \rb of the trees|הָעֵ֔ץ\rb*, \rb belongs to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*; \rb it|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb is holy|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb wishes|גָּאֹ֥ל\rb* \rb to redeem|יִגְאַ֛ל\rb* \rb part of his tithe|מִמַּֽעַשְׂר֑וֹ\rb*, \rb he must add|יֹסֵ֥ף\rb* \rb a fifth|חֲמִשִׁית֖וֹ\rb* \rb to its value|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb Every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb tenth|מַעְשַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb animal from the herd|בָּקָר֙\rb* \rb or flock|וָצֹ֔אן\rb*\rb |כֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb passes|יַעֲבֹ֖ר\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the shepherd’s rod|הַשָּׁ֑בֶט\rb*\rb |הָֽעֲשִׂירִ֕י\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb holy|קֹּ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 33 \rb He must not|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb inspect|יְבַקֵּ֛ר\rb* \rb whether it is good|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb or|בֵּֽין־\rb* \rb bad|לָרַ֖ע\rb*, \rb and he shall not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb make any substitution|יְמִירֶ֑נּוּ\rb*. \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb he does make a substitution|הָמֵ֣ר\rb*\rb |יְמִירֶ֔נּוּ\rb*, \rb both the animal|ה֧וּא\rb* \rb and its substitute|וּתְמוּרָת֛וֹ\rb*\rb |יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb shall become|וְהָֽיָה־\rb* \rb holy|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb*; \rb they cannot|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be redeemed|יִגָּאֵֽל׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 34 \rb These|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are the commandments|הַמִּצְוֺ֗ת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave|צִוָּ֧ה\rb* \rb to Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַ֖ר\rb* \rb Sinai|סִינָֽי׃\rb*.
